\s1 Daniel Removed to Babylon
\p \v 1 \rb In the third|שָׁל֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the reign|לְמַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֧ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and besieged|וַיָּ֥צַר\rb* \rb it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֨י\rb* \rb delivered|וַיִּתֵּן֩\rb* \rb into his hand|בְּיָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb along with some|וּמִקְצָת֙\rb* \rb of the articles|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb from the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*. \rb He carried these off|וַיְבִיאֵ֥ם\rb* \rb to the land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Shinar|שִׁנְעָ֖ר\rb*,\f + \fr 1:2 \ft That is, Babylonia\f* \rb to the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of his god|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb*, \rb where|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he put|הֵבִ֔יא\rb* \rb them|הַכֵּלִ֣ים\rb*\rb |בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb in the treasury|אוֹצַ֥ר\rb* \rb of his god|אֱלֹהָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Ashpenaz|לְאַשְׁפְּנַ֖ז\rb*, \rb the chief|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb of his court officials|סָרִיסָ֑יו\rb*, \rb to bring in|לְהָבִ֞יא\rb* \rb some|וּמִן־\rb* \rb Israelites|מִבְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb from the royal|הַמְּלוּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb family|וּמִזֶּ֥רַע\rb*\f + \fr 1:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa from the seed of the kingdom\f* \rb and the nobility|הַֽפַּרְתְּמִֽים׃\rb*— \v 4 \rb young men|יְלָדִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb without|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb blemish|מְאוּם\rb*, \rb handsome|וְטוֹבֵ֨י\rb*\rb |מַרְאֶ֜ה\rb*, \rb gifted|וּמַשְׂכִּילִ֣ים\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֗ה\rb*, \rb knowledgeable|וְיֹ֤דְעֵי\rb*\rb |דַ֙עַת֙\rb*, \rb quick|מַדָּ֔ע\rb* \rb to understand|וּמְבִינֵ֣י\rb*,\rb |וַאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb and qualified|כֹּ֣חַ\rb* \rb to serve|לַעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb in the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בְּהֵיכַ֣ל\rb*— \rb and to teach them|וּֽלֲלַמְּדָ֥ם\rb* \rb the language|וּלְשׁ֥וֹן\rb* \rb and literature|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 1:4 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f*
\p \v 5 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb assigned|וַיְמַן֩\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֨ם\rb*\rb |י֣וֹם\rb* \rb daily|בְּיוֹמ֗וֹ\rb* \rb provisions|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb food|בַּ֤ג\rb* \rb and wine|וּמִיֵּ֣ין\rb*\rb |מִשְׁתָּ֔יו\rb*. \rb They were to be trained|וּֽלְגַדְּלָ֖ם\rb* \rb for three|שָׁל֑וֹשׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb after which|וּמִ֨קְצָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb they were to enter|יַֽעַמְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king’s service|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Among these young men|בָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb were some|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb from|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*: \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֣אל\rb*, \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Mishael|מִֽישָׁאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָֽה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb The chief|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb official|הַסָּרִיסִ֖ים\rb* \rb gave them|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb new names|שֵׁמ֑וֹת\rb*: \rb To Daniel|לְדָֽנִיֵּ֜אל\rb* \rb he gave|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb the name Belteshazzar|בֵּ֣לְטְשַׁאצַּ֗ר\rb*; \rb to Hananiah|וְלַֽחֲנַנְיָה֙\rb*, \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֔ךְ\rb*; \rb to Mishael|וּלְמִֽישָׁאֵ֣ל\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֔ךְ\rb*; \rb and to Azariah|וְלַעֲזַרְיָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |עֲבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb Abednego|נְגֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Daniel’s Faithfulness
\p \v 8 \rb But Daniel|דָּנִיֵּאל֙\rb* \rb made|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb up|עַל־\rb* \rb his mind|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb he would not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb defile himself|יִתְגָּאַ֛ל\rb* \rb with the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb food|בְּפַתְבַּ֥ג\rb* \rb or wine|וּבְיֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |מִשְׁתָּ֑יו\rb*. \rb So he asked|וַיְבַקֵּשׁ֙\rb* \rb the chief|מִשַּׂ֣ר\rb* \rb official|הַסָּרִיסִ֔ים\rb* \rb for permission|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to defile himself|יִתְגָּאָֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Now God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had granted|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּ֣נִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb favor|לְחֶ֖סֶד\rb* \rb and compassion|וּֽלְרַחֲמִ֑ים\rb* \rb from|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the chief|שַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb official|הַסָּרִיסִֽים׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb but he|שַׂ֤ר\rb*\rb |הַסָּרִיסִים֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb to Daniel|לְדָ֣נִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb fear|יָרֵ֤א\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has assigned|מִנָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your food|מַאֲכַלְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and drink|מִשְׁתֵּיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb For|אֲשֶׁ֡ר\rb* \rb why|לָמָּה֩\rb* \rb should he see|יִרְאֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your faces|פְּנֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb looking thinner|זֹֽעֲפִ֗ים\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb those of the other young men|הַיְלָדִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb your age|כְּגִֽילְכֶ֔ם\rb*? \rb You would endanger|וְחִיַּבְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my head|רֹאשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb before the king|לַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 11 \rb Then Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֖אל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the steward|הַמֶּלְצַ֑ר\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the chief|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb official|הַסָּֽרִיסִ֔ים\rb* \rb had appointed|מִנָּה֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֣אל\rb*, \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Mishael|מִֽישָׁאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָֽה׃\rb*, \v 12 “\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb test|נַס־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb for ten|עֲשָׂרָ֑ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים\rb*. \rb Let us be given|וְיִתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb only|מִן־\rb* \rb vegetables|הַזֵּרֹעִ֛ים\rb* \rb to eat|וְנֹאכְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and water|וּמַ֥יִם\rb* \rb to drink|וְנִשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then compare|וְיֵרָא֤וּ\rb*\rb |לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb our appearances|מַרְאֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb with those|וּמַרְאֵה֙\rb* \rb of the young men|הַיְלָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb who are eating|הָאֹ֣כְלִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb food|פַּתְבַּ֣ג\rb*, \rb and deal|עֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb according to what|וְכַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you see|תִּרְאֵ֔ה\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb So he consented|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb*\rb |לַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb and tested them|וַיְנַסֵּ֖ם\rb* \rb for ten|עֲשָׂרָֽה׃\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֥ים\rb*. \v 15 \rb And at|מִן־\rb* \rb the end|וּמִקְצָת֙\rb* \rb of ten|עֲשָׂרָ֔ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֣ים\rb*, \rb they looked|נִרְאָ֤ה\rb*\rb |מַרְאֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb healthier|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb and better nourished|וּבְרִיאֵ֖י\rb*\rb |בָּשָׂ֑ר\rb* \rb than all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the young men|הַיְלָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb who were eating|הָאֹ֣כְלִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb food|פַּתְבַּ֥ג\rb*. \v 16 \rb So|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb the steward|הַמֶּלְצַ֗ר\rb* \rb continued to withhold|נֹשֵׂא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their choice food|פַּתְבָּגָ֔ם\rb* \rb and the wine|וְיֵ֖ין\rb* \rb they were to drink|מִשְׁתֵּיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and he gave|וְנֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb vegetables instead|זֵרְעֹנִֽים׃\rb*.
\s1 Daniel’s Wisdom
\p \v 17 \rb To these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּעְתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb young men|וְהַיְלָדִ֤ים\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb knowledge|מַדָּ֥ע\rb* \rb and understanding|וְהַשְׂכֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb in every kind|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of literature|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb and wisdom|וְחָכְמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And Daniel|וְדָנִיֵּ֣אל\rb* \rb had insight|הֵבִ֔ין\rb* \rb into all kinds|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of visions|חָז֖וֹן\rb* \rb and dreams|וַחֲלֹמֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Now at the end|וּלְמִקְצָת֙\rb* \rb of the time|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb specified|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb by the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לַהֲבִיאָ֑ם\rb*, \rb the chief|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb official|הַסָּרִיסִ֔ים\rb* \rb presented them|וַיְבִיאֵם֙\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻכַדְנֶצַּֽר׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb* \rb spoke with them|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*, \rb and among|אִתָּם֮\rb* \rb all the young men|מִכֻּלָּ֔ם\rb* \rb he found|נִמְצָא֙\rb* \rb no one|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb equal to Daniel|כְּדָנִיֵּ֣אל\rb*, \rb Hananiah|חֲנַנְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Mishael|מִֽישָׁאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So they entered|וַיַּֽעַמְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king’s service|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb In every|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb matter|דְּבַר֙\rb* \rb of wisdom|חָכְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb and understanding|בִּינָ֔ה\rb* \rb about which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb consulted|בִּקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb them|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb he found them|וַֽיִּמְצָאֵ֞ם\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb times|יָד֗וֹת\rb* \rb better than|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the magicians|הָֽאַשָּׁפִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb and enchanters|הַֽחַרְטֻמִּים֙\rb* \rb in his entire|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכוּתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And Daniel|דָּֽנִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb remained|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb there until|עַד־\rb* \rb the first|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb* \rb Cyrus|לְכ֥וֹרֶשׁ\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar’s Troubling Dream
\p \v 1 \rb In the second|שְׁתַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of his|נְבֻֽכַדְנֶצַּ֔ר\rb* \rb reign|לְמַלְכוּת֙\rb*, \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻֽכַדְנֶצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb had dreams|חָלַ֥ם\rb*\rb |חֲלֹמ֑וֹת\rb* \rb that troubled|וַתִּתְפָּ֣עֶם\rb* \rb his spirit|רוּח֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and sleep|וּשְׁנָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb escaped|נִהְיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So the king|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb* \rb gave orders|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to summon|לִקְרֹ֨א\rb* \rb the magicians|וְלָֽאַשָּׁפִ֗ים\rb*, \rb enchanters|לַֽחַרְטֻמִּ֜ים\rb*, \rb sorcerers|וְלַֽמְכַשְּׁפִים֙\rb*, \rb and astrologers|וְלַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb*\f + \fr 2:2 \ft Or \fqa Chaldeans\ft ; also in verses 4, 5, and 10\f* \rb to explain|לְהַגִּ֥יד\rb*\rb |לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb his dreams|חֲלֹמֹתָ֑יו\rb*. \rb When they came|וַיָּבֹ֕אוּ\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּֽעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb he|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb said to them|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*,\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* “\rb I have had a dream|חֲל֣וֹם\rb*\rb |חָלָ֑מְתִּי\rb*, \rb and my spirit|רוּחִ֔י\rb* \rb is anxious|וַתִּפָּ֣עֶם\rb* \rb to understand|לָדַ֖עַת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb it|הַחֲלֽוֹם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then the astrologers|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֛ים\rb* \rb answered|וַֽיְדַבְּר֧וּ\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Aramaic|אֲרָמִ֑ית\rb*,\f + \fr 2:4 \ft The original text from this point of \ref Daniel 2:4|DAN 2:4\ref* through Daniel 7:28 is in Aramaic.\f* “\rb O king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*, \rb may you live|חֱיִ֔י\rb* \rb forever|לְעָלְמִ֣ין\rb*! \rb Tell|אֱמַ֥ר\rb* \rb your servants|לְעַבְדַּיִךְ\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָ֛א\rb*, \rb and we will give|נְחַוֵּֽא׃\rb* \rb the interpretation|וּפִשְׁרָ֥א\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb The king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb replied|עָנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb to the astrologers|לְכַשְׂדָּיֵא\rb*, “\rb My word|מִלְּתָ֖א\rb*\rb |מִנִּ֣י\rb* \rb is final|אַזְדָּ֑א\rb*: \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you do not|לָ֤א\rb* \rb tell me|תְהֽוֹדְעוּנַּ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָ֣א\rb* \rb and its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵ֔הּ\rb*, \rb you will be cut|תִּתְעַבְד֔וּן\rb* \rb into pieces|הַדָּמִין֙\rb* \rb and your houses|וּבָתֵּיכ֖וֹן\rb* \rb will be reduced|יִתְּשָׂמֽוּן׃\rb* \rb to rubble|נְוָלִ֥י\rb*. \v 6 \rb But if|וְהֵ֨ן\rb* \rb you tell me|תְּֽהַחֲוֺ֔ן\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָ֤א\rb* \rb and its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵהּ֙\rb*, \rb you will receive|תְּקַבְּל֖וּן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb me|קֳדָמָ֑י\rb* \rb gifts|מַתְּנָ֤ן\rb* \rb and rewards|וּנְבִזְבָּה֙\rb* \rb and great|שַׂגִּ֔יא\rb* \rb honor|וִיקָ֣ר\rb*. \rb So|לָהֵ֕ן\rb* \rb tell me|הַחֲוֺֽנִי׃\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָ֥א\rb* \rb and its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵ֖הּ\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb They answered|עֲנ֥וֹ\rb* \rb a second time|תִנְיָנ֖וּת\rb*, “\rb Let the king|מַלְכָּ֕א\rb* \rb tell|וְאָמְרִ֑ין\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָ֛א\rb*\rb |יֵאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to his servants|לְעַבְד֖וֹהִי\rb*, \rb and we will give|נְהַחֲוֵֽה׃\rb* \rb the interpretation|וּפִשְׁרָ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb The king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb replied|עָנֵ֤ה\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנָ֔ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb for|מִן־\rb* \rb sure|יַצִּיב֙\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אַנְתּ֣וּן\rb* \rb are stalling|זָבְנִ֑ין\rb* \rb for time|עִדָּנָ֖א\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb because|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you see|חֲזֵית֔וֹן\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb my|מִנִּ֥י\rb* \rb word|מִלְּתָֽא׃\rb* \rb is final|אַזְדָּ֖א\rb*. \v 9 \rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb If|הֵן־\rb* \rb you do not|לָ֨א\rb* \rb tell me|תְהֽוֹדְעֻנַּ֜נִי\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָא֩\rb*, \rb there is|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb only one|חֲדָה־\rb* \rb decree for you|דָֽתְכ֗וֹן\rb*. \rb You have conspired|הַזְמִנְתּוּן\rb* \rb to speak|לְמֵאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb before me|קָֽדָמַ֔י\rb* \rb false|כִדְבָ֤ה\rb* \rb and fraudulent|וּשְׁחִיתָה֙\rb* \rb words|וּמִלָּ֨ה\rb*, \rb hoping|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb the situation|עִדָּנָ֖א\rb* \rb will change|יִשְׁתַּנֵּ֑א\rb*. \rb Therefore|לָהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb tell|אֱמַ֣רוּ\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָא֙\rb*, \rb and I will know|וְֽאִנְדַּ֕ע\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb you can give me|תְּהַחֲוֻנַּֽנִי׃\rb* \rb its interpretation|פִשְׁרֵ֖הּ\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb The astrologers|כַשְׂדָּיֵא\rb*\rb |קֳדָם־\rb* \rb answered|עֲנ֨וֹ\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*,\rb |וְאָ֣מְרִ֔ין\rb* “\rb No|לָֽא־\rb*\rb |אִיתַ֤י\rb*\rb |אֲנָשׁ֙\rb* \rb one|עַל־\rb* \rb on earth|יַבֶּשְׁתָּ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֚י\rb* \rb can|יוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb do|לְהַחֲוָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb what the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb requests|מִלַּ֣ת\rb*!\rb |קֳבֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |דִּ֚י\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb No|לָ֣א\rb* \rb king|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb however great|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb and powerful|וְשַׁלִּ֔יט\rb*, \rb has ever asked|שְׁאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb anything|מִלָּ֤ה\rb* \rb like this|כִדְנָה֙\rb* \rb of any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb magician|חַרְטֹּ֖ם\rb*, \rb enchanter|וְאָשַׁ֥ף\rb*, \rb or astrologer|וְכַשְׂדָּֽי׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb |וּמִלְּתָ֨א\rb* \rb What|דִֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֤ה\rb* \rb requests|שָׁאֵל֙\rb* \rb is so difficult|יַקִּירָ֔ה\rb* \rb that no|לָ֣א\rb* \rb one|וְאָחֳרָן֙\rb* \rb can tell it|יְחַוִּנַּ֖הּ\rb* \rb to|קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb him|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb except|לָהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלָהִ֔ין\rb*, \rb whose|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb dwelling|מְדָ֣רְה֔וֹן\rb* \rb is|אִיתֽוֹהִי׃\rb* \rb not|לָ֥א\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb mortals|בִּשְׂרָ֖א\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb This response made|קֳבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֕א\rb* \rb so|שַׂגִּ֑יא\rb* \rb angry|בְּנַ֖ס\rb* \rb and furious|וּקְצַ֣ף\rb* \rb that he gave orders|וַאֲמַר֙\rb* \rb to destroy|לְה֣וֹבָדָ֔ה\rb* \rb all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the wise men|חַכִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb So the decree|וְדָתָ֣א\rb* \rb went out|נֶפְקַ֔ת\rb* \rb that the wise men|וְחַכִּֽימַיָּ֖א\rb* \rb were to be executed|מִֽתְקַטְּלִ֑ין\rb*, \rb and men went to look for|וּבְע֛וֹ\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֥אל\rb* \rb and his friends|וְחַבְר֖וֹהִי\rb* \rb to execute them|לְהִתְקְטָלָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Dream Revealed to Daniel
\p \v 14 \rb When|בֵּאדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb Arioch|לְאַרְי֕וֹךְ\rb*, \rb the commander|רַב־\rb* \rb of the king’s|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*\rb |דִּ֚י\rb* \rb guard|טַבָּחַיָּ֖א\rb*,\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb went out|נְפַ֣ק\rb* \rb to execute|לְקַטָּלָ֔ה\rb* \rb the wise men|לְחַכִּימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֗אל\rb* \rb responded|הֲתִיב֙\rb* \rb with discretion|עֵטָ֣א\rb* \rb and tact|וּטְעֵ֔ם\rb*. \v 15 “\rb Why|עַל־\rb*\rb |מָ֥ה\rb* \rb is the decree|דָתָ֛א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb*\rb |קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb so harsh|מְהַחְצְפָ֖ה\rb*?” \rb he asked|עָנֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֗ר\rb*\rb |לְאַרְיוֹךְ֙\rb*\rb |מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*\rb |שַׁלִּיטָ֣א\rb*\rb |דִֽי־\rb*.
\p \rb Then|אֱדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb Arioch|אַרְי֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb explained|הוֹדַ֥ע\rb* \rb the situation|מִלְּתָ֔א\rb* \rb to Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּֽאל׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb So Daniel|וְדָ֣נִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb went in|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb and asked|וּבְעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*\rb |דִּ֚י\rb* \rb to give|יִנְתֵּן־\rb* \rb him|לֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb some time|זְמָ֣ן\rb*, \rb so that he could give|לְהַֽחֲוָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb him|לְמַלְכָּֽא׃פ\rb* \rb the interpretation|וּפִשְׁרָ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Then|אֱדַ֥יִן\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּֽנִיֵּ֖אל\rb* \rb returned|אֲזַ֑ל\rb* \rb to his house|לְבַיְתֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb and explained|הוֹדַֽע׃\rb* \rb the matter|מִלְּתָ֥א\rb* \rb to his friends|חַבְר֖וֹהִי\rb* \rb Hananiah|וְ֠לַחֲנַנְיָה\rb*, \rb Mishael|מִֽישָׁאֵ֧ל\rb*, \rb and Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֛ה\rb*, \v 18 \rb urging them to plead|לְמִבְעֵא֙\rb* \rb for mercy|וְרַחֲמִ֗ין\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb from|קֳדָם֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb this|דְּנָ֑ה\rb* \rb mystery|רָזָ֖ה\rb*, \rb so that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֣אל\rb* \rb and his friends|וְחַבְר֔וֹהִי\rb* \rb would not|לָ֤א\rb* \rb be killed|יְהֹֽבְדוּן֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the rest|שְׁאָ֖ר\rb* \rb of the wise men|חַכִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb During|אֱדַ֗יִן\rb* \rb the night|לֵילְיָ֖א\rb*, \rb the mystery|רָזָ֣ה\rb* \rb was revealed|גֲלִ֑י\rb*\rb |אֱדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb to Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֛אל\rb* \rb in a vision|בְּחֶזְוָ֥א\rb*, \rb and he|דָּֽנִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb blessed|בָּרִ֖ךְ\rb* \rb the God|לֶאֱלָ֥הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּֽא׃\rb* \v 20 \rb |עָנֵ֤ה\rb*\rb |דָֽנִיֵּאל֙\rb* \rb and declared|וְאָמַ֔ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Blessed|מְבָרַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb be|לֶהֱוֵ֨א\rb* \rb the name|שְׁמֵ֤הּ\rb* \rb of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָא֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb forever|עָלְמָ֖א\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֣ד־\rb* \rb ever|עָלְמָ֑א\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|דִּ֧י\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמְתָ֛א\rb* \rb and power|וּגְבוּרְתָ֖א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb belong to Him|לֵֽהּ־\rb*\rb |הִֽיא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb He|וְ֠הוּא\rb* \rb changes|מְהַשְׁנֵ֤א\rb* \rb the times|עִדָּנַיָּא֙\rb* \rb and seasons|וְזִמְנַיָּ֔א\rb*;
\q2 \rb He removes|מְהַעְדֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכִ֖ין\rb* \rb and establishes|וּמְהָקֵ֣ים\rb* \rb them|מַלְכִ֑ין\rb*.
\q1 \rb He gives|יָהֵ֤ב\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמְתָא֙\rb* \rb to the wise|לְחַכִּימִ֔ין\rb*
\q2 \rb and knowledge|וּמַנְדְּעָ֖א\rb* \rb to the discerning|לְיָדְעֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בִינָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb He|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb reveals|גָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb the deep|עַמִּיקָתָ֖א\rb* \rb and hidden things|וּמְסַתְּרָתָ֑א\rb*;
\q2 \rb He knows|יָדַע֙\rb* \rb what|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb lies in darkness|בַחֲשׁוֹכָ֔א\rb*,
\q2 \rb and light|וּנְהִירָא\rb* \rb dwells|שְׁרֵֽא׃\rb* \rb with Him|עִמֵּ֥הּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb To You|לָ֣ךְ׀\rb*, \rb O God|אֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of my fathers|אֲבָהָתִ֗י\rb*,
\q2 \rb I|אֲנָ֔ה\rb* \rb give thanks|מְהוֹדֵ֤א\rb* \rb and praise|וּמְשַׁבַּח֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb because|דִּ֧י\rb* \rb You have given|יְהַ֣בְתְּ\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb wisdom|חָכְמְתָ֛א\rb* \rb and power|וּגְבוּרְתָ֖א\rb*.
\q1 \rb And now|וּכְעַ֤ן\rb* \rb You have made known to me|הֽוֹדַעְתַּ֙נִי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb what|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb we have requested|בְעֵ֣ינָא\rb*\rb |מִנָּ֔ךְ\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb You have made known to us|הוֹדַעְתֶּֽנָא׃\rb*
\q2 \rb the dream|מִלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb*.”
\s1 Daniel Interprets the Dream
\p \v 24 \rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb Therefore|קֳבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֗ה\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּֽנִיֵּאל֙\rb* \rb went|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Arioch|אַרְי֔וֹךְ\rb*, \rb whom|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb had appointed|מַנִּ֣י\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהוֹבָדָ֖ה\rb* \rb the wise men|לְחַכִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶ֑ל\rb*,\rb |אֲזַ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and said|אֲמַר־\rb* \rb to him|לֵ֗הּ\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb execute|תְּהוֹבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb the wise men|לְחַכִּימֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶל֙\rb*! \rb Bring me|הַעֵ֙לְנִי֙\rb* \rb before|קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, \rb and I will give|אֲחַוֵּֽא׃ס\rb* \rb him|לְמַלְכָּ֥א\rb* \rb the interpretation|וּפִשְׁרָ֖א\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb Arioch|אַרְיוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb hastily|בְּהִתְבְּהָלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֱדַ֤יִן\rb* \rb brought|הַנְעֵ֥ל\rb* \rb Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֖אל\rb* \rb before|קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and said|אֲמַר־\rb* \rb to him|לֵ֗הּ\rb*, “\rb I have found|הַשְׁכַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb a man|גְּבַר֙\rb* \rb among|מִן־\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the exiles|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |גָֽלוּתָא֙\rb* \rb from Judah|יְה֔וּד\rb* \rb who|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb will tell|יְהוֹדַֽע׃\rb* \rb the king|לְמַלְכָּ֥א\rb* \rb the interpretation|פִשְׁרָ֖א\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb The king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb responded|עָנֵ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, \rb whose|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb name|שְׁמֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb was Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּ֑ר\rb*,\rb |הַאִיתַיִךְ\rb* “\rb Are you able|כָּהֵ֗ל\rb* \rb to tell me|לְהוֹדָעֻתַ֛נִי\rb* \rb what|דִֽי־\rb* \rb I saw|חֲזֵ֖ית\rb* \rb in the dream|חֶלְמָ֥א\rb*, \rb as well as its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵֽהּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 27 \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֛אל\rb*\rb |קֳדָ֥ם\rb* \rb answered|עָנֵ֧ה\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb No|לָ֧א\rb* \rb wise man|חַכִּימִ֣ין\rb*, \rb enchanter|אָֽשְׁפִ֗ין\rb*, \rb medium|חַרְטֻמִּין֙\rb*, \rb or magician|גָּזְרִ֔ין\rb* \rb can|יָכְלִ֖ין\rb* \rb explain|לְהַֽחֲוָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the king|לְמַלְכָּֽא׃\rb* \rb the mystery|רָזָה֙\rb* \rb of which|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|מַלְכָּ֣א\rb* \rb inquires|שָׁאֵ֔ל\rb*. \v 28 \rb But|בְּרַ֡ם\rb* \rb there is|אִיתַ֞י\rb* \rb a God|אֱלָ֤הּ\rb* \rb in heaven|בִּשְׁמַיָּא֙\rb* \rb who reveals|גָּלֵ֣א\rb* \rb mysteries|רָזִ֔ין\rb*, \rb and He has made known|וְהוֹדַ֗ע\rb* \rb to King|לְמַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶצַּ֔ר\rb* \rb what|מָ֛ה\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb will happen|לֶהֱוֵ֖א\rb* \rb in the latter|בְּאַחֲרִ֣ית\rb* \rb days|יוֹמַיָּ֑א\rb*. \rb Your dream|חֶלְמָ֨ךְ\rb* \rb and the visions|וְחֶזְוֵ֥י\rb* \rb that came into your mind|רֵאשָׁ֛ךְ\rb* \rb as you lay on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb your bed|מִשְׁכְּבָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb were these|דְּנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃פ\rb*:
\p \v 29 \rb As you|אַ֣נְתְּה\rb* \rb lay on|עַל־\rb* \rb your bed|מִשְׁכְּבָ֣ךְ\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb*, \rb your thoughts|רַעְיוֹנָךְ֙\rb* \rb turned|סְלִ֔קוּ\rb* \rb to|מָ֛ה\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb*\rb |לֶהֱוֵ֖א\rb* \rb the future|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |דְנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the Revealer|וְגָלֵ֧א\rb* \rb of Mysteries|רָזַיָּ֛א\rb* \rb made known to you|הוֹדְעָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb what|מָה־\rb*\rb |דִ֥י\rb* \rb will happen|לֶהֱוֵֽא׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb And to me|וַאֲנָ֗ה\rb* \rb this|דְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb mystery|רָזָ֥א\rb* \rb has been revealed|גֱּלִ֣י\rb*, \rb not|לָ֤א\rb* \rb because|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have|אִיתַ֥י\rb* \rb more wisdom|בְחָכְמָה֙\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb any man|כָּל־\rb* \rb alive|חַיַּיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb but|לָהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb in order that|עַל־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרַת֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֤י\rb* \rb the interpretation|פִשְׁרָא֙\rb* \rb might be made known|יְהוֹדְע֔וּן\rb* \rb to the king|לְמַלְכָּ֣א\rb*, \rb and that you may understand|תִּנְדַּֽע׃\rb* \rb the thoughts|וְרַעְיוֹנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your mind|לִבְבָ֖ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb As you|אַ֣נְתְּה\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb*, \rb were watching|חָזֵ֤ה\rb*,\rb |הֲוַ֙יְתָ֙\rb* \rb a|חַד֙\rb* \rb great|שַׂגִּ֔יא\rb* \rb statue|צְלֵ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 2:31 \ft Or \fqa image\ft ; here and through the rest of Daniel 2\f* \rb appeared|וַאֲל֨וּ\rb*. \rb A great|רַ֛ב\rb* \rb and dazzling|וְזִיוֵ֥הּ\rb* \rb statue|צַלְמָ֨א\rb*\rb |יַתִּ֖יר\rb* \rb stood|קָאֵ֣ם\rb* \rb before you|לְקָבְלָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and its form|וְרֵוֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb was awesome|דְּחִֽיל׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb The head|רֵאשֵׁהּ֙\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb of the statue|צַלְמָ֗א\rb* \rb was pure|טָ֔ב\rb* \rb gold|דְהַ֣ב\rb*, \rb its chest|חֲד֥וֹהִי\rb* \rb and arms|וּדְרָע֖וֹהִי\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb were silver|כְסַ֑ף\rb*, \rb its belly|מְע֥וֹהִי\rb* \rb and thighs|וְיַרְכָתֵ֖הּ\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb were bronze|נְחָֽשׁ׃\rb*, \v 33 \rb its legs|שָׁק֖וֹהִי\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb were iron|פַרְזֶ֑ל\rb*, \rb and its feet|רַגְל֕וֹהִי\rb* \rb were part|מִנְּהוֹן\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb and part|וּמִנְּהוֹן\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb clay|חֲסַֽף׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb As you|הֲוַ֗יְתָ\rb*\rb |עַ֠ד\rb* \rb watched|חָזֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb a stone|אֶ֙בֶן֙\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb was cut out|הִתְגְּזֶ֤רֶת\rb*,\f + \fr 2:34 \ft LXX \fqa cut out from a mountain\f* \rb but not|לָ֣א\rb* \rb by human hands|בִידַ֔יִן\rb*. \rb It struck|וּמְחָ֤ת\rb* \rb the statue|לְצַלְמָא֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its feet|רַגְל֔וֹהִי\rb* \rb of|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזְלָ֖א\rb* \rb and clay|וְחַסְפָּ֑א\rb*, \rb and crushed|וְהַדֵּ֖קֶת\rb* \rb them|הִמּֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb the iron|פַּרְזְלָא֩\rb*, \rb clay|חַסְפָּ֨א\rb*, \rb bronze|נְחָשָׁ֜א\rb*, \rb silver|כַּסְפָּ֣א\rb*, \rb and gold|וְדַהֲבָ֗א\rb* \rb were shattered|דָּ֣קוּ\rb*\rb |כַחֲדָ֡ה\rb* \rb and became|וַהֲווֹ֙\rb* \rb like chaff|כְּע֣וּר\rb* \rb on|מִן־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|אִדְּרֵי־\rb* \rb in summer|קַ֔יִט\rb*. \rb The wind|רוּחָ֔א\rb* \rb carried them|הִמּוֹן֙\rb* \rb away|וּנְשָׂ֤א\rb*, \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb not|לָא־\rb* \rb a trace|אֲתַ֖ר\rb* \rb of them|לְה֑וֹן\rb* \rb could be found|הִשְׁתֲּכַ֣ח\rb*. \rb But the stone|וְאַבְנָ֣א׀\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb had struck|מְחָ֣ת\rb* \rb the statue|לְצַלְמָ֗א\rb* \rb became|הֲוָ֛ת\rb* \rb a great|רַ֖ב\rb* \rb mountain|לְט֥וּר\rb* \rb and filled|וּמְלָ֥ת\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb earth|אַרְעָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb This|דְּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb was the dream|חֶלְמָ֔א\rb*; \rb now we will tell|נֵאמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |קֳדָם־\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb* \rb its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵ֖הּ\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb You|אַ֣נְתְּה\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, \rb are the king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb of kings|מַלְכַיָּ֑א\rb*, \rb to whom|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָ֣הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb has given|יְהַב־\rb*\rb |לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb sovereignty|מַלְכוּתָ֥א\rb*, \rb power|חִסְנָ֛א\rb*, \rb strength|וְתָקְפָּ֥א\rb*, \rb and glory|וִֽיקָרָ֖א\rb*. \v 38 \rb Wherever|וּבְכָל־\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the sons|בְּֽנֵי־\rb* \rb of men|אֲ֠נָשָׁא\rb* \rb or beasts|חֵיוַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the field|בָּרָ֤א\rb* \rb or birds|וְעוֹף־\rb* \rb of the air|שְׁמַיָּא֙\rb* \rb dwell|דָאֲרִין\rb*, \rb He has given them|יְהַ֣ב\rb* \rb into your hand|בִּידָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and has made you ruler|וְהַשְׁלְטָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over them all|בְּכָלְּה֑וֹן\rb*. \rb You are|אַנְתְּה־\rb* \rb that|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb head|רֵאשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb of|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb gold|דַהֲבָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb But after you|וּבָתְרָ֗ךְ\rb*, \rb there will arise|תְּק֛וּם\rb* \rb another|אָחֳרִ֖י\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכ֥וּ\rb*, \rb inferior|אֲרַ֣עא\rb* \rb to yours|מִנָּ֑ךְ\rb*.
\p \rb Next, a|אָחֳרִי֙\rb* \rb third|תְלִיתָיָא\rb* \rb kingdom|וּמַלְכ֨וּ\rb*, \rb one of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb bronze|נְחָשָׁ֔א\rb*,\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb will rule|תִשְׁלַ֖ט\rb* \rb the whole|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb earth|אַרְעָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb Finally, there will be|תֶּהֱוֵ֥א\rb* \rb a fourth|רְבִיעָיָה\rb* \rb kingdom|וּמַלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb as strong|תַקִּיפָ֖ה\rb* \rb as iron|כְּפַרְזְלָ֑א\rb*; \rb for|קֳבֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |דִּ֤י\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזְלָא֙\rb* \rb shatters|מְהַדֵּ֤ק\rb* \rb and crushes|וְחָשֵׁל֙\rb* \rb all things|כֹּ֔לָּא\rb*, \rb and like iron|וּֽכְפַרְזְלָ֛א\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb crushes|מְרָעַ֥ע\rb* \rb all things|כָּל־\rb*, \rb it will shatter|תַּדִּ֥ק\rb* \rb and crush|וְתֵרֹֽעַ׃\rb* \rb all the others|אִלֵּ֖ין\rb*. \v 41 \rb And just as|וְדִֽי־\rb* \rb you saw that|חֲזַ֜יְתָה\rb* \rb the feet|רַגְלַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb and toes|וְאֶצְבְּעָתָ֗א\rb* \rb were made|מִנְּהוֹן\rb*\rb |פֶחָר֙\rb* \rb partly of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb fired clay|חֲסַ֤ף\rb* \rb and partly of|וּמִנְּהוֹן\rb* \rb iron|פַּרְזֶ֔ל\rb*, \rb so this will be|תֶּהֱוֵ֔ה\rb* \rb a divided|פְלִיגָה֙\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכ֤וּ\rb*, \rb yet|וּמִן־\rb* \rb some of the strength|נִצְבְּתָ֥א\rb* \rb of|דִ֥י\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזְלָ֖א\rb* \rb will be in it|לֶֽהֱוֵא־\rb* —\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb just as|קֳבֵל֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you saw|חֲזַ֔יְתָה\rb* \rb the iron|פַּ֨רְזְלָ֔א\rb* \rb mixed|מְעָרַ֖ב\rb* \rb with clay|בַּחֲסַ֥ף\rb*\rb |טִינָֽא׃\rb*. \v 42 \rb And as the toes|וְאֶצְבְּעָת֙\rb* \rb of the feet|רַגְלַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb were partly|מִנְּהוֹן\rb* \rb iron|פַּרְזֶ֖ל\rb*\rb |וּמִנְּהוֹן\rb* \rb and partly|מִן־\rb* \rb clay|חֲסַ֑ף\rb*, \rb so this kingdom|מַלְכוּתָא֙\rb* \rb will be|תֶּהֱוֵ֣ה\rb* \rb partly|קְצָ֤ת\rb* \rb strong|תַקִּיפָ֔ה\rb* \rb and partly|וּמִנַּ֖הּ\rb*\rb |תֶּהֱוֵ֥ה\rb* \rb brittle|תְבִירָֽה׃\rb*. \v 43 \rb As|דִי\rb* \rb you saw|חֲזַ֗יְתָ\rb* \rb the iron|פַּרְזְלָא֙\rb* \rb mixed|מְעָרַב֙\rb* \rb with clay|בַּחֲסַ֣ף\rb*\rb |טִינָ֔א\rb*, \rb so the peoples|בִּזְרַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֲנָשָׁ֔א\rb*\f + \fr 2:43 \ft Aramaic \fqa the seed of men\f* \rb will mix with one another|מִתְעָרְבִ֤ין\rb*\rb |לֶהֱוֺן֙\rb* \rb but will not|וְלָֽא־\rb*\rb |לֶהֱוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb hold together|דָּבְקִ֖ין\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֑ה\rb* \rb any more|הֵֽא־\rb* \rb than|כְדִ֣י\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזְלָ֔א\rb*\rb |לָ֥א\rb* \rb mixes|מִתְעָרַ֖ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb clay|חַסְפָּֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 44 \rb In the days|וּֽבְיוֹמֵיה֞וֹן\rb* \rb of those|אִנּ֗וּן\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלָ֨הּ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֤א\rb* \rb will set up|יְקִים֩\rb* \rb a kingdom|מַלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb that|דִּ֤י\rb* \rb will never|לְעָלְמִין֙\rb*\rb |לָ֣א\rb* \rb be destroyed|תִתְחַבַּ֔ל\rb*, \rb nor will|לָ֣א\rb* \rb it|וּמַ֨לְכוּתָ֔ה\rb* \rb be left|תִשְׁתְּבִ֑ק\rb* \rb to another|אָחֳרָ֖ן\rb* \rb people|לְעַ֥ם\rb*. \rb It will shatter|תַּדִּ֤ק\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אִלֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb kingdoms|מַלְכְוָתָ֔א\rb*\rb |וְהִ֖יא\rb* \rb and bring them to an end|וְתָסֵיף֙\rb*, \rb but will itself stand|תְּק֥וּם\rb* \rb forever|לְעָלְמַיָּֽא׃\rb*. \v 45 \rb And just as|כָּל־\rb*\rb |קֳבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb you saw|חֲזַ֡יְתָ\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb a stone|אֶ֜בֶן\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb being cut out|אִתְגְּזֶ֨רֶת\rb* \rb of the mountain|מִטּוּרָא֩\rb* \rb without|לָ֣א\rb* \rb human hands|בִידַ֗יִן\rb*, \rb and it shattered|וְ֠הַדֶּקֶת\rb* \rb the iron|פַּרְזְלָ֨א\rb*, \rb bronze|נְחָשָׁ֤א\rb*, \rb clay|חַסְפָּא֙\rb*, \rb silver|כַּסְפָּ֣א\rb*, \rb and gold|וְדַהֲבָ֔א\rb*, \rb so the great|רַב֙\rb* \rb God|אֱלָ֥הּ\rb* \rb has told|הוֹדַ֣ע\rb* \rb the king|לְמַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb what|מָ֛ה\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb will happen|לֶהֱוֵ֖א\rb* \rb in the future|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |דְנָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb The dream|חֶלְמָ֖א\rb* \rb is true|וְיַצִּ֥יב\rb*, \rb and its interpretation|פִּשְׁרֵֽהּ׃פ\rb* \rb is trustworthy|וּמְהֵימַ֥ן\rb*.”
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar Promotes Daniel
\p \v 46 \rb At this|בֵּ֠אדַיִן\rb*, \rb King|מַלְכָּ֤א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶצַּר֙\rb* \rb fell|נְפַ֣ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his face|אַנְפּ֔וֹהִי\rb*, \rb paid homage|סְגִ֑ד\rb* \rb to Daniel|וּלְדָנִיֵּ֖אל\rb*, \rb and ordered|אֲמַ֖ר\rb* \rb that an offering|וּמִנְחָה֙\rb* \rb and incense|וְנִ֣יחֹחִ֔ין\rb* \rb be presented|לְנַסָּ֥כָה\rb* \rb to him|לֵֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 47 \rb The king|מַלְכָּ֨א\rb* \rb said|עָנֵה֩\rb* \rb to Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֜אל\rb*,\rb |וְאָמַ֗ר\rb* “\rb Your God|אֱלָהֲכ֗וֹן\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is truly|מִן־\rb*\rb |קְשֹׁט֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָ֧הּ\rb* \rb of gods|אֱלָהִ֛ין\rb* \rb and Lord|וּמָרֵ֥א\rb* \rb of kings|מַלְכִ֖ין\rb*, \rb the Revealer|וְגָלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Mysteries|רָזִ֑ין\rb*, \rb since|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you were able|יְכֵ֔לְתָּ\rb* \rb to reveal|לְמִגְלֵ֖א\rb* \rb this|דְנָֽה׃\rb* \rb mystery|רָזָ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 48 \rb Then|אֱדַ֨יִן\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb* \rb promoted|רַבִּ֗י\rb* \rb Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֣אל\rb* \rb and gave|יְהַב־\rb* \rb him|לֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb many|שַׂגִּיאָן֙\rb* \rb generous|רַבְרְבָ֤ן\rb* \rb gifts|וּמַתְּנָ֨ן\rb*. \rb He made him ruler|וְהַ֨שְׁלְטֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb province|מְדִינַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb and chief|וְרַב־\rb* \rb administrator|סִגְנִ֔ין\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wise men|חַכִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 49 \rb And at Daniel’s|וְדָנִיֵּאל֙\rb* \rb request|בְּעָ֣א\rb*,\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb appointed|וּמַנִּ֗י\rb* \rb Shadrach|לְשַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֑וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַ֤ל\rb* \rb manage|עֲבִֽידְתָּא֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֚י\rb* \rb the province|מְדִינַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*, \rb while Daniel|וְדָנִיֵּ֖אל\rb* \rb remained in the king’s|מַלְכָּֽא׃פ\rb* \rb court|בִּתְרַ֥ע\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar’s Golden Statue
\p \v 1 \rb King|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb made|עֲבַד֙\rb* \rb a golden|דְהַ֔ב\rb* \rb statue|צְלֵ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Or \fqa image\ft ; here and throughout Daniel 3\f*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb sixty|שִׁתִּ֔ין\rb* \rb cubits|אַמִּ֣ין\rb* \rb high|רוּמֵהּ֙\rb* \rb and six|שִׁ֑ת\rb* \rb cubits|אַמִּ֣ין\rb* \rb wide|פְּתָיֵ֖הּ\rb*,\f + \fr 3:1 \ft The statue was approximately 90 feet high and 9 feet wide (27.4 meters high and 2.7 meters wide).\f* \rb and he set it up|אֲקִימֵהּ֙\rb* \rb on the plain|בְּבִקְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Dura|דּוּרָ֔א\rb* \rb in the province|בִּמְדִינַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Then King|מַלְכָּ֡א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|וּנְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb sent|שְׁלַ֡ח\rb* \rb word to assemble|לְמִכְנַ֣שׁ׀\rb* \rb the satraps|לַֽאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּ֡א\rb*, \rb prefects|סִגְנַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb governors|וּֽפַחֲוָתָ֡א\rb*, \rb advisers|אֲדַרְגָּזְרַיָּא֩\rb*, \rb treasurers|גְדָ֨בְרַיָּ֤א\rb*, \rb judges|דְּתָבְרַיָּא֙\rb*, \rb magistrates|תִּפְתָּיֵ֔א\rb*, \rb and all the other|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb officials|שִׁלְטֹנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the provinces|מְדִֽינָתָ֑א\rb* \rb to attend|לְמֵתֵא֙\rb* \rb the dedication|לַחֲנֻכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the statue|צַלְמָ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb*\rb |נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb had set up|הֲקֵ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb So|בֵּאדַ֡יִן\rb* \rb the satraps|אֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּ֡א\rb*, \rb prefects|סִגְנַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb governors|וּֽפַחֲוָתָ֡א\rb*, \rb advisers|אֲדַרְגָּזְרַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb treasurers|גְדָבְרַיָּא֩\rb*, \rb judges|דְּתָ֨בְרַיָּ֜א\rb*, \rb magistrates|תִּפְתָּיֵ֗א\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the rulers|שִׁלְטֹנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the provinces|מְדִֽינָתָ֔א\rb* \rb assembled|מִֽתְכַּנְּשִׁ֡ין\rb* \rb for the dedication|לַחֲנֻכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the statue|צַלְמָ֔א\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb had set up|הֲקֵ֖ים\rb*, \rb and they stood|וְקָאֲמִין\rb* \rb before|לָקֳבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb it|צַלְמָ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb*\rb |נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּֽר׃\rb*\rb |הֲקֵ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then the herald|וְכָרוֹזָ֖א\rb* \rb loudly|בְחָ֑יִל\rb* \rb proclaimed|קָרֵ֣א\rb*, “\rb O people|עַֽמְמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb of every nation|אֻמַּיָּ֖א\rb* \rb and language|וְלִשָּׁנַיָּֽא׃\rb*, \rb this is what you are commanded|אָֽמְרִין֙\rb*: \v 5 \rb As soon as|בְּעִדָּנָ֡א\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb you hear|תִשְׁמְע֡וּן\rb* \rb the sound|קָ֣ל\rb* \rb of the horn|קַרְנָ֣א\rb*, \rb flute|מַ֠שְׁרוֹקִיתָא\rb*, \rb zither|קִיתָרוֹס\rb*, \rb lyre|סַבְּכָ֤א\rb*, \rb harp|פְּסַנְתֵּרִין֙\rb*, \rb pipes|סוּמְפֹּ֣נְיָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb kinds|זְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of music|זְמָרָ֑א\rb*,\f + \fr 3:5 \ft The precise identification of some musical instruments in this chapter is uncertain.\f* \rb you must fall down|תִּפְּל֤וּן\rb* \rb and worship|וְתִסְגְּדוּן֙\rb* \rb the golden|דַּהֲבָ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb statue that|לְצֶ֣לֶם\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb has set up|הֲקֵ֖ים\rb*. \v 6 \rb And whoever|וּמַן־\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb does not|לָ֥א\rb* \rb fall down|יִפֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb and worship|וְיִסְגֻּ֑ד\rb* \rb will immediately|שַׁעֲתָ֣א\rb* \rb be thrown|יִתְרְמֵ֔א\rb* \rb into|לְגֽוֹא־\rb* \rb the blazing|יָקִֽדְתָּֽא׃\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֖א\rb* \rb furnace|אַתּ֥וּן\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |קֳבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Therefore|דְּנָ֡ה\rb*,\rb |זִמְנָ֡א\rb* \rb as soon as|כְּדִ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb the people|עַמְמַיָּ֡א\rb* \rb heard|שָֽׁמְעִ֣ין\rb* \rb the sound|קָ֣ל\rb* \rb of the horn|קַרְנָא֩\rb*, \rb flute|מַשְׁר֨וֹקִיתָ֜א\rb*, \rb zither|קִיתָרֹס\rb*, \rb lyre|שַׂבְּכָא֙\rb*, \rb harp|פְּסַנְטֵרִ֔ין\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb kinds|זְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of music|זְמָרָ֑א\rb*, \rb the people|עַֽמְמַיָּ֜א\rb* \rb of every|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb nation|אֻמַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb and language|וְלִשָּׁנַיָּ֗א\rb* \rb would fall down|נָֽפְלִ֨ין\rb* \rb and worship|סָֽגְדִין֙\rb* \rb the golden|דַּהֲבָ֔א\rb* \rb statue|לְצֶ֣לֶם\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb had set up|הֲקֵ֖ים\rb*.
\s1 Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego Accused
\p \v 8 \rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |קֳבֵ֤ל\rb* \rb At this time|דְּנָה֙\rb*\rb |זִמְנָ֔א\rb* \rb some astrologers|כַּשְׂדָּאִ֑ין\rb*\f + \fr 3:8 \ft Or \fqa Chaldeans\f* \rb came forward|קְרִ֖בוּ\rb*\rb |גֻּבְרִ֣ין\rb* \rb and maliciously|וַאֲכַ֥לוּ\rb* \rb accused|קַרְצֵיה֖וֹן\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb the Jews|יְהוּדָיֵֽא׃\rb*, \v 9 \rb saying|עֲנוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאָ֣מְרִ֔ין\rb* \rb to King|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|לִנְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֖ר\rb*, “\rb O king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb*, \rb may you live|חֱיִֽי׃\rb* \rb forever|לְעָלְמִ֥ין\rb*! \v 10 \rb You|אַנְתָּה\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּא֮\rb*, \rb have issued|שָׂ֣מְתָּ\rb* \rb a decree|טְּעֵם֒\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb everyone|כָל־\rb*\rb |אֱנָ֡שׁ\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb hears|יִשְׁמַ֡ע\rb* \rb the sound|קָ֣ל\rb* \rb of the horn|קַרְנָ֣א\rb*, \rb flute|מַ֠שְׁרֹקִיתָא\rb*, \rb zither|קִיתָרֹס\rb*, \rb lyre|שַׂבְּכָ֤א\rb*, \rb harp|פְסַנְתֵּרִין֙\rb*, \rb pipes|וְסִיפֹּנְיָה\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb kinds|זְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of music|זְמָרָ֑א\rb* \rb must fall down|יִפֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb and worship|וְיִסְגֻּ֖ד\rb* \rb the golden|דַּהֲבָֽא׃\rb* \rb statue|לְצֶ֥לֶם\rb*, \v 11 \rb and that whoever|וּמַן־\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb does not|לָ֥א\rb* \rb fall down|יִפֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb and worship|וְיִסְגֻּ֑ד\rb* \rb will be thrown|יִתְרְמֵ֕א\rb* \rb into|לְגֽוֹא־\rb* \rb the blazing|יָקִֽדְתָּֽא׃\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֖א\rb* \rb furnace|אַתּ֥וּן\rb*. \v 12 \rb But there are|אִיתַ֞י\rb* \rb some|גֻּבְרִ֣ין\rb* \rb Jews|יְהוּדָאיִ֗ן\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have appointed|מַנִּ֤יתָ\rb*\rb |יָתְהוֹן֙\rb* \rb to manage|עַל־\rb*\rb |עֲבִידַת֙\rb* \rb the province|מְדִינַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* — \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֑וֹ\rb* —\rb |גֻּבְרַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb who|אִלֵּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb have ignored|לָא־\rb*\rb |שָׂ֨מֽוּ\rb*\rb |עֲלַיִךְ\rb* \rb you|טְעֵ֔ם\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*, \rb and have refused to|לָ֣א\rb* \rb serve|פָלְחִ֔ין\rb* \rb your gods|לֵאלָהַיִךְ\rb* \rb or worship|סָגְדִֽין׃ס\rb* \rb the golden|דַּהֲבָ֛א\rb* \rb statue|וּלְצֶ֧לֶם\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have set up|הֲקֵ֖ימְתָּ\rb*\rb |לָ֥א\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֤יִן\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּר֙\rb*, \rb furious|וַחֲמָ֔ה\rb* \rb with rage|בִּרְגַ֣ז\rb*, \rb summoned|אֲמַר֙\rb*\rb |לְהַיְתָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb Shadrach|לְשַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֑וֹ\rb*. \rb So|בֵּאדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb these|אִלֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb were brought|הֵיתָ֖יוּ\rb* \rb before|קֳדָ֥ם\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb |עָנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb and Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻֽכַדְנֶצַּר֙\rb* \rb said|וְאָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to them|לְה֔וֹן\rb*, “\rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֑וֹ\rb*, \rb is it true|הַצְדָּ֕א\rb* \rb that you do not|לָ֤א\rb*\rb |אִֽיתֵיכוֹן֙\rb* \rb serve|פָּֽלְחִ֔ין\rb* \rb my gods|לֵֽאלָהַ֗י\rb* \rb or worship|סָֽגְדִֽין׃\rb* \rb the golden|דַּהֲבָ֛א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb statue|וּלְצֶ֧לֶם\rb* \rb I have set up|הֲקֵ֖ימֶת\rb*?\rb |לָ֥א\rb* \v 15 \rb Now|כְּעַ֞ן\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb when|בְעִדָּנָ֡א\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb you hear|תִשְׁמְע֡וּן\rb* \rb the sound|קָ֣ל\rb* \rb of the horn|קַרְנָ֣א\rb*, \rb flute|מַשְׁרוֹקִיתָ֣א\rb*, \rb zither|קִיתָרֹס\rb*, \rb lyre|שַׂבְּכָ֡א\rb*, \rb harp|פְּסַנְתֵּרִין֩\rb*, \rb pipes|וְסוּמְפֹּ֨נְיָ֜ה\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb kinds|זְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of music|זְמָרָ֗א\rb*, \rb if|הֵ֧ן\rb* \rb you are|אִֽיתֵיכ֣וֹן\rb* \rb ready|עֲתִידִ֗ין\rb* \rb to fall down|תִּפְּל֣וּן\rb* \rb and worship|וְתִסְגְּדוּן֮\rb* \rb the statue|לְצַלְמָ֣א\rb*\rb |דִֽי־\rb* \rb I have made, very good|עַבְדֵת֒\rb*. \rb But if|וְהֵן֙\rb* \rb you refuse|לָ֣א\rb* \rb to worship|תִסְגְּד֔וּן\rb*, \rb you will be thrown|תִתְרְמ֔וֹן\rb* \rb at once|שַׁעֲתָ֣ה\rb* \rb into|לְגֽוֹא־\rb* \rb the blazing|יָקִֽדְתָּ֑א\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֖א\rb* \rb furnace|אַתּ֥וּן\rb*. \rb Then what|וּמַן־\rb* \rb god|אֱלָ֔הּ\rb* \rb will be able|ה֣וּא\rb*\rb |דֵּ֥י\rb* \rb to deliver you|יְשֵֽׁיזְבִנְכ֖וֹן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb my hands|יְדָֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 16 \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֤ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁךְ֙\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאָמְרִ֖ין\rb* \rb replied|עֲנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb to the king|לְמַלְכָּ֑א\rb*, “\rb O Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶצַּ֔ר\rb*, \rb we|אֲנַ֧חְנָה\rb* \rb have|לָֽא־\rb* \rb no need|חַשְׁחִ֨ין\rb* \rb to answer you|לַהֲתָבוּתָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb this|דְּנָ֛ה\rb* \rb matter|פִּתְגָ֖ם\rb*. \v 17 \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָהַ֙נָא֙\rb* \rb whom|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֣חְנָא\rb* \rb serve|פָֽלְחִ֔ין\rb* \rb exists|אִיתַ֗י\rb*, \rb then He is able|יָכִ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 3:17 \ft Or \fqa If this be so, then the God whom we serve is able\f* \rb to deliver us|לְשֵׁיזָבוּתַ֑נָא\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the blazing|יָקִֽדְתָּ֛א\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֧א\rb* \rb furnace|אַתּ֨וּן\rb* \rb and from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb your hand|יְדָ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb*\rb |יְשֵׁיזִֽב׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But even if|וְהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb He does not|לָ֔א\rb*, \rb let it|לֶהֱוֵא־\rb* \rb be known|יְדִ֥יעַ\rb* \rb to you|לָ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*, \rb that|דִּ֤י\rb* \rb we will not|לָא־\rb*\rb |אִיתַיְנָא\rb* \rb serve|פָֽלְחִ֔ין\rb* \rb your gods|לֵֽאלָהָיִךְ֙\rb* \rb or worship|נִסְגֻּֽד׃ס\rb* \rb the golden|דַּהֲבָ֛א\rb* \rb statue|וּלְצֶ֧לֶם\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have set up|הֲקֵ֖ימְתָּ\rb*\rb |לָ֥א\rb*.”
\s1 The Fiery Furnace
\p \v 19 \rb At this|בֵּאדַ֨יִן\rb*, \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֜ר\rb* \rb was filled|הִתְמְלִ֣י\rb* \rb with rage|חֱמָ֗א\rb*, \rb and the expression|וּצְלֵ֤ם\rb* \rb on his face|אַנְפּ֙וֹהִי֙\rb* \rb changed|אֶשְׁתַּנּוּ\rb* \rb toward|עַל־\rb* \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He gave orders|עָנֵ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְאָמַר֙\rb* \rb to heat|לְמֵזֵ֣א\rb* \rb the furnace|לְאַתּוּנָ֔א\rb*\rb |חַ֨ד־\rb* \rb seven times|שִׁבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb hotter|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb than|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb usual|חֲזֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְמֵזְיֵֽהּ׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb |וּלְגֻבְרִ֤ין\rb* \rb and he commanded|אֲמַר֙\rb* \rb some mighty men|גִּבָּֽרֵי־\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֙יִל֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb in his army|בְחַיְלֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb to tie up|לְכַפָּתָ֔ה\rb* \rb Shadrach|לְשַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֑וֹ\rb* \rb and throw them|לְמִרְמֵ֕א\rb* \rb into the blazing|יָקִֽדְתָּֽא׃\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֖א\rb* \rb furnace|לְאַתּ֥וּן\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb So|בֵּאדַ֜יִן\rb* \rb they|אִלֵּ֗ךְ\rb*\rb |גֻּבְרַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb were tied up|כְּפִ֙תוּ֙\rb*, \rb wearing robes|בְּסַרְבָּלֵיהוֹן֙\rb*, \rb trousers|פַּטִּישֵׁיהוֹן\rb*, \rb turbans|וְכַרְבְּלָתְה֖וֹן\rb*, \rb and other clothes|וּלְבֻשֵׁיה֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and they were thrown|וּרְמִ֕יו\rb* \rb into|לְגֽוֹא־\rb* \rb the blazing|יָקִֽדְתָּֽא׃\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֖א\rb* \rb furnace|אַתּ֥וּן\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |קֳבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֗ה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֞י\rb* \rb The king’s|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb command|מִלַּ֤ת\rb* \rb was so urgent|מַחְצְפָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the furnace|וְאַתּוּנָ֖א\rb* \rb so|יַתִּ֑ירָא\rb* \rb hot|אֵזֵ֣ה\rb* \rb that the fiery|נוּרָֽא׃\rb* \rb flames|שְׁבִיבָ֖א\rb* \rb killed|קַטִּ֣ל\rb*\rb |הִמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb the|אִלֵּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb who|דִּ֤י\rb* \rb carried up|הַסִּ֙קוּ֙\rb* \rb Shadrach|לְשַׁדְרַ֤ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁךְ֙\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֔וֹ\rb*. \v 23 \rb And these|אִלֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb three|תְּלָ֣תֵּה֔וֹן\rb* \rb men|וְגֻבְרַיָּ֤א\rb*, \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֖ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֑וֹ\rb*, \rb firmly bound|מְכַפְּתִֽין׃פ\rb*, \rb fell|נְפַ֛לוּ\rb* \rb into|לְגֽוֹא־\rb* \rb the blazing|יָֽקִדְתָּ֖א\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֥א\rb* \rb furnace|אַתּוּן־\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Suddenly|אֱדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*\rb |תְּוַ֖הּ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb jumped up|וְקָ֣ם\rb* \rb in amazement|בְּהִתְבְּהָלָ֑ה\rb*\rb |עָנֵ֨ה\rb* \rb and asked|וְאָמַ֜ר\rb* \rb his advisers|לְהַדָּֽבְר֗וֹהִי\rb*, “\rb Did we not|הֲלָא֩\rb* \rb throw|רְמֵ֤ינָא\rb* \rb three|תְּלָתָ֜א\rb* \rb men|גֻבְרִ֨ין\rb*, \rb firmly bound|מְכַפְּתִ֔ין\rb*, \rb into|לְגוֹא־\rb* \rb the fire|נוּרָא֙\rb*?”
\p “\rb Certainly|יַצִּיבָ֖א\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb*,” \rb they replied|עָנַ֤יִן\rb*\rb |וְאָמְרִין֙\rb*.
\p \v 25 “\rb Look|הָֽא־\rb*!”\rb |עָנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb he exclaimed|וְאָמַ֗ר\rb*. “\rb I|אֲנָ֨ה\rb* \rb see|חָזֵ֜ה\rb* \rb four|אַרְבְּעָ֗ה\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרִ֣ין\rb*, \rb unbound|שְׁרַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb and unharmed|וַחֲבָ֖ל\rb*\rb |לָא־\rb*\rb |אִיתַ֣י\rb*, \rb walking around|מַהְלְכִ֣ין\rb* \rb in|בְּגֽוֹא־\rb* \rb the fire|נוּרָ֔א\rb* — \rb and the fourth|רְבִיעָיָא\rb* \rb looks|וְרֵוֵהּ֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb like|דָּמֵ֖ה\rb* \rb a son|לְבַר־\rb* \rb of the gods|אֱלָהִֽין׃ס\rb*!\f + \fr 3:25 \ft Or \fqa like the Son of God\f*”
\p \v 26 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֜יִן\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֗ר\rb* \rb approached|קְרֵ֣ב\rb* \rb the door|לִתְרַע֮\rb* \rb of the blazing|יָקִֽדְתָּא֒\rb* \rb fiery|נוּרָ֣א\rb* \rb furnace|אַתּ֣וּן\rb*\rb |עָנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb and called out|וְאָמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֨ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֧ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵד־\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֛וֹ\rb*, \rb servants|עַבְד֛וֹהִי\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb of the Most High|עִלָּיָא\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָ֥א\rb*, \rb come out|פֻּ֣קוּ\rb*!”\rb |וֶאֱת֑וֹ\rb*
\p \rb So|בֵּאדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֛ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֖וֹ\rb* \rb came out|נָֽפְקִ֗ין\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb*\rb |גּ֥וֹא\rb* \rb the fire|נוּרָֽא׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb and when the satraps|אֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּ֞א\rb*, \rb prefects|סִגְנַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb governors|וּפַחֲוָתָא֮\rb*, \rb and royal|מַלְכָּא֒\rb* \rb advisers|וְהַדָּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb had gathered around|וּ֠מִֽתְכַּנְּשִׁין\rb*, \rb they saw|חָזַ֣יִן\rb* \rb that the fire|נוּרָ֜א\rb* \rb had no|לָֽא־\rb* \rb effect|שְׁלֵ֨ט\rb* \rb on the bodies|בְּגֶשְׁמְה֗וֹן\rb* \rb of these|אִלֵּ֡ךְ\rb*\rb |דִּי֩\rb* \rb men|לְגֻבְרַיָּ֣א\rb*. \rb Not|לָ֣א\rb* \rb a hair|וּשְׂעַ֤ר\rb* \rb of their heads|רֵֽאשְׁהוֹן֙\rb* \rb was singed|הִתְחָרַ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb their robes|וְסָרְבָּלֵיה֖וֹן\rb* \rb were unaffected|לָ֣א\rb*\rb |שְׁנ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and there was no|לָ֥א\rb*\rb |עֲדָ֖ת\rb* \rb smell|וְרֵ֣יחַ\rb* \rb of fire|נ֔וּר\rb* \rb on them|בְּהֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶצַּ֜ר\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb declared|עָנֵ֨ה\rb*, “\rb Blessed|בְּרִ֤יךְ\rb* \rb be the God|אֱלָהֲהוֹן֙\rb* \rb of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֤ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁךְ֙\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֔וֹ\rb*, \rb who has sent|שְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb His angel|מַלְאֲכֵהּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 3:28 \ft Or \fqa Angel\f* \rb and delivered|וְשֵׁיזִ֣ב\rb* \rb His servants|לְעַבְד֔וֹהִי\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb trusted|הִתְרְחִ֖צוּ\rb* \rb in Him|עֲל֑וֹהִי\rb*. \rb They violated|שַׁנִּ֔יו\rb*\rb |וִיהַ֣בוּ\rb* \rb the king’s|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb command|וּמִלַּ֤ת\rb* \rb and risked their lives|גֶשְׁמֵיהוֹן\rb*\rb |דִּ֠י\rb*\rb |לָֽא־\rb* \rb rather than serve|יִפְלְח֤וּן\rb*\rb |וְלָֽא־\rb* \rb or worship|יִסְגְּדוּן֙\rb* \rb any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb god|אֱלָ֔הּ\rb* \rb except|לָהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb their own God|לֵאלָֽהֲהֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb Therefore I|וּמִנִּי֮\rb* \rb decree|שִׂ֣ים\rb*\rb |טְעֵם֒\rb* \rb that|דִּי֩\rb* \rb the people|עַ֨ם\rb* \rb of any|כָל־\rb* \rb nation|אֻמָּ֜ה\rb* \rb or language|וְלִשָּׁ֗ן\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb say|יֵאמַ֤ר\rb* \rb anything offensive|שֵׁלָה\rb* \rb against|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָהֲה֗וֹן\rb* \rb of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb Shadrach|שַׁדְרַ֤ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁךְ֙\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֔וֹא\rb* \rb will be cut|יִתְעֲבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb into pieces|הַדָּמִ֣ין\rb* \rb and their houses|וּבַיְתֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb reduced|יִשְׁתַּוֵּ֑ה\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb to rubble|נְוָלִ֣י\rb*. \rb For|קֳבֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is|אִיתַי֙\rb* \rb no|לָ֤א\rb* \rb other|אָחֳרָ֔ן\rb* \rb god|אֱלָ֣ה\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb can|יִכֻּ֥ל\rb* \rb deliver|לְהַצָּלָ֖ה\rb* \rb in this way|כִּדְנָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 30 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb promoted|הַצְלַ֛ח\rb* \rb Shadrach|לְשַׁדְרַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb Meshach|מֵישַׁ֛ךְ\rb*,\rb |וַעֲבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb and Abednego|נְג֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the province|בִּמְדִינַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃פ\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar Confesses God’s Kingdom
\p \v 1 \rb King|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֣ר\rb*,
\p \rb To the people|עַֽמְמַיָּ֞א\rb* \rb of every|לְֽכָל־\rb* \rb nation|אֻמַיָּ֧א\rb* \rb and language|וְלִשָּׁנַיָּ֛א\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb dwell|דָאֲרִין\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth|אַרְעָ֖א\rb*:
\p \rb May your prosperity|שְׁלָמְכ֥וֹן\rb* \rb be multiplied|יִשְׂגֵּֽא׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb I am pleased|שְׁפַ֥ר\rb*\rb |קָֽדָמַ֖י\rb* \rb to declare|לְהַחֲוָיָֽה׃\rb* \rb the signs|אָֽתַיָּא֙\rb* \rb and wonders|וְתִמְהַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb that|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb the Most High|עִלָּיָא\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָ֖א\rb* \rb has performed|עֲבַ֣ד\rb* \rb for me|עִמִּ֔י\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb How|כְּמָ֣ה\rb* \rb great|רַבְרְבִ֔ין\rb* \rb are His signs|אָת֙וֹהִי֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb how|כְּמָ֣ה\rb* \rb mighty|תַקִּיפִ֑ין\rb* \rb His wonders|וְתִמְה֖וֹהִי\rb*!
\q1 \rb His kingdom|מַלְכוּתֵהּ֙\rb* \rb is an eternal|עָלַ֔ם\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכ֣וּת\rb*;
\q2 \rb His dominion endures|וְשָׁלְטָנֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb from|עִם־\rb* \rb generation|דָּ֥ר\rb* \rb to generation|וְדָֽר׃\rb*.
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar’s Dream of a Great Tree
\p \v 4 \rb I|אֲנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֗ר\rb*, \rb was|הֲוֵית֙\rb* \rb at ease|שְׁלֵ֤ה\rb* \rb in my house|בְּבֵיתִ֔י\rb* \rb and flourishing|וְרַעְנַ֖ן\rb* \rb in my palace|בְּהֵיכְלִֽי׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb I had|חֲזֵ֖ית\rb* \rb a dream|חֵ֥לֶם\rb*, \rb and it frightened me|וִֽידַחֲלִנַּ֑נִי\rb*; \rb while I was in|עַֽל־\rb* \rb my bed|מִשְׁכְּבִ֔י\rb*, \rb the images|וְהַרְהֹרִין֙\rb* \rb and visions|וְחֶזְוֵ֥י\rb* \rb in my mind|רֵאשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb alarmed me|יְבַהֲלֻנַּֽנִי׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb So|וּמִנִּי֙\rb* \rb I issued|שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb a decree|טְעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb that all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the wise men|חַכִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb be brought|לְהַנְעָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb before me|קָֽדָמַ֔י\rb* \rb to|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb interpret|פְשַׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָ֖א\rb* \rb for me|יְהֽוֹדְעֻנַּֽנִי׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb When|בֵּאדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb the magicians|חַרְטֻמַיָּא֙\rb*, \rb enchanters|אָֽשְׁפַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb astrologers|כַּשְׂדָּיֵא\rb*,\f + \fr 4:7 \ft Or \fqa Chaldeans\f* \rb and diviners|וְגָזְרַיָּ֑א\rb* \rb came in|עָלֲלִין\rb*, \rb I|אֲנָה֙\rb*\rb |קֳדָ֣מֵיה֔וֹן\rb* \rb told them|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb the dream|וְחֶלְמָ֗א\rb*, \rb but they could not|לָא־\rb* \rb interpret it|וּפִשְׁרֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb for me|לִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb But at|וְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb last|אָחֳרֵ֡ין\rb*, \rb into my presence|קָֽדָמַ֨י\rb* \rb came|עַל֩\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֜אל\rb* (\rb whose|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb name is|שְׁמֵ֤הּ\rb* \rb Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּר֙\rb* \rb after the name|כְּשֻׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of my god|אֱלָהִ֔י\rb*, \rb and in whom|וְדִ֛י\rb* \rb is the spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of the holy|קַדִּישִׁ֖ין\rb* \rb gods|אֱלָהִ֥ין\rb*\rb |בֵּ֑הּ\rb*). \rb And I told him|אַמְרֵֽת׃\rb* \rb the dream|וְחֶלְמָ֖א\rb*\rb |קָֽדָמ֥וֹהִי\rb*: \v 9 “\rb O Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּר֮\rb*, \rb chief|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb of the magicians|חַרְטֻמַיָּא֒\rb*,\rb |דִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb I|אֲנָ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יִדְעֵ֗ת\rb* \rb that|דִּ֠י\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the holy|קַדִּישִׁין֙\rb* \rb gods|אֱלָהִ֤ין\rb* \rb is in you|בָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and that|וְכָל־\rb* \rb no|לָא־\rb* \rb mystery|רָ֖ז\rb* \rb baffles|אָנֵ֣ס\rb* \rb you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb So explain to me|אֱמַֽר׃\rb* \rb the visions|חֶזְוֵ֨י\rb*\rb |דִֽי־\rb* \rb I saw|חֲזֵ֛ית\rb* \rb in my dream|חֶלְמִ֧י\rb*, \rb and their interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵ֖הּ\rb*. \v 10 \rb In these visions|וְחֶזְוֵ֥י\rb* \rb of my mind|רֵאשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb as I was lying|עַֽל־\rb* \rb in bed|מִשְׁכְּבִ֑י\rb*, \rb I saw this|חָזֵ֣ה\rb* \rb come to pass|הֲוֵ֔ית\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb There was|וַאֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb a tree|אִילָ֛ן\rb* \rb in the midst|בְּג֥וֹא\rb* \rb of the land|אַרְעָ֖א\rb*,
\q2 \rb and its height|וְרוּמֵ֥הּ\rb* \rb was great|שַׂגִּֽיא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb The tree|אִֽילָנָ֖א\rb* \rb grew large|רְבָ֥ה\rb* \rb and strong|וּתְקִ֑ף\rb*;
\q2 \rb its top|וְרוּמֵהּ֙\rb* \rb reached|יִמְטֵ֣א\rb* \rb the sky|לִשְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb*,
\q1 \rb and it was visible|וַחֲזוֹתֵ֖הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb to the ends|לְס֥וֹף\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of the earth|אַרְעָֽא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Its leaves|עָפְיֵ֤הּ\rb* \rb were beautiful|שַׁפִּיר֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb its fruit|וְאִנְבֵּ֣הּ\rb* \rb was abundant|שַׂגִּ֔יא\rb*,
\q2 \rb and upon it|בֵ֑הּ\rb* \rb was food|וּמָז֨וֹן\rb* \rb for all|לְכֹ֖לָּא־\rb*.
\q1 \rb Under it|תְּחֹת֜וֹהִי\rb* \rb the beasts|חֵיוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|בָּרָ֗א\rb* \rb found shelter|תַּטְלֵ֣ל׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb in its branches|וּבְעַנְפ֙וֹהִי֙\rb* \rb the birds|צִפֲּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the air|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb nested|יְדֻרוּן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and from it|וּמִנֵּ֖הּ\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb creature|בִּשְׂרָֽא׃\rb* \rb was fed|יִתְּזִ֥ין\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb As I lay|עַֽל־\rb* \rb on my bed|מִשְׁכְּבִ֑י\rb*,\rb |וַאֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb I also saw|חָזֵ֥ה\rb*\rb |הֲוֵ֛ית\rb* \rb in the visions|בְּחֶזְוֵ֥י\rb* \rb of my mind|רֵאשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb a watcher|עִ֣יר\rb*,\f + \fr 4:13 \ft Or \fqa an angelic watcher \ft or \fqa a messenger\ft ; also in verses 17 and 23\f* \rb a holy one|וְקַדִּ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb coming down|נָחִֽת׃\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֖א\rb*. \v 14 \rb He called out|קָרֵ֨א\rb* \rb in a loud voice|בְחַ֜יִל\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |אָמַ֗ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Cut down|גֹּ֤דּוּ\rb* \rb the tree|אִֽילָנָא֙\rb* \rb and chop off|וְקַצִּ֣צוּ\rb* \rb its branches|עַנְפ֔וֹהִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb strip off|אַתַּ֥רוּ\rb* \rb its leaves|עָפְיֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb and scatter|וּבַדַּ֣רוּ\rb* \rb its fruit|אִנְבֵּ֑הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Let the beasts|חֵֽיוְתָא֙\rb* \rb flee|תְּנֻ֤ד\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb under it|תַּחְתּ֔וֹהִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the birds|וְצִפְּרַיָּ֖א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb its branches|עַנְפֽוֹהִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb But|בְּרַ֨ם\rb* \rb leave|שְׁבֻ֔קוּ\rb* \rb the stump|עִקַּ֤ר\rb* \rb with its roots|שָׁרְשׁ֙וֹהִי֙\rb* \rb in the ground|בְּאַרְעָ֣א\rb*,
\q2 \rb with a band|וּבֶֽאֱסוּר֙\rb* \rb of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזֶ֣ל\rb* \rb and bronze around it|וּנְחָ֔שׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb in the tender grass|בְּדִתְאָ֖א\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the field|בָרָ֑א\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb Let him be drenched|יִצְטַבַּ֔ע\rb* \rb with the dew|וּבְטַ֤ל\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּא֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and graze|חֲלָקֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the beasts|חֵיוְתָ֥א\rb* \rb on the grass|בַּעֲשַׂ֥ב\rb* \rb of the earth|אַרְעָֽא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Let his mind|לִבְבֵהּ֙\rb* \rb be changed|יְשַׁנּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb that of a man|אֱנוֹשָׁא\rb*,
\q2 \rb and let him be given|יִתְיְהִ֣ב\rb* \rb the mind|וּלְבַ֥ב\rb* \rb of a beast|חֵיוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb till seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb times|עִדָּנִ֖ין\rb* \rb pass him|יַחְלְפ֥וּן\rb* \rb by|עֲלֽוֹהִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb This decision|פִּתְגָמָ֔א\rb* \rb is the decree|בִּגְזֵרַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the watchers|עִירִין֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the verdict|שְׁאֵֽלְתָ֑א\rb* \rb declared|וּמֵאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb by the holy ones|קַדִּישִׁ֖ין\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that|עַד־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרַ֡ת\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the living|חַ֠יַּיָּא\rb* \rb will know|יִנְדְּע֣וּן\rb*
\q1 \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Most High|עִלָּיָא\rb* \rb rules|שַׁלִּ֨יט\rb* \rb over the kingdom|בְּמַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb of mankind|אֱנוֹשָׁא\rb*
\q2 \rb and gives it|יִתְּנִנַּ֔הּ\rb* \rb to whom|וּלְמַן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֤י\rb* \rb He wishes|יִצְבֵּא֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb setting|יְקִ֥ים\rb* \rb over it|עֲלַיַּהּ׃\rb* \rb the lowliest|וּשְׁפַ֥ל\rb* \rb of men|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb*.’
\p \v 18 \rb This|דְּנָה֙\rb* \rb is the dream|חֶלְמָ֣א\rb* \rb that I|אֲנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb King|מַלְכָּ֣א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֑ר\rb*, \rb saw|חֲזֵ֔ית\rb*. \rb Now|וְאַנְתָּה\rb*, \rb Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּ֜ר\rb*, \rb tell me|אֱמַ֗ר\rb* \rb the interpretation|פִּשְׁרֵ֣א׀\rb*, \rb because|קֳבֵל֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb none|לָֽא־\rb* \rb of the wise men|חַכִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of my kingdom|מַלְכוּתִ֗י\rb* \rb can|יָכְלִ֤ין\rb* \rb interpret it|פִּשְׁרָא֙\rb* \rb for me|לְהוֹדָ֣עֻתַ֔נִי\rb*. \rb But you|וְאַנְתָּה\rb* \rb are able|כָּהֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb because|דִּ֛י\rb* \rb the spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of the holy|קַדִּישִׁ֖ין\rb* \rb gods|אֱלָהִ֥ין\rb* \rb is in you|בָּֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\s1 Daniel Interprets the Second Dream
\p \v 19 \rb For|אֱדַ֨יִן\rb* \rb a|חֲדָ֔ה\rb* \rb time|כְּשָׁעָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּֽנִיֵּ֜אל\rb*, \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb was also known as|שְׁמֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּ֗ר\rb*, \rb was perplexed|אֶשְׁתּוֹמַם֙\rb*, \rb and his thoughts|וְרַעְיֹנֹ֖הִי\rb* \rb alarmed him|יְבַהֲלֻנֵּ֑הּ\rb*.
\p \rb So the king|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb said|עָנֵ֨ה\rb*, “\rb Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּר֙\rb*, \rb do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb let the dream|חֶלְמָ֤א\rb* \rb or its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵא֙\rb* \rb alarm you|יְבַהֲלָ֔ךְ\rb*.”
\p “\rb My lord|מָרְאִי\rb*,”\rb |וְאָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb replied|עָנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb Belteshazzar|בֵלְטְשַׁאצַּר֙\rb*, “\rb may the dream|חֶלְמָ֥א\rb* \rb apply to those who hate you|לְשָׂנְאַיִךְ\rb*, \rb and its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵ֥הּ\rb* \rb to your enemies|לְעָרַיִךְ׃\rb*!
\p \v 20 \rb The tree|אִֽילָנָא֙\rb* \rb you saw|חֲזַ֔יְתָ\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb grew large|רְבָ֖ה\rb* \rb and strong|וּתְקִ֑ף\rb*, \rb whose top|וְרוּמֵהּ֙\rb* \rb reached|יִמְטֵ֣א\rb* \rb the sky|לִשְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb and was visible|וַחֲזוֹתֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the earth|אַרְעָֽא׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb whose foliage|וְעָפְיֵ֤הּ\rb* \rb was beautiful|שַׁפִּיר֙\rb* \rb and whose fruit|וְאִנְבֵּ֣הּ\rb* \rb was abundant|שַׂגִּ֔יא\rb*, \rb providing food|וּמָז֨וֹן\rb* \rb for all|לְכֹ֖לָּא־\rb*, \rb under which|תְּחֹת֗וֹהִי\rb* \rb the beasts|חֵיוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|בָּרָ֔א\rb* \rb lived|תְּדוּר֙\rb*, \rb and in whose branches|וּבְעַנְפ֕וֹהִי\rb* \rb the birds|צִפֲּרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the air|שְׁמַיָּֽא׃\rb* \rb nested|יִשְׁכְּנָ֖ן\rb*— \v 22 \rb you|אַנְתָּה\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, \rb are that tree|ה֣וּא\rb*!\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb For you have become great|רְבַ֖ית\rb* \rb and strong|וּתְקֵ֑פְתְּ\rb*; \rb your greatness|וּרְבוּתָ֤ךְ\rb* \rb has grown|רְבָת֙\rb* \rb to reach|וּמְטָ֣ת\rb* \rb the sky|לִשְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb and your dominion|וְשָׁלְטָנָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb extends to the ends|לְס֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the earth|אַרְעָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb And|וְדִ֣י\rb* \rb you, O king|מַלְכָּ֡א\rb*, \rb saw|חֲזָ֣ה\rb* \rb a watcher|עִ֣יר\rb*, \rb a holy one|וְקַדִּ֣ישׁ\rb*, \rb coming down|נָחִ֣ת׀\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֡א\rb* \rb and saying|וְאָמַר֩\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Cut down|גֹּ֨דּוּ\rb* \rb the tree|אִֽילָנָ֜א\rb* \rb and destroy it|וְחַבְּל֗וּהִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb but|בְּרַ֨ם\rb* \rb leave|שְׁבֻ֔קוּ\rb* \rb the stump|עִקַּ֤ר\rb* \rb with its roots|שָׁרְשׁ֙וֹהִי֙\rb* \rb in the ground|בְּאַרְעָ֣א\rb*,
\q1 \rb with a band|וּבֶאֱסוּר֙\rb* \rb of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזֶ֣ל\rb* \rb and bronze around it|וּנְחָ֔שׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb in the tender grass|בְּדִתְאָ֖א\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the field|בָרָ֑א\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb Let him be drenched|יִצְטַבַּ֗ע\rb* \rb with the dew|וּבְטַ֧ל\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֣א\rb*,
\q2 \rb and graze|חֲלָקֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the beasts|חֵיוַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the field|בָּרָא֙\rb*
\q2 \rb till|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb times|עִדָּנִ֖ין\rb* \rb pass him|יַחְלְפ֥וּן\rb* \rb by|עֲלֽוֹהִי׃\rb*.’
\p \v 24 \rb This|דְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb is the interpretation|פִשְׁרָ֖א\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*, \rb and this is the decree|וּגְזֵרַ֤ת\rb* \rb that the Most High|עִלָּיָא\rb*\rb |הִ֔יא\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb has issued|מְטָ֖ת\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb my lord|מַרְאִי\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb*:
\p \v 25 \rb You will be driven away|טָֽרְדִ֣ין\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb mankind|אֲנָשָׁ֡א\rb*, \rb and your dwelling|מְדֹרָ֜ךְ\rb* \rb will be|לֶהֱוֵ֨ה\rb* \rb with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the beasts|חֵיוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|בָּרָא֩\rb*. \rb You will feed on|יְטַֽעֲמ֗וּן\rb* \rb grass|וְעִשְׂבָּ֥א\rb* \rb like an ox|כְתוֹרִ֣ין׀\rb* \rb and be drenched|מְצַבְּעִ֔ין\rb* \rb with the dew|וּמִטַּ֤ל\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּא֙\rb*, \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb times|עִדָּנִ֖ין\rb* \rb shall pass|יַחְלְפ֣וּן\rb* \rb you by|עֲלָ֑יךְ\rb*, \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb you acknowledge|תִנְדַּ֗ע\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Most High|עִלָּיאָ֙\rb* \rb rules|שַׁלִּ֤יט\rb* \rb over the kingdom|בְּמַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb of mankind|אֲנָשָׁ֔א\rb* \rb and gives it|יִתְּנִנַּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb to whom|וּלְמַן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb He wishes|יִצְבֵּ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb As for|וְדִ֣י\rb* \rb the command|אֲמַ֗רוּ\rb* \rb to leave|לְמִשְׁבַּ֞ק\rb* \rb the stump|עִקַּ֤ר\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the tree|אִֽילָנָ֔א\rb* \rb with its roots|שָׁרְשׁ֙וֹהִי֙\rb*, \rb your kingdom|מַלְכוּתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb will be restored|קַיָּמָ֑ה\rb* \rb to you|מִן־\rb* \rb as soon as|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you acknowledge|תִנְדַּ֔ע\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb Heaven|שְׁמַיָּֽא׃\rb* \rb rules|שַׁלִּטִ֖ן\rb*. \v 27 \rb Therefore|לָהֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb may my advice|מִלְכִּי֙\rb* \rb be pleasing|יִשְׁפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb to you|עֲלַיִךְ\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb*. \rb Break away|פְרֻ֔ק\rb* \rb from your sins|וַחֲטָיָךְ\rb* \rb by doing what is right|בְּצִדְקָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and from your iniquities|וַעֲוָיָתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb by showing mercy|בְּמִחַ֣ן\rb* \rb to the oppressed|עֲנָ֑יִן\rb*. \rb Perhaps|הֵ֛ן\rb* \rb there will be|תֶּהֱוֵ֥א\rb* \rb an extension|אַרְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb of your prosperity|לִשְׁלֵוְתָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Second Dream Fulfilled
\p \v 28 \rb All|כֹּ֣לָּא\rb* \rb this happened|מְּטָ֔א\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּֽא׃פ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֖ר\rb*. \v 29 \rb Twelve|תְּרֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עֲשַׂ֑ר\rb* \rb months|יַרְחִ֖ין\rb* \rb later|לִקְצָ֥ת\rb*, \rb as he was|הֲוָֽה׃\rb* \rb walking|מְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the roof of the royal palace|הֵיכַ֧ל\rb*\rb |מַלְכוּתָ֛א\rb* \rb of|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb Babylon|בָבֶ֖ל\rb*, \v 30 \rb the king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb exclaimed|עָנֵ֤ה\rb*, “\rb Is this|דָא־\rb*\rb |הִ֖יא\rb* \rb not|הֲלָ֥א\rb* \rb Babylon|בָּבֶ֣ל\rb* \rb the Great|רַבְּתָ֑א\rb*, \rb which|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb I myself|אֲנָ֤ה\rb* \rb have built|בֱנַיְתַהּ֙\rb* \rb as a royal|מַלְכ֔וּ\rb* \rb residence|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb by the might|בִּתְקַ֥ף\rb* \rb of my power|חִסְנִ֖י\rb* \rb and for the glory|וְלִיקָ֥ר\rb* \rb of my majesty|הַדְרִֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 31 \rb While the words|מִלְּתָא֙\rb* \rb were still|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb in the king’s|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb mouth|בְּפֻ֣ם\rb*, \rb a voice|קָ֖ל\rb* \rb came|נְפַ֑ל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֣א\rb*: “\rb It is decreed|אָֽמְרִין֙\rb* \rb to you|לָ֤ךְ\rb*, \rb King|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֣ר\rb*, \rb that the kingdom|מַלְכוּתָ֖ה\rb* \rb has departed|עֲדָ֥ת\rb* \rb from you|מִנָּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb You will be driven away|טָֽרְדִ֜ין\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb mankind|אֲנָשָׁא֩\rb* \rb to live|מְדֹרָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb with|וְֽעִם־\rb* \rb the beasts|חֵיוַ֧ת\rb* \rb of the field|בָּרָ֣א\rb*, \rb and you will feed on|יְטַעֲמ֔וּן\rb* \rb grass|עִשְׂבָּ֤א\rb* \rb like an ox|כְתוֹרִין֙\rb*. \rb And seven|וְשִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb times|עִדָּנִ֖ין\rb* \rb will pass|יַחְלְפ֣וּן\rb* \rb you by|עִלַיִךְ\rb*, \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb you acknowledge|תִנְדַּ֗ע\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Most High|עִלָּיאָ֙\rb* \rb rules|שַׁלִּ֤יט\rb* \rb over the kingdom|בְּמַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb of mankind|אֲנָשָׁ֔א\rb* \rb and gives it|יִתְּנִנַּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb to whom|וּלְמַן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb He wishes|יִצְבֵּ֖א\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb At that|בַּהּ־\rb* \rb moment|שַׁעֲתָ֗א\rb* \rb the sentence|מִלְּתָא֮\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּר֒\rb* \rb was fulfilled|סָ֣פַת\rb*. \rb He was driven away|טְרִ֔יד\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb mankind|אֲנָשָׁ֣א\rb*. \rb He ate|יֵאכֻ֔ל\rb* \rb grass|וְעִשְׂבָּ֤א\rb* \rb like an ox|כְתוֹרִין֙\rb*, \rb and his body|גִּשְׁמֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb was drenched|יִצְטַבַּ֑ע\rb* \rb with the dew|וּמִטַּ֥ל\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֖א\rb*, \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb his hair|שַׂעְרֵ֛הּ\rb* \rb grew|רְבָ֖ה\rb* \rb like the feathers of an eagle|כְּנִשְׁרִ֥ין\rb* \rb and his nails|וְטִפְר֥וֹהִי\rb* \rb like the claws of a bird|כְצִפְּרִֽין׃\rb*.
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar Restored
\p \v 34 \rb But at the end|וְלִקְצָ֣ת\rb* \rb of those days|יֽוֹמַיָּה֩\rb* \rb I|אֲנָ֨ה\rb*, \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֜ר\rb*, \rb looked up|עַיְנַ֣י׀\rb*\rb |נִטְלֵ֗ת\rb* \rb to heaven|לִשְׁמַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb and my sanity|וּמַנְדְּעִי֙\rb* \rb was restored|יְת֔וּב\rb* \rb to me|עֲלַ֣י\rb*. \rb Then I praised|בָּרְכֵ֔ת\rb* \rb the Most High|וּלְעִלָּיָא\rb*, \rb and I honored|שַׁבְּחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and glorified|וְהַדְּרֵ֑ת\rb*\rb |דִּ֤י\rb* \rb Him who lives|וּלְחַ֥י\rb* \rb forever|עָלְמָ֖א\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb For His dominion|שָׁלְטָנֵהּ֙\rb* \rb is an everlasting|עָלַ֔ם\rb* \rb dominion|שָׁלְטָ֣ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and His kingdom|וּמַלְכוּתֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb endures from|עִם־\rb* \rb generation|דָּ֥ר\rb* \rb to generation|וְדָֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 35 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the peoples|דָּאֲרֵי\rb* \rb of the earth|אַרְעָא֙\rb*
\q2 \rb are counted|חֲשִׁיבִ֔ין\rb* \rb as nothing|כְּלָ֣ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb and He does|עָבֵד֙\rb* \rb as He pleases|וּֽכְמִצְבְּיֵ֗הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb with the army|בְּחֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb*
\q2 \rb and the peoples|וְדָאֲרֵי\rb* \rb of the earth|אַרְעָ֑א\rb*.
\q1 \rb There is|אִיתַי֙\rb* \rb no|וְלָ֤א\rb* \rb one who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb can restrain|יְמַחֵ֣א\rb* \rb His hand|בִידֵ֔הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb or say|וְיֵ֥אמַר\rb* \rb to Him|לֵ֖הּ\rb*, ‘\rb What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb have You done|עֲבַֽדְתְּ׃\rb*?’”
\p \v 36 \rb At|בֵּהּ־\rb* \rb the same time|זִמְנָ֞א\rb* \rb my sanity|מַנְדְּעִ֣י׀\rb* \rb was restored|יְת֣וּב\rb*\rb |עֲלַ֗י\rb*, \rb my honor|הַדְרִ֤י\rb* \rb and splendor|וְזִוִי֙\rb* \rb returned|יְת֣וּב\rb* \rb to me|עֲלַ֔י\rb* \rb for the glory|וְלִיקַ֨ר\rb* \rb of my kingdom|מַלְכוּתִ֜י\rb*. \rb My advisers|הַדָּֽבְרַ֥י\rb* \rb and nobles|וְרַבְרְבָנַ֖י\rb* \rb sought me out|יְבַע֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and I was restored|הָתְקְנַ֔ת\rb* \rb to|וְעַל־\rb* \rb my throne|מַלְכוּתִ֣י\rb*, \rb and surpassing|יַתִּירָ֖ה\rb* \rb greatness|וּרְב֥וּ\rb* \rb was added|ה֥וּסְפַת\rb* \rb to me|לִֽי׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb Now|כְּעַ֞ן\rb* \rb I|אֲנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֗ר\rb*, \rb praise|מְשַׁבַּ֨ח\rb* \rb and exalt|וּמְרוֹמֵ֤ם\rb* \rb and glorify|וּמְהַדַּר֙\rb* \rb the King|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb for|דִּ֤י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb His works|מַעֲבָד֙וֹהִי֙\rb* \rb are true|קְשֹׁ֔ט\rb* \rb and all His ways|וְאֹרְחָתֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb are just|דִּ֑ין\rb*. \rb And He is able|יָכִ֖ל\rb* \rb to humble|לְהַשְׁפָּלָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb those|וְדִי֙\rb* \rb who walk|מַהְלְכִ֣ין\rb* \rb in pride|בְּגֵוָ֔ה\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 Belshazzar’s Feast
\p \v 1 \rb Later,|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb*\f + \fr 5:1 \ft Aramaic does not include \fqa Later\ft . Some translators include \fqa Many years later \ft to account for the time elapsed, probably about 30 years, since the previous chapter.\f* \rb King Belshazzar|בֵּלְשַׁאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb held|עֲבַד֙\rb* \rb a great|רַ֔ב\rb* \rb feast|לְחֶ֣ם\rb* \rb for a thousand|אֲלַ֑ף\rb* \rb of his nobles|לְרַבְרְבָנ֖וֹהִי\rb*, \rb and he drank|שָׁתֵֽה׃\rb* \rb wine|חַמְרָ֥א\rb* \rb with|וְלָקֳבֵ֥ל\rb* \rb them|אַלְפָּ֖א\rb*. \v 2 \rb Under the influence of the wine|חַמְרָ֗א\rb*, \rb Belshazzar|בֵּלְשַׁאצַּ֞ר\rb* \rb gave orders|אֲמַ֣ר׀\rb*\rb |בִּטְעֵ֣ם\rb* \rb to bring|לְהַיְתָיָה֙\rb* \rb in the gold|דַּהֲבָ֣א\rb* \rb and silver|וְכַסְפָּ֔א\rb* \rb vessels|לְמָאנֵי֙\rb* \rb that|דִּ֤י\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb his father|אֲב֔וּהִי\rb*\f + \fr 5:2 \ft Or \fqa predecessor \ft or \fqa grandfather\ft ; also in verses 11, 13, and 18\f* \rb had taken|הַנְפֵּק֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכְלָ֖א\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that the king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb could drink|וְיִשְׁתּ֣וֹן\rb* \rb from them|בְּה֗וֹן\rb*, \rb along with his nobles|וְרַבְרְבָנ֔וֹהִי\rb*, \rb his wives|שֵׁגְלָתֵ֖הּ\rb*, \rb and his concubines|וּלְחֵנָתֵֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Thus|בֵּאדַ֗יִן\rb* \rb they brought in|הַיְתִיו֙\rb* \rb the gold|דַהֲבָ֔א\rb* \rb vessels|מָאנֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb had been taken|הַנְפִּ֗קוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵֽיכְלָ֛א\rb*,\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the house|בֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of God|אֱלָהָ֖א\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירֽוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and the king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb drank|וְאִשְׁתִּ֣יו\rb* \rb from them|בְּה֗וֹן\rb*, \rb along with his nobles|וְרַבְרְבָנ֔וֹהִי\rb*, \rb his wives|שֵׁגְלָתֵ֖הּ\rb*, \rb and his concubines|וּלְחֵנָתֵֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb As they drank|אִשְׁתִּ֖יו\rb* \rb the wine|חַמְרָ֑א\rb*, \rb they praised|וְ֠שַׁבַּחוּ\rb* \rb their gods|לֵֽאלָהֵ֞י\rb* \rb of gold|דַּהֲבָ֧א\rb* \rb and silver|וְכַסְפָּ֛א\rb*, \rb bronze|נְחָשָׁ֥א\rb* \rb and iron|פַרְזְלָ֖א\rb*, \rb wood|אָעָ֥א\rb* \rb and stone|וְאַבְנָֽא׃\rb*.
\s1 The Handwriting on the Wall
\p \v 5 \rb At|בַּהּ־\rb* \rb that moment|שַׁעֲתָ֗ה\rb* \rb the fingers|אֶצְבְּעָן֙\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb a human|אֱנָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb appeared|נְפַקוּ\rb* \rb and wrote|וְכָֽתְבָן֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the plaster|גִּירָ֕א\rb* \rb of|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the wall|כְתַ֥ל\rb*, \rb near|לָקֳבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb the lampstand|נֶבְרַשְׁתָּ֔א\rb* \rb in|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb the royal|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb palace|הֵיכְלָ֖א\rb*. \rb As the king|וּמַלְכָּ֣א\rb* \rb watched|חָזֵ֔ה\rb* \rb the hand|פַּ֥ס\rb*\rb |יְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|דִּ֥י\rb* \rb was writing|כָתְבָֽה׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb |אֱדַ֤יִן\rb*\rb |מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb his face|זִיוֺ֣הִי\rb* \rb grew pale|שְׁנ֔וֹהִי\rb* \rb and his thoughts|וְרַעיֹנֹ֖הִי\rb* \rb so alarmed him|יְבַהֲלוּנֵּ֑הּ\rb* \rb that his hips|חַרְצֵהּ֙\rb*\rb |וְקִטְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb gave way|מִשְׁתָּרַ֔יִן\rb* \rb and his knees|וְאַ֨רְכֻבָּתֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb knocked together|דָּ֥א\rb*\rb |לְדָ֖א\rb*\rb |נָֽקְשָֽׁן׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb The king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*\rb |בְּחַ֔יִל\rb* \rb called out for|קָרֵ֤א\rb* \rb the enchanters|לְאָ֣שְׁפַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb astrologers|כַּשְׂדָּיֵא\rb*,\f + \fr 5:7 \ft Or \fqa Chaldeans\ft ; also in verse 11\f* \rb and diviners|וְגָזְרַיָּ֑א\rb* \rb to be brought in|לְהֶֽעָלָה֙\rb*,\rb |עָנֵ֨ה\rb* \rb and he|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb* \rb said|וְאָמַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb to these wise men|לְחַכִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶ֗ל\rb*, “\rb Whoever|דִּ֣י\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb*\rb |אֱ֠נָשׁ\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb reads|יִקְרֵ֞ה\rb* \rb this|דְנָ֗ה\rb* \rb inscription|כְּתָבָ֣ה\rb* \rb and tells me|יְחַוִּנַּ֔נִי\rb* \rb its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵהּ֙\rb* \rb will be clothed|יִלְבַּ֗שׁ\rb* \rb in purple|אַרְגְּוָנָ֣א\rb* \rb and have a gold|דַהֲבָא֙\rb* \rb chain|וְהַמּוֹנְכָא\rb*\rb |דִֽי־\rb* \rb placed around|עַֽל־\rb* \rb his neck|צַוְּארֵ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and he will be made the third|וְתַלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb highest ruler|יִשְׁלַֽט׃ס\rb* \rb in the kingdom|בְמַלְכוּתָ֖א\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb So|אֱדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the king’s|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb wise men|חַכִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb came in|עָלֲלִין\rb*, \rb but they could|כָהֲלִ֤ין\rb* \rb not|וְלָֽא־\rb* \rb read|לְמִקְרֵ֔א\rb* \rb the inscription|כְּתָבָא֙\rb* \rb or interpret it|וּפִשְׁרָא\rb*\rb |לְהוֹדָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb for him|לְמַלְכָּֽא׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Then|אֱ֠דַיִן\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּ֤א\rb* \rb Belshazzar|בֵלְשַׁאצַּר֙\rb* \rb became even more|שַׂגִּ֣יא\rb* \rb terrified|מִתְבָּהַ֔ל\rb*, \rb his face|וְזִיוֺ֖הִי\rb* \rb grew even more pale|שָׁנַ֣יִן\rb*,\rb |עֲל֑וֹהִי\rb* \rb and his nobles|וְרַבְרְבָנ֖וֹהִי\rb* \rb were bewildered|מִֽשְׁתַּבְּשִֽׁין׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Hearing|לָקֳבֵ֨ל\rb* \rb the outcry|מִלֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb and his nobles|וְרַבְרְבָנ֔וֹהִי\rb*, \rb the queen|מַלְכְּתָ֕א\rb*\f + \fr 5:10 \ft Or \fqa queen mother\f* \rb entered|עַלֲלַת\rb* \rb the banquet|מִשְׁתְּיָ֖א\rb* \rb hall|לְבֵ֥ית\rb*. “\rb O king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*, \rb may you live|חֱיִ֔י\rb* \rb forever|לְעָלְמִ֣ין\rb*!”\rb |עֲנָ֨ת\rb* \rb she|מַלְכְּתָ֜א\rb* \rb said|וַאֲמֶ֗רֶת\rb*. “\rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb let your thoughts|רַעְיוֹנָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb terrify you|יְבַהֲלוּךְ֙\rb*, \rb or your face|וְזִיוָ֖יךְ\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb grow pale|יִשְׁתַּנּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb There is|אִיתַ֨י\rb* \rb a man|גְּבַ֜ר\rb* \rb in your kingdom|בְּמַלְכוּתָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb who|דִּ֠י\rb* \rb has the spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the holy|קַדִּישִׁין֮\rb* \rb gods|אֱלָהִ֣ין\rb* \rb in him|בֵּהּ֒\rb*. \rb In the days|וּבְיוֹמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your father|אֲב֗וּךְ\rb* \rb he was found|הִשְׁתְּכַ֣חַת\rb* \rb to have insight|נַהִיר֧וּ\rb*, \rb intelligence|וְשָׂכְלְתָנ֛וּ\rb*, \rb and wisdom|וְחָכְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb like that|כְּחָכְמַת־\rb* \rb of the gods|אֱלָהִ֖ין\rb*.
\p \rb Your father|אֲב֔וּךְ\rb*, \rb King|וּמַלְכָּ֤א\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻֽכַדְנֶצַּר֙\rb*, \rb appointed him|הֲקִימֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb chief|רַ֧ב\rb* \rb of the magicians|חַרְטֻמִּ֣ין\rb*, \rb enchanters|אָֽשְׁפִ֗ין\rb*, \rb astrologers|כַּשְׂדָּאִין֙\rb*, \rb and diviners|גָּזְרִ֔ין\rb*. \rb Your own father|אֲב֥וּךְ\rb*, \rb the king|מַלְכָּֽא׃\rb*, \v 12 \rb did this|כָּל־\rb* \rb because|קֳבֵ֡ל\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Daniel|בְּדָ֣נִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, \rb the one|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|מַלְכָּ֥א\rb* \rb named|שָׂם־\rb*\rb |שְׁמֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּ֑ר\rb*, \rb was found|הִשְׁתְּכַ֤חַת\rb* \rb to have an extraordinary|יַתִּירָ֡ה\rb* \rb spirit|ר֣וּחַ׀\rb*, \rb as well as knowledge|וּמַנְדַּ֡ע\rb*, \rb understanding|וְשָׂכְלְתָנ֡וּ\rb*, \rb and the ability to interpret|מְפַשַּׁ֣ר\rb* \rb dreams|חֶלְמִין֩\rb*, \rb explain|וַֽאַֽחֲוָיַ֨ת\rb* \rb riddles|אֲחִידָ֜ן\rb*, \rb and solve|וּמְשָׁרֵ֣א\rb* \rb difficult problems|קִטְרִ֗ין\rb*. \rb Summon|יִתְקְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֥אל\rb*, \rb therefore|כְּעַ֛ן\rb*, \rb and he will give you|יְהַֽחֲוֵֽה׃פ\rb* \rb the interpretation|וּפִשְׁרָ֥ה\rb*.”
\s1 Daniel Interprets the Handwriting
\p \v 13 \rb So|בֵּאדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּֽנִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb was brought|הֻעַ֖ל\rb* \rb before|קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*,\rb |עָנֵ֨ה\rb* \rb who|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb* \rb asked|וְאָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb him|לְדָנִיֵּ֗אל\rb*, “\rb Are you|אַנְתָּה\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּאל֙\rb*, \rb one|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb*\rb |יְה֔וּד\rb* \rb the exiles|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |גָלוּתָא֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb my father|אַ֖בִי\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֥א\rb* \rb brought|הַיְתִ֛י\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהֽוּד׃\rb*? \v 14 \rb I have heard|וְשִׁמְעֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |עֲלַיִךְ\rb* \rb that|דִּ֛י\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of the gods|אֱלָהִ֖ין\rb* \rb is in you|בָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and that you have insight|וְנַהִיר֧וּ\rb*, \rb intelligence|וְשָׂכְלְתָנ֛וּ\rb*, \rb and extraordinary|יַתִּירָ֖ה\rb* \rb wisdom|וְחָכְמָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now|וּכְעַ֞ן\rb* \rb the wise men|חַכִּֽימַיָּא֙\rb* \rb and enchanters|אָֽשְׁפַיָּ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb were brought|הֻעַ֣לּוּ\rb* \rb before me|קָֽדָמַ֗י\rb* \rb to read|יִקְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb this|דְנָה֙\rb* \rb inscription|כְתָבָ֤ה\rb* \rb and interpret it|וּפִשְׁרֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb for me|לְהוֹדָעֻתַ֑נִי\rb*, \rb but they could|כָהֲלִ֥ין\rb* \rb not|וְלָֽא־\rb* \rb give|לְהַחֲוָיָֽה׃\rb* \rb its|מִלְּתָ֖א\rb* \rb interpretation|פְּשַֽׁר־\rb*. \v 16 \rb But|וַאֲנָה֙\rb* \rb I have heard|שִׁמְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb about you|עֲלַיִךְ\rb*, \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb you are able|תוּכַל\rb* \rb to give interpretations|פִּשְׁרִ֛ין\rb*\rb |לְמִפְשַׁ֖ר\rb* \rb and solve|לְמִשְׁרֵ֑א\rb* \rb difficult problems|וְקִטְרִ֣ין\rb*. \rb Therefore|כְּעַ֡ן\rb*, \rb if|הֵן֩\rb* \rb you can|תּוּכַל\rb* \rb read|לְמִקְרֵ֗א\rb* \rb this inscription|כְּתָבָ֜א\rb* \rb and give me|לְהוֹדָ֣עֻתַ֔נִי\rb* \rb its interpretation|וּפִשְׁרֵהּ֙\rb*, \rb you will be clothed|תִלְבַּ֗שׁ\rb* \rb in purple|אַרְגְּוָנָ֣א\rb* \rb and have a gold|דַהֲבָא֙\rb* \rb chain|וְהַמּוֹנְכָא\rb* \rb placed around|עַֽל־\rb* \rb your neck|צַוְּארָ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb and you will be made the third|וְתַלְתָּ֥א\rb* \rb highest ruler|תִּשְׁלַֽט׃פ\rb* \rb in the kingdom|בְמַלְכוּתָ֖א\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb In response|בֵּאדַ֜יִן\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֗אל\rb* \rb said|וְאָמַר֙\rb*\rb |קֳדָ֣ם\rb*\rb |עָנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb to the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, “\rb You may keep|לֶֽהֶוְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb your gifts|מַתְּנָתָךְ֙\rb* \rb for yourself|לָ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and give|הַ֑ב\rb* \rb your rewards|וּנְבָ֥זְבְּיָתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to someone else|לְאָחֳרָ֣ן\rb*. \rb Nevertheless|בְּרַ֗ם\rb*, \rb I will read|אֶקְרֵ֣א\rb* \rb the inscription|כְּתָבָא֙\rb* \rb for the king|לְמַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb and interpret it|וּפִשְׁרָ֖א\rb* \rb for him|אֲהוֹדְעִנֵּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb As for you|אַנְתָּה\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*, \rb the Most High|עִלָּיָא\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָא֙\rb* \rb gave|יְהַ֖ב\rb* \rb your father|אֲבֽוּךְ׃\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|לִנְבֻכַדְנֶצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb sovereignty|מַלְכוּתָ֤א\rb* \rb and greatness|וּרְבוּתָא֙\rb*, \rb glory|וִיקָרָ֣א\rb* \rb and honor|וְהַדְרָ֔ה\rb*. \v 19 \rb Because of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the greatness|רְבוּתָא֙\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb He bestowed|יְהַב־\rb* \rb on him|לֵ֔הּ\rb*, \rb the people|עַֽמְמַיָּ֗א\rb* \rb of every|כֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb nation|אֻמַיָּא֙\rb* \rb and language|וְלִשָּׁ֣נַיָּ֔א\rb*\rb |הֲו֛וֹ\rb* \rb trembled|זָאֲעִין\rb* \rb in fear|וְדָחֲלִ֖ין\rb* \rb before|מִן־\rb* \rb him|קֳדָמ֑וֹהִי\rb*. \rb He|הֲוָ֣א\rb* \rb killed|קָטֵ֗ל\rb* \rb whom|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|הֲוָ֨ה\rb* \rb wished|צָבֵ֜א\rb* \rb and kept alive|מַחֵ֔א\rb* \rb whom|וְדִֽי־\rb* \rb he|הֲוָ֤ה\rb* \rb wished|צָבֵא֙\rb*;\rb |הֲוָ֣ה\rb* \rb he exalted|מָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb whom|וְדִֽי־\rb* \rb he|הֲוָ֤ה\rb* \rb wished|צָבֵא֙\rb*\rb |הֲוָ֣ה\rb* \rb and humbled|מַשְׁפִּֽיל׃\rb* \rb whom|וְדִֽי־\rb* \rb he|הֲוָ֥ה\rb* \rb wished|צָבֵ֖א\rb*.\rb |הֲוָ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb But when|וּכְדִי֙\rb* \rb his heart|לִבְבֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb became arrogant|רִ֣ם\rb* \rb and his spirit|וְרוּחֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb was hardened|תִּֽקְפַ֣ת\rb* \rb with pride|לַהֲזָדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he was deposed|הָנְחַת֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb his royal|מַלְכוּתֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb throne|כָּרְסֵ֣א\rb*, \rb and his glory|וִֽיקָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb was taken|הֶעְדִּ֥יוּ\rb* \rb from him|מִנֵּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb He was driven away|טְרִ֜יד\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb mankind|בְּנֵי֩\rb*\rb |אֲנָשָׁ֨א\rb*, \rb and his mind|וְלִבְבֵ֣הּ׀\rb* \rb was like|עִם־\rb* \rb that of a beast|חֵיוְתָ֣א\rb*.\rb |שְׁוִי\rb* \rb He lived|מְדוֹרֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb the wild donkeys|עֲרָֽדַיָּא֙\rb* \rb and ate|יְטַ֣עֲמוּנֵּ֔הּ\rb* \rb grass|עִשְׂבָּ֤א\rb* \rb like an ox|כְתוֹרִין֙\rb*, \rb and his body|גִּשְׁמֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb was drenched|יִצְטַבַּ֑ע\rb* \rb with the dew|וּמִטַּ֥ל\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֖א\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb he acknowledged|יְדַ֗ע\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Most High|עִלָּיָא\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָ֤א\rb* \rb rules|שַׁלִּ֞יט\rb* \rb over the kingdom|בְּמַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb of mankind|אֲנָשָׁ֔א\rb*, \rb setting|יְהָקֵ֥ים\rb* \rb over it|עֲלַיֵהּ׃\rb* \rb whom|וּלְמַן־\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb He wishes|יִצְבֵּ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb But you|וְאַנְתָּה\rb* \rb his son|בְּרֵהּ֙\rb*,\f + \fr 5:22 \ft Or \fqa descendant \ft or \fqa successor \ft or \fqa grandson\f* \rb O Belshazzar|בֵּלְשַׁאצַּ֔ר\rb*, \rb have not|לָ֥א\rb* \rb humbled|הַשְׁפֵּ֖לְתְּ\rb* \rb your heart|לִבְבָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb even though|קֳבֵ֕ל\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb* \rb you knew|יְדַֽעְתָּ׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|דְּנָ֖ה\rb*. \v 23 \rb Instead, you have exalted|הִתְרוֹמַ֡מְתָּ\rb* \rb yourself against|וְעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the Lord|מָרֵֽא־\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֣א׀\rb*. \rb The vessels|וּלְמָֽאנַיָּ֨א\rb* \rb from|דִֽי־\rb* \rb His house|בַיְתֵ֜הּ\rb* \rb were brought|הַיְתִ֣יו\rb* \rb to you|קָדָמַיִךְ\rb*, \rb and as you|וְאַנְתָּה\rb* \rb drank|שָׁתַ֣יִן\rb* \rb wine|חַמְרָא֮\rb* \rb from them|בְּהוֹן֒\rb* \rb with your nobles|וְרַבְרְבָנַיִךְ\rb*, \rb wives|שֵֽׁגְלָתָ֣ךְ\rb*, \rb and concubines|וּלְחֵנָתָךְ֮\rb*, \rb you praised|שַׁבַּ֑חְתָּ\rb* \rb your gods|וְלֵֽאלָהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of silver|כַסְפָּֽא־\rb* \rb and gold|וְ֠דַהֲבָא\rb*, \rb bronze|נְחָשָׁ֨א\rb* \rb and iron|פַרְזְלָ֜א\rb*, \rb wood|אָעָ֣א\rb* \rb and stone|וְאַבְנָ֗א\rb*, \rb which|דִּ֠י\rb* \rb cannot|לָֽא־\rb* \rb see|חָזַ֧יִן\rb* \rb or|וְלָא־\rb* \rb hear|שָׁמְעִ֛ין\rb* \rb or|וְלָ֥א\rb* \rb understand|יָדְעִ֖ין\rb*. \rb But you have failed to|לָ֥א\rb* \rb glorify|הַדַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb* \rb the God|וְלֵֽאלָהָ֞א\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb holds|לֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb in His hand|בִּידֵ֛הּ\rb* \rb your very breath|נִשְׁמְתָ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your ways|אֹרְחָתָ֥ךְ\rb*. \v 24 \rb Therefore|בֵּאדַ֙יִן֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |קֳדָמ֔וֹהִי\rb* \rb He sent|שְׁלִ֖יַחַ\rb*\rb |פַּסָּ֣א\rb*\rb |דִֽי־\rb* \rb the hand|יְדָ֑א\rb* \rb that wrote|רְשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb the|דְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb inscription|וּכְתָבָ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Now this|וּדְנָ֥ה\rb* \rb is the inscription|כְתָבָ֖א\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb was written|רְשִׁ֑ים\rb*:
\pc \rb MENE|מְנֵ֥א\rb*, \rb MENE|מְנֵ֖א\rb*, \rb TEKEL|תְּקֵ֥ל\rb*, \rb PARSIN|וּפַרְסִֽין׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb And this|דְּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb is the interpretation|פְּשַֽׁר־\rb* \rb of the message|מִלְּתָ֑א\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb MENE|מְנֵ֕א\rb*\f + \fr 5:26 \fqa Mene \ft sounds like the Aramaic for \fqa numbered\ft .\f* \rb means that God|אֱלָהָ֥א\rb* \rb has numbered|מְנָֽה־\rb* \rb the days of your reign|מַלְכוּתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb and brought it to an end|וְהַשְׁלְמַֽהּ׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 27 \rb TEKEL|תְּקֵ֑ל\rb*\f + \fr 5:27 \fqa Tekel \ft sounds like the Aramaic for \fqa weighed\ft .\f* \rb means that you have been weighed|תְּקִ֥ילְתָּה\rb* \rb on the scales|בְמֹֽאזַנְיָ֖א\rb* \rb and found|וְהִשְׁתְּכַ֥חַתְּ\rb* \rb deficient|חַסִּֽיר׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 28 \rb PERES|פְּרֵ֑ס\rb*\f + \fr 5:28 \fqa Peres \ft (the singular of \fqa Parsin\ft ) sounds like the Aramaic for \fqa divided \ft and for \fqa Persia\ft .\f* \rb means that your kingdom|מַלְכוּתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb has been divided|פְּרִיסַת֙\rb* \rb and given over|וִיהִיבַ֖ת\rb* \rb to the Medes|לְמָדַ֥י\rb* \rb and Persians|וּפָרָֽס׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֣יִן׀\rb* \rb Belshazzar|בֵּלְשַׁאצַּ֗ר\rb* \rb gave the command|אֲמַ֣ר\rb*, \rb and they clothed|וְהַלְבִּ֤ישׁוּ\rb* \rb Daniel|לְדָֽנִיֵּאל֙\rb* \rb in purple|אַרְגְּוָנָ֔א\rb*, \rb placed a gold|דַהֲבָ֖א\rb* \rb chain|וְהַמּוֹנְכָא\rb* \rb around|עַֽל־\rb* \rb his neck|צַוְּארֵ֑הּ\rb*, \rb and proclaimed|וְהַכְרִ֣זֽוּ\rb* \rb him|עֲל֔וֹהִי\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb*\rb |לֶהֱוֵ֥א\rb* \rb the third highest|תַּלְתָּ֖א\rb* \rb ruler|שַׁלִּ֛יט\rb* \rb in the kingdom|בְּמַלְכוּתָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb That|בֵּ֚הּ\rb* \rb very night|בְּלֵ֣ילְיָ֔א\rb* \rb Belshazzar|בֵּלְאשַׁצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb king|מַלְכָּ֥א\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַשְׂדָּיָא׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 5:30 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* \rb was slain|קְטִ֕יל\rb*, \v 31 \rb and Darius|וְדָרְיָ֙וֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb the Mede|מָֽדָיאָ֔\rb* \rb received|קַבֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכוּתָ֑א\rb* \rb at the age|כְּבַ֥ר\rb*\rb |שְׁנִ֖ין\rb* \rb of sixty-two|שִׁתִּ֥ין\rb*\rb |וְתַרְתֵּֽין׃\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 The Plot against Daniel
\p \v 1 \rb Now it|שְׁפַר֙\rb* \rb pleased|קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb Darius|דָּרְיָ֔וֶשׁ\rb* \rb to appoint|וַהֲקִים֙\rb* \rb 120|מְאָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֑ין\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb satraps|לַאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּ֖א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |מַלְכוּתָ֔א\rb* \rb to rule|לֶהֱוֺ֖ן\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכוּתָֽא׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb and over them|וְעֵ֤לָּא\rb*\rb |מִנְּהוֹן֙\rb* \rb three|תְּלָתָ֔א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb administrators|סָרְכִ֣ין\rb*, \rb including Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֖אל\rb*,\rb |חַֽד־\rb*\rb |מִנְּה֑וֹן\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb to whom|לְהוֹן֙\rb* \rb these|אִלֵּ֗ין\rb* \rb satraps|אֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּ֣א\rb*\rb |יָהֲבִ֤ין\rb* \rb were accountable|טַעְמָ֔א\rb* \rb so that the king|וּמַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb would|לֶהֱוֵ֥א\rb* \rb not|לָֽא־\rb* \rb suffer loss|נָזִֽק׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Soon|אֱדַ֙יִן֙\rb*, \rb by|קֳבֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb his extraordinary|יַתִּירָא֙\rb* \rb spirit|ר֤וּחַ\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֣אל\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הֲוָ֣א\rb* \rb distinguished himself|מִתְנַצַּ֔ח\rb* \rb among|עַל־\rb* \rb the administrators|סָרְכַיָּ֖א\rb* \rb and satraps|וַאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּ֑א\rb*. \rb So the king|וּמַלְכָּ֣א\rb* \rb planned|עֲשִׁ֔ית\rb* \rb to set him|לַהֲקָמוּתֵ֖הּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכוּתָֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Thus|אֱדַ֨יִן\rb* \rb the administrators|סָֽרְכַיָּ֜א\rb* \rb and satraps|וַאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּ֗א\rb* \rb sought|הֲו֨וֹ\rb*\rb |בָעַ֧יִן\rb*\rb |לְהַשְׁכָּחָ֥ה\rb* \rb a charge|עִלָּ֛ה\rb* \rb against Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֖אל\rb* \rb concerning|מִצַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכוּתָ֑א\rb*, \rb but they could|יָכְלִ֣ין\rb* \rb find|לְהַשְׁכָּחָ֗ה\rb* \rb no|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לָא־\rb* \rb charge|עִלָּ֨ה\rb* \rb or corruption|וּשְׁחִיתָ֜ה\rb*, \rb because|קֳבֵל֙\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb was trustworthy|מְהֵימַ֣ן\rb*, \rb and no|לָ֥א\rb* \rb negligence|שָׁלוּ֙\rb* \rb or corruption|וּשְׁחִיתָ֔ה\rb* \rb was found|הִשְׁתְּכַ֖חַת\rb* \rb in him|עֲלֽוֹהִי׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Finally|אֱ֠דַיִן\rb* \rb these|אִלֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֤א\rb* \rb said|אָֽמְרִ֔ין\rb*,\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* “\rb We will never|לָ֧א\rb* \rb find|נְהַשְׁכַּ֛ח\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb charge|עִלָּ֑א\rb* \rb against this|דְּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֥אל\rb* \rb unless|לָהֵ֕ן\rb* \rb we find something|הַשְׁכַּ֥חְנָֽה\rb* \rb against him|עֲל֖וֹהִי\rb* \rb concerning the law|בְּדָ֥ת\rb* \rb of his God|אֱלָהֵֽהּ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb So|אֱ֠דַיִן\rb* \rb the administrators|סָרְכַיָּ֤א\rb* \rb and satraps|וַאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּא֙\rb*\rb |אִלֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb went together|הַרְגִּ֖שׁוּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb*\rb |וְכֵן֙\rb* \rb and said|אָמְרִ֣ין\rb*, “\rb O King|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb* \rb Darius|דָּרְיָ֥וֶשׁ\rb*, \rb may you live|חֱיִֽי׃\rb* \rb forever|לְעָלְמִ֥ין\rb*! \v 7 \rb All|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the royal|מַלְכוּתָ֗א\rb* \rb administrators|סָרְכֵ֣י\rb*, \rb prefects|סִגְנַיָּ֤א\rb*, \rb satraps|וַֽאֲחַשְׁדַּרְפְּנַיָּא֙\rb*, \rb advisers|הַדָּֽבְרַיָּ֣א\rb*, \rb and governors|וּפַחֲוָתָ֔א\rb* \rb have agreed|אִתְיָעַ֜טוּ\rb* \rb that the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb should establish|לְקַיָּמָ֤ה\rb* \rb an ordinance|קְיָם֙\rb* \rb and enforce|וּלְתַקָּפָ֖ה\rb* \rb a decree|אֱסָ֑ר\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb for|עַד־\rb* \rb thirty|תְּלָתִ֗ין\rb* \rb days|יוֹמִ֣ין\rb* \rb anyone|כָל־\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb petitions|יִבְעֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |בָ֠עוּ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb god|אֱלָ֨הּ\rb* \rb or man|וֶֽאֱנָ֜שׁ\rb* \rb except you|לָהֵן֙\rb*,\rb |מִנָּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, \rb will be thrown|יִתְרְמֵ֕א\rb* \rb into the den|לְגֹ֖ב\rb* \rb of lions|אַרְיָוָתָֽא׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Therefore|כְּעַ֣ן\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, \rb establish|תְּקִ֥ים\rb* \rb the decree|אֱסָרָ֖א\rb* \rb and sign|וְתִרְשֻׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the document|כְּתָבָ֑א\rb* \rb so that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb it cannot|לָ֧א\rb* \rb be changed|לְהַשְׁנָיָ֛ה\rb* — \rb in accordance with the law|כְּדָת־\rb* \rb of the Medes|מָדַ֥י\rb* \rb and Persians|וּפָרַ֖ס\rb*, \rb which|דִּי־\rb* \rb cannot|לָ֥א\rb* \rb be repealed|תֶעְדֵּֽא׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Therefore|כָּל־\rb*\rb |קֳבֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֑ה\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּא֙\rb* \rb Darius|דָּֽרְיָ֔וֶשׁ\rb* \rb signed|רְשַׁ֥ם\rb* \rb the written|כְּתָבָ֖א\rb* \rb decree|וֶאֱסָרָֽא׃\rb*.
\s1 Daniel in the Lions’ Den
\p \v 10 \rb Now when|כְּדִ֨י\rb* \rb Daniel|וְ֠דָנִיֵּאל\rb* \rb learned|יְדַ֜ע\rb* \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the document|כְּתָבָא֙\rb* \rb had been signed|רְשִׁ֤ים\rb*, \rb he went|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb into his house|לְבַיְתֵ֔הּ\rb*, \rb where the windows|וְכַוִּ֨ין\rb* \rb of his|לֵהּ֙\rb* \rb upper room|בְּעִלִּיתֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb opened|פְּתִיחָ֥ן\rb* \rb toward|נֶ֖גֶד\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשְׁלֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and three|תְּלָתָ֨ה\rb* \rb times|וְזִמְנִין֩\rb* \rb a day|בְיוֹמָ֜א\rb* \rb he|ה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb got down|בָּרֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his knees|בִּרְכ֗וֹהִי\rb*, \rb prayed|וּמְצַלֵּ֤א\rb*, \rb and gave thanks|וּמוֹדֵא֙\rb* \rb to|קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb his God|אֱלָהֵ֔הּ\rb*,\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb just as|קֳבֵל֙\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb*\rb |הֲוָ֣א\rb* \rb he had done|עָבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb before|מִן־\rb*\rb |קַדְמַ֖ת\rb*\rb |דְּנָֽה׃ס\rb*. \v 11 \rb Then|אֱ֠דַיִן\rb* \rb these|אִלֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֤א\rb* \rb went as a group|הַרְגִּ֔שׁוּ\rb* \rb and found|וְהַשְׁכַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֑אל\rb* \rb petitioning|בָּעֵ֥א\rb* \rb and imploring|וּמִתְחַנַּ֖ן\rb*\rb |קֳדָ֥ם\rb* \rb his God|אֱלָהֵֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb So|בֵּ֠אדַיִן\rb* \rb they approached|קְרִ֨יבוּ\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּא֮\rb* \rb and asked|וְאָמְרִ֥ין\rb*\rb |קֳדָם־\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb his royal|מַלְכָּא֒\rb* \rb decree|אֱסָ֣ר\rb*: “\rb Did you not|הֲלָ֧א\rb* \rb sign|רְשַׁ֗מְתָּ\rb* \rb a decree|אֱסָ֣ר\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb for|עַד־\rb* \rb thirty|תְּלָתִ֗ין\rb* \rb days|יוֹמִ֣ין\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb man|אֱנָ֡שׁ\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb petitions|יִבְעֵה֩\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb god|אֱלָ֨הּ\rb* \rb or man|וֶֽאֱנָ֜שׁ\rb* \rb except you|לָהֵן֙\rb*,\rb |מִנָּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*, \rb will be thrown|יִתְרְמֵ֕א\rb* \rb into the den|לְג֖וֹב\rb* \rb of lions|אַרְיָותָ֑א\rb*?”
\p \rb The king|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֗ר\rb* \rb replied|עָנֵ֨ה\rb*, “\rb According to the law|כְּדָת־\rb* \rb of the Medes|מָדַ֥י\rb* \rb and Persians|וּפָרַ֖ס\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb the order|מִלְּתָ֛א\rb* \rb stands|יַצִּיבָ֧א\rb*, \rb and it cannot|לָ֥א\rb* \rb be repealed|תֶעְדֵּֽא׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Then|בֵּ֠אדַיִן\rb* \rb they told|עֲנ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאָמְרִין֮\rb*\rb |קֳדָ֣ם\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּא֒\rb*, “\rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֡אל\rb*, \rb one|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb*\rb |דִּי֩\rb* \rb the exiles|בְּנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |גָלוּתָ֜א\rb* \rb from|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Judah|יְה֗וּד\rb*, \rb shows no|לָא־\rb* \rb regard|שָׂ֨ם\rb* \rb for you|עֲלַיִךְ\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*, \rb or for|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the decree|אֱסָרָ֖א\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have signed|רְשַׁ֑מְתָּ\rb*. \rb He still makes|בָּעֵ֖א\rb* \rb his petition|בָּעוּתֵֽהּ׃\rb* \rb three|תְּלָתָה֙\rb* \rb times|וְזִמְנִ֤ין\rb* \rb a day|בְּיוֹמָ֔א\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb |אֱדַ֨יִן\rb* \rb As soon as|כְּדִ֧י\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb* \rb heard|שְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb this|מִלְּתָ֣א\rb*, \rb he was deeply|שַׂגִּיא֙\rb* \rb distressed|בְּאֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |עֲל֔וֹהִי\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֧ל\rb* \rb set|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb his mind|בָּ֖ל\rb* \rb on delivering|לְשֵׁיזָבוּתֵ֑הּ\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֛אל\rb*, \rb and he labored|מִשְׁתַּדַּ֖ר\rb* \rb until|וְעַד֙\rb* \rb sundown|מֶֽעָלֵ֣י\rb*\rb |שִׁמְשָׁ֔א\rb*\rb |הֲוָ֥א\rb* \rb to rescue him|לְהַצָּלוּתֵֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb the|אִלֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb approached|הַרְגִּ֖שׁוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the king together|מַלְכָּ֑א\rb* \rb and said|וְאָמְרִ֣ין\rb* \rb to him|לְמַלְכָּ֗א\rb*, “\rb Remember|דַּ֤ע\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*, \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb by the law|דָת֙\rb* \rb of the Medes|לְמָדַ֣י\rb* \rb and Persians|וּפָרַ֔ס\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb no|כָל־\rb* \rb decree|אֱסָ֥ר\rb* \rb or ordinance|וּקְיָ֛ם\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb established|יְהָקֵ֖ים\rb* \rb by the king|מַלְכָּ֥א\rb* \rb can be changed|לְהַשְׁנָיָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So|בֵּאדַ֜יִן\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֣א\rb* \rb gave the order|אֲמַ֗ר\rb*, \rb and they brought|וְהַיְתִיו֙\rb* \rb Daniel|לְדָ֣נִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb and threw him|וּרְמ֕וֹ\rb* \rb into the den|לְגֻבָּ֖א\rb* \rb of|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb lions|אַרְיָוָתָ֑א\rb*.
\p \rb The king|מַלְכָּא֙\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb said|עָנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb to Daniel|לְדָנִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, “\rb May your God|אֱלָהָ֗ךְ\rb*, \rb whom|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַנְתָּה\rb* \rb serve|פָּֽלַֽח־\rb* \rb continually|בִּתְדִירָ֔א\rb*,\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb deliver you|יְשֵׁיזְבִנָּֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 17 \rb A|חֲדָ֔ה\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb was brought|וְהֵיתָ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb and placed|וְשֻׂמַ֖ת\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the mouth|פֻּ֣ם\rb* \rb of the den|גֻּבָּ֑א\rb*, \rb and the king|מַלְכָּ֜א\rb* \rb sealed it|וְחַתְמַ֨הּ\rb* \rb with his own signet ring|בְּעִזְקְתֵ֗הּ\rb* \rb and with the rings|וּבְעִזְקָת֙\rb* \rb of his nobles|רַבְרְבָנ֔וֹהִי\rb*, \rb so that|דִּ֛י\rb* \rb nothing|לָא־\rb*\rb |צְב֖וּ\rb* \rb concerning Daniel|בְּדָנִיֵּֽאל׃\rb* \rb could be changed|תִשְׁנֵ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then|אֱ֠דַיִן\rb* \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֤א\rb* \rb went|אֲזַ֨ל\rb* \rb to his palace|לְהֵֽיכְלֵהּ֙\rb* \rb and spent the night|וּבָ֣ת\rb* \rb fasting|טְוָ֔ת\rb*. \rb No|לָא־\rb* \rb entertainment|וְדַחֲוָ֖ן\rb* \rb was brought|הַנְעֵ֣ל\rb* \rb before him|קָֽדָמ֑וֹהִי\rb*, \rb and sleep|וְשִׁנְתֵּ֖הּ\rb* \rb fled|נַדַּ֥ת\rb* \rb from him|עֲלֽוֹהִי׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb |בֵּאדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb At the first light|בְּנָגְהָ֑א\rb* \rb of dawn|בִּשְׁפַּרְפָּרָ֖א\rb*, \rb the king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb* \rb got up|יְק֣וּם\rb* \rb and hurried|וּבְהִ֨תְבְּהָלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲזַֽל׃\rb* \rb to the den|לְגֻבָּ֥א\rb* \rb of|דִֽי־\rb* \rb lions|אַרְיָוָתָ֖א\rb*. \v 20 \rb When he reached|וּכְמִקְרְבֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb the den|לְגֻבָּ֔א\rb*, \rb he cried out|זְעִ֑ק\rb*\rb |לְדָ֣נִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb in a voice|בְּקָ֥ל\rb* \rb of anguish|עֲצִ֖יב\rb*\rb |מַלְכָּ֜א\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָנֵ֨ה\rb*\rb |לְדָנִיֵּ֗אל\rb*, “\rb O Daniel|דָּֽנִיֵּאל֙\rb*, \rb servant|עֲבֵד֙\rb* \rb of the living|חַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָ֣א\rb*, \rb has your God|אֱלָהָ֗ךְ\rb*, \rb whom|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַנְתָּה\rb* \rb serve|פָּֽלַֽח־\rb* \rb continually|בִּתְדִירָ֔א\rb*, \rb been able|הַיְכִ֥ל\rb* \rb to deliver you|לְשֵׁיזָבוּתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the lions|אַרְיָוָתָֽא׃\rb*?”
\p \v 21 \rb Then|אֱדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֶּ֔אל\rb* \rb replied|מַלִּ֑ל\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb*\rb |מַלְכָּ֖א\rb*, “\rb O king|מַלְכָּ֖א\rb*, \rb may you live|חֱיִֽי׃\rb* \rb forever|לְעָלְמִ֥ין\rb*! \v 22 \rb My God|אֱלָהִ֞י\rb* \rb sent|שְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb His angel|מַלְאֲכֵ֗הּ\rb* \rb and shut|וּֽסֲגַ֛ר\rb* \rb the mouths|פֻּ֥ם\rb* \rb of the lions|אַרְיָוָתָ֖א\rb*. \rb They have not|וְלָ֣א\rb* \rb hurt me|חַבְּל֑וּנִי\rb*,\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb for|קֳבֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |דִּ֤י\rb* \rb I was found|הִשְׁתְּכַ֣חַת\rb* \rb innocent|זָכוּ֙\rb* \rb in His sight|קָֽדָמ֙וֹהִי֙\rb*, \rb and|וְאַ֤ף\rb* \rb I have done|עַבְדֵֽת׃\rb* \rb no|לָ֥א\rb* \rb wrong|חֲבוּלָ֖ה\rb* \rb against you|קָדָמַיִךְ\rb*, \rb O king|מַלְכָּ֔א\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb |בֵּאדַ֣יִן\rb* \rb The king|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb was overjoyed|שַׂגִּיא֙\rb*\rb |טְאֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |עֲל֔וֹהִי\rb* \rb and gave orders|אֲמַ֖ר\rb* \rb to lift|לְהַנְסָקָ֣ה\rb* \rb Daniel|וּלְדָ֣נִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the den|גֻּבָּ֑א\rb*, \rb and when Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֜אל\rb* \rb was lifted|וְהֻסַּ֨ק\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the den|גֻּבָּ֗א\rb*,\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb no|לָא־\rb* \rb wounds whatsoever|חֲבָל֙\rb* \rb were found|הִשְׁתְּכַ֣ח\rb* \rb on him|בֵּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb because|דִּ֖י\rb* \rb he had trusted|הֵימִ֥ן\rb* \rb in his God|בֵּאלָהֵֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb At the command|וַאֲמַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the king|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb*, \rb the|אִלֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb men|גֻּבְרַיָּ֤א\rb* \rb who|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb had falsely accused|אֲכַ֤לוּ\rb*\rb |קַרְצ֙וֹהִי֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb Daniel|דָֽנִיֵּ֔אל\rb* \rb were brought|וְהַיְתִ֞יו\rb* \rb and thrown|רְמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb into the den|וּלְגֹ֤ב\rb* \rb of lions|אַרְיָוָתָא֙\rb*— \rb they|אִנּ֖וּן\rb* \rb and their children|בְּנֵיה֣וֹן\rb* \rb and wives|וּנְשֵׁיה֑וֹן\rb*. \rb And before|וְלָֽא־\rb* \rb they had reached|מְט֞וֹ\rb* \rb the bottom|לְאַרְעִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the den|גֻּבָּ֗א\rb*,\rb |עַ֠ד\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the lions|אַרְיָ֣וָתָ֔א\rb* \rb overpowered|שְׁלִ֤טֽוּ\rb* \rb them|בְהוֹן֙\rb* \rb and crushed|הַדִּֽקוּ׃\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their bones|גַּרְמֵיה֖וֹן\rb*.
\s1 Darius Honors God
\p \v 25 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֜יִן\rb* \rb King|מַלְכָּ֗א\rb* \rb Darius|דָּרְיָ֣וֶשׁ\rb* \rb wrote|כְּ֠תַב\rb* \rb to the people|עַֽמְמַיָּ֞א\rb* \rb of every|לְֽכָל־\rb* \rb nation|אֻמַיָּ֧א\rb* \rb and language|וְלִשָּׁנַיָּ֛א\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb throughout|דָאֲרִין\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אַרְעָ֖א\rb*: “\rb May your prosperity|שְׁלָמְכ֥וֹן\rb* \rb abound|יִשְׂגֵּֽא׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb |קֳדָמַי֮\rb* \rb I hereby|שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb decree|טְעֵם֒\rb* \rb that|דִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb in every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb part|שָׁלְטָ֣ן\rb* \rb of my kingdom|מַלְכוּתִ֗י\rb*, \rb men are to tremble|זָאֲעִין\rb* \rb in fear|וְדָ֣חֲלִ֔ין\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb before|קֳדָ֖ם\rb* \rb the God|אֱלָהֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb of|דִּי־\rb* \rb Daniel|דָֽנִיֵּ֑אל\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb For|דִּי־\rb* \rb He|ה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb is the living|חַיָּ֗א\rb* \rb God|אֱלָהָ֣א\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He endures forever|וְקַיָּם֙\rb*\rb |לְעָ֣לְמִ֔ין\rb*;
\q1 \rb His kingdom|וּמַלְכוּתֵהּ֙\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb will never|לָ֣א\rb* \rb be destroyed|תִתְחַבַּ֔ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and His dominion|וְשָׁלְטָנֵ֖הּ\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb will never end|סוֹפָֽא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb He delivers|מְשֵׁיזִ֣ב\rb* \rb and rescues|וּמַצִּ֗ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb He performs|וְעָבֵד֙\rb* \rb signs|אָתִ֣ין\rb* \rb and wonders|וְתִמְהִ֔ין\rb*
\q2 \rb in the heavens|בִּשְׁמַיָּ֖א\rb* \rb and on the earth|וּבְאַרְעָ֑א\rb*,
\q1 \rb for He|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb has rescued|שֵׁיזִ֣יב\rb* \rb Daniel|לְדָֽנִיֵּ֔אל\rb*
\q2 \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the power|יַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the lions|אַרְיָוָתָֽא׃\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb So Daniel|וְדָנִיֵּ֣אל\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb prospered|הַצְלַ֖ח\rb* \rb during the reign|בְּמַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb of Darius|דָּרְיָ֑וֶשׁ\rb* \rb and the reign|וּבְמַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of Cyrus|כּ֥וֹרֶשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 6:28 \ft Or \fqa prospered during the reign of Darius, that is, the reign of Cyrus\f* \rb the Persian|פָּרְסָיָא׃פ\rb*.
\c 7
\s1 Daniel’s Vision of the Four Beasts
\r (\ref Revelation 13:1–10|REV 13:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the first|חֲדָ֗ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Belshazzar|לְבֵלְאשַׁצַּר֙\rb* \rb over Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּאל֙\rb* \rb had|חֲזָ֔ה\rb* \rb a dream|חֵ֣לֶם\rb*, \rb and visions|וְחֶזְוֵ֥י\rb* \rb passed through his mind|רֵאשֵׁ֖הּ\rb* \rb as he lay|עַֽל־\rb* \rb on his bed|מִשְׁכְּבֵ֑הּ\rb*.\rb |בֵּאדַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb He wrote down|כְתַ֔ב\rb* \rb the dream|חֶלְמָ֣א\rb*, \rb and this is the summary|רֵ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of his account|מִלִּ֖ין\rb*\rb |אֲמַֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּאל֙\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb declared|עָנֵ֤ה\rb*: “\rb In my vision|בְּחֶזְוִ֖י\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb the night|לֵֽילְיָ֑א\rb* \rb I|הֲוֵ֛ית\rb* \rb looked|חָזֵ֥ה\rb*, \rb and suddenly|וַאֲר֗וּ\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb winds|רוּחֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb were churning up|מְגִיחָ֖ן\rb* \rb the great|רַבָּֽא׃\rb* \rb sea|לְיַמָּ֥א\rb*.\f + \fr 7:2 \ft Perhaps \fqa the Great Sea\ft , that is, the Mediterranean Sea\f* \v 3 \rb Then four|וְאַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb great|רַבְרְבָ֔ן\rb* \rb beasts|חֵיוָן֙\rb* \rb came up|סָלְקָ֖ן\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the sea|יַמָּ֑א\rb*, \rb each one|דָּ֥א\rb* \rb different|שָׁנְיָ֖ן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the others|דָּֽא׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 4 \rb The first beast|קַדְמָיְתָ֣א\rb* \rb was like a lion|כְאַרְיֵ֔ה\rb*, \rb and it had|לַ֑הּ\rb* \rb the wings|וְגַפִּ֥ין\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb of an eagle|נְשַׁ֖ר\rb*. \rb I|הֲוֵ֡ית\rb* \rb watched|חָזֵ֣ה\rb* \rb until|עַד֩\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb its wings|גַפַּ֜יהּ\rb* \rb were torn off|מְּרִ֨יטוּ\rb* \rb and it was lifted up|וּנְטִ֣ילַת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|אַרְעָ֗א\rb* \rb and made to stand|הֳקִימַ֔ת\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb two feet|רַגְלַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb like a man|כֶּאֱנָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb and given|יְהִ֥יב\rb* \rb the mind|וּלְבַ֥ב\rb* \rb of a man|אֱנָ֖שׁ\rb*.
\li1 \v 5 \rb Suddenly|וַאֲר֣וּ\rb* \rb another|אָחֳרִ֨י\rb* \rb beast appeared|חֵיוָה֩\rb*, \rb which|תִנְיָנָ֜ה\rb* \rb looked like|דָּמְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb a bear|לְדֹ֗ב\rb*. \rb It was raised up|הֳקִמַ֔ת\rb* \rb on one|חַד֙\rb* \rb of its sides|וְלִשְׂטַר־\rb*, \rb and it had three|וּתְלָ֥ת\rb* \rb ribs|עִלְעִ֛ין\rb* \rb in its mouth|בְּפֻמַּ֖הּ\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb its teeth|שִׁנַּיַּהּ\rb*. \rb So|וְכֵן֙\rb* \rb it was told|אָמְרִ֣ין\rb*, ‘\rb Get up|ק֥וּמִֽי\rb* \rb and gorge yourself|אֲכֻ֖לִי\rb* \rb on flesh|בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |שַׂגִּֽיא׃\rb*!’
\li1 \v 6 \rb Next|בָּאתַ֨ר\rb*\rb |דְּנָ֜ה\rb*, \rb as I|הֲוֵ֗ית\rb* \rb watched|חָזֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb suddenly|וַאֲר֤וּ\rb* \rb another beast appeared|אָֽחֳרִי֙\rb*. \rb It was like a leopard|כִּנְמַ֔ר\rb*, \rb and on|עַל־\rb* \rb its back|גַּבַּיַּהּ\rb* \rb it had|וְלַ֨הּ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֛ע\rb* \rb wings|גַּפִּ֥ין\rb* \rb like those of|דִּי־\rb* \rb a bird|ע֖וֹף\rb*. \rb The beast also|לְחֵ֣יוְתָ֔א\rb* \rb had four|וְאַרְבְּעָ֤ה\rb* \rb heads|רֵאשִׁין֙\rb*, \rb and it was given|יְהִ֥יב\rb* \rb authority to rule|וְשָׁלְטָ֖ן\rb*.
\li1 \v 7 \rb After|בָּאתַ֣ר\rb* \rb this|דְּנָה֩\rb*, \rb as I|הֲוֵ֜ית\rb* \rb watched|חָזֵ֨ה\rb* \rb in my vision|בְּחֶזְוֵ֣י\rb* \rb in the night|לֵֽילְיָ֗א\rb*, \rb suddenly|וַאֲר֣וּ\rb* \rb a fourth|רְבִיעָיָה\rb* \rb beast appeared|חֵיוָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and it was terrifying|דְּחִילָה֩\rb* — \rb dreadful|וְאֵֽימְתָנִ֨י\rb* \rb and extremely|יַתִּ֗ירָא\rb* \rb strong|וְתַקִּיפָ֜א\rb* — \rb with|לַהּ֙\rb* \rb large|רַבְרְבָ֔ן\rb* \rb iron|פַרְזֶ֥ל\rb* \rb teeth|וְשִׁנַּ֨יִן\rb*.\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb It devoured|אָֽכְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and crushed|וּמַדֱּקָ֔ה\rb*; \rb then it trampled|רָפְסָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְהִ֣יא\rb* \rb underfoot|בְּרַגְלַיַּהּ\rb* \rb whatever was left|וּשְׁאָרָ֖א\rb*. \rb It was different|מְשַׁנְּיָ֗ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the beasts|חֵֽיוָתָא֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb before it|קָֽדָמַ֔יהּ\rb*, \rb and it had ten|עֲשַׂ֖ר\rb* \rb horns|וְקַרְנַ֥יִן\rb*. \v 8 \rb While I was|הֲוֵ֜ית\rb* \rb contemplating|מִשְׂתַּכַּ֨ל\rb* \rb the horns|בְּקַרְנַיָּ֗א\rb*,\rb |וַ֠אֲלוּ\rb* \rb suddenly another|אָחֳרִ֤י\rb* \rb horn|קֶ֣רֶן\rb*, \rb a little one|זְעֵירָה֙\rb*, \rb came up|סִלְקָ֣ת\rb* \rb among them|בֵּינֵיהוֹן\rb*, \rb and three|וּתְלָ֗ת\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the first|קַדְמָ֣יָתָ֔א\rb* \rb horns|קַרְנַיָּא֙\rb* \rb were uprooted|אֶתְעֲקַרוּ\rb* \rb before|מִן־\rb* \rb it|קֳדָמַיַּהּ\rb*.\rb |וַאֲל֨וּ\rb* \rb This|דָ֔א\rb* \rb horn|בְּקַרְנָא־\rb* \rb had eyes|עַיְנִ֜ין\rb* \rb like those|כְּעַיְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of a man|אֲנָשָׁא֙\rb* \rb and a mouth|וּפֻ֖ם\rb* \rb that spoke|מְמַלִּ֥ל\rb* \rb words of arrogance|רַבְרְבָֽן׃\rb*.
\s1 Daniel’s Vision of the Ancient of Days
\p \v 9 \rb As|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |דִּ֤י\rb* \rb I continued|הֲוֵ֗ית\rb* \rb to watch|חָזֵ֣ה\rb*,
\b 
\q1 \rb thrones|כָרְסָוָן֙\rb* \rb were set in place|רְמִ֔יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the Ancient|וְעַתִּ֥יק\rb* \rb of Days|יוֹמִ֖ין\rb* \rb took His seat|יְתִ֑ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb His clothing|לְבוּשֵׁ֣הּ׀\rb* \rb was white|חִוָּ֗ר\rb* \rb as snow|כִּתְלַ֣ג\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the hair|וּשְׂעַ֤ר\rb* \rb of His head|רֵאשֵׁהּ֙\rb* \rb was like pure|נְקֵ֔א\rb* \rb wool|כַּעֲמַ֣ר\rb*.
\q1 \rb His throne|כָּרְסְיֵהּ֙\rb* \rb was flaming|שְׁבִיבִ֣ין\rb*\rb |דִּי־\rb* \rb with fire|נ֔וּר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and its wheels|גַּלְגִּלּ֖וֹהִי\rb* \rb were all ablaze|דָּלִֽק׃\rb*\rb |נ֥וּר\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb A river|נְהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of|דִּי־\rb* \rb fire|נ֗וּר\rb* \rb was flowing|נָגֵ֤ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb coming out|וְנָפֵק֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb His presence|קֳדָמ֔וֹהִי\rb*.
\q1 \rb Thousands|אֶ֤לֶף\rb* \rb upon thousands|אַלְפִים\rb* \rb attended Him|יְשַׁמְּשׁוּנֵּ֔הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and myriads|וְרִבּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb upon myriads|רִבְּוָן\rb* \rb stood|יְקוּמ֑וּן\rb* \rb before Him|קָֽדָמ֣וֹהִי\rb*.
\q1 \rb The court|דִּינָ֥א\rb* \rb was convened|יְתִ֖ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the books|וְסִפְרִ֥ין\rb* \rb were opened|פְּתִֽיחוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then|בֵּאדַ֗יִן\rb* \rb I kept|הֲוֵ֔ית\rb* \rb watching|חָזֵ֣ה\rb* \rb because of|מִן־\rb*\rb |קָל֙\rb* \rb the arrogant|רַבְרְבָתָ֔א\rb* \rb words|מִלַּיָּ֣א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb the horn|קַרְנָ֖א\rb* \rb was speaking|מְמַלֱּלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb As|עַד֩\rb*\rb |דִּ֨י\rb* \rb I continued to watch|חָזֵ֣ה\rb*,\rb |הֲוֵ֡ית\rb* \rb the beast|חֵֽיוְתָא֙\rb* \rb was slain|קְטִילַ֤ת\rb*, \rb and its body|גִּשְׁמַ֔הּ\rb* \rb was destroyed|וְהוּבַ֣ד\rb* \rb and thrown into|וִיהִיבַ֖ת\rb* \rb the blazing|לִיקֵדַ֥ת\rb* \rb fire|אֶשָּֽׁא׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb As for the rest|וּשְׁאָר֙\rb* \rb of the beasts|חֵֽיוָתָ֔א\rb*, \rb their dominion|שָׁלְטָנְה֑וֹן\rb* \rb was removed|הֶעְדִּ֖יו\rb*, \rb but they were granted|יְהִ֥יבַת\rb*\rb |לְה֖וֹן\rb* \rb an extension|וְאַרְכָ֧ה\rb* \rb of life|בְחַיִּ֛ין\rb* \rb for|עַד־\rb* \rb a season|זְמַ֥ן\rb* \rb and a time|וְעִדָּֽן׃\rb*.
\s1 Daniel’s Vision of the Son of Man
\p \v 13 \rb In my vision|בְּחֶזְוֵ֣י\rb* \rb in the night|לֵֽילְיָ֔א\rb* \rb I continued|הֲוֵית֙\rb* \rb to watch|חָזֵ֤ה\rb*,
\b 
\q1 \rb and I saw|וַאֲרוּ֙\rb* \rb One like the Son|כְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Man|אֱנָ֖שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 7:13 \ft Or \fqa one like a son of man\f*
\q2 \rb coming|אָתֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |הֲוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the clouds|עֲנָנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb*.\f + \fr 7:13 \ft See \ref Matthew 24:30|MAT 24:30\ref*, Matthew 26:64, Mark 13:26, Mark 14:62, Luke 21:27, Revelation 1:13, and Revelation 14:14.\f*
\q1 \rb He approached|מְטָ֔ה\rb* \rb the Ancient|עַתִּ֤יק\rb* \rb of Days|יֽוֹמַיָּא֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and was led|הַקְרְבֽוּהִי׃\rb* \rb into His presence|וּקְדָמ֖וֹהִי\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb And|וְלֵ֨הּ\rb* \rb He was given|יְהִ֤יב\rb* \rb dominion|שָׁלְטָן֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb glory|וִיקָ֣ר\rb*, \rb and kingship|וּמַלְכ֔וּ\rb*,
\q1 \rb that the people|עַֽמְמַיָּ֗א\rb* \rb of every|וְכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb nation|אֻמַיָּ֛א\rb* \rb and language|וְלִשָּׁנַיָּ֖א\rb*
\q2 \rb should serve|יִפְלְח֑וּן\rb* \rb Him|לֵ֣הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb His dominion|שָׁלְטָנֵ֞הּ\rb* \rb is an everlasting|עָלַם֙\rb* \rb dominion|שָׁלְטָ֤ן\rb*
\q2 \rb that|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb will not|לָ֣א\rb* \rb pass away|יֶעְדֵּ֔ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb and His kingdom is one|וּמַלְכוּתֵ֖הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb that|דִּי־\rb* \rb will never|לָ֥א\rb* \rb be destroyed|תִתְחַבַּֽל׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Daniel’s Visions Interpreted
\p \v 15 \rb I|אֲנָ֥ה\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֖אל\rb*, \rb was grieved|אֶתְכְּרִיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb in|בְּג֣וֹא\rb* \rb my spirit|רוּחִ֛י\rb*\rb |נִדְנֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the visions|וְחֶזְוֵ֥י\rb* \rb in my mind|רֵאשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb alarmed me|יְבַהֲלֻנַּֽנִי׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb I approached|קִרְבֵ֗ת\rb* \rb one|חַד֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb those who were standing there|קָ֣אֲמַיָּ֔א\rb*, \rb and I asked|אֶבְעֵֽא־\rb* \rb him|מִנֵּ֖הּ\rb* \rb the true meaning|וְיַצִּיבָ֥א\rb* \rb of|עַֽל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|דְּנָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb So he told|וַאֲמַר־\rb* \rb me|לִ֕י\rb*\rb |יְהוֹדְעִנַּֽנִי׃\rb* \rb the interpretation|וּפְשַׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of these things|מִלַּיָּ֖א\rb*: \v 17 ‘\rb These|אִלֵּין֙\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֑ע\rb* \rb great|רַבְרְבָתָ֔א\rb* \rb beasts|חֵיוָתָ֣א\rb*\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb are|אִנִּ֖ין\rb* \rb four|אַרְבְּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכִ֖ין\rb* \rb who will arise|יְקוּמ֥וּן\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the earth|אַרְעָֽא׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But the saints|קַדִּישֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of the Most High|עֶלְיוֹנִ֑ין\rb* \rb will receive|וִֽיקַבְּלוּן֙\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכוּתָ֔א\rb* \rb and possess|וְיַחְסְנ֤וּן\rb* \rb it|מַלְכוּתָא֙\rb* \rb forever|עַֽד־\rb*\rb |עָ֣לְמָ֔א\rb* — \rb yes, forever|וְעַ֖ד\rb*\rb |עָלַ֥ם\rb* \rb and ever|עָלְמַיָּֽא׃\rb*.’
\p \v 19 \rb Then|אֱדַ֗יִן\rb* \rb I wanted|צְבִית֙\rb* \rb to know the true meaning|לְיַצָּבָ֔א\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb the fourth|רְבִיעָ֣יְתָ֔א\rb* \rb beast|חֵֽיוְתָא֙\rb*, \rb which|דִּֽי־\rb* \rb was|הֲוָ֥ת\rb* \rb different|שָֽׁנְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb all the others|כָּלְּהוֹן\rb* — \rb extremely|יַתִּ֗ירָה\rb* \rb terrifying|דְּחִילָ֣ה\rb* — \rb devouring|אָֽכְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and crushing|מַדֲּקָ֔ה\rb* \rb with iron|פַרְזֶל֙\rb* \rb teeth|שִׁנַּיַּהּ\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb and bronze|נְחָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb claws|וְטִפְרַ֣יהּ\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb*, \rb then trampling|רָֽפְסָֽה׃\rb* \rb underfoot|בְּרַגְלַ֥יהּ\rb* \rb whatever was left|וּשְׁאָרָ֖א\rb*. \v 20 \rb I also wanted to know about|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the ten|עֲשַׂר֙\rb* \rb horns|קַרְנַיָּ֤א\rb* \rb on its head|בְרֵאשַׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb and the other|וְאָחֳרִי֙\rb*\rb |דִּ֣י\rb* \rb horn that|דִּ֣י\rb* \rb came up|סִלְקַ֔ת\rb*, \rb before which|קֳדָמַיַּהּ\rb* \rb three of them|תְּלָ֑ת\rb* \rb fell|וּנְפַלוּ\rb*— \rb the horn|וְקַרְנָ֨א\rb* \rb whose appearance was|וְחֶזְוַ֖הּ\rb* \rb more imposing than|מִן־\rb* \rb the others|חַבְרָתַֽהּ׃\rb*,\rb |דִכֵּ֜ן\rb* \rb with eyes|וְעַיְנִ֣ין\rb* \rb and with|לַ֗הּ\rb* \rb a mouth|וְפֻם֙\rb* \rb that spoke|מְמַלִּ֣ל\rb* \rb words of arrogance|רַבְרְבָ֔ן\rb*\rb |רַ֥ב\rb*. \v 21 \rb As I|הֲוֵ֔ית\rb* \rb watched|חָזֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb this|דִכֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb horn|וְקַרְנָ֣א\rb* \rb was waging|עָבְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb war|קְרָ֖ב\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the saints|קַדִּישִׁ֑ין\rb* \rb and prevailing|וְיָכְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb against them|לְהֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 22 \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |דִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Ancient|עַתִּיק֙\rb* \rb of Days|יֽוֹמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb arrived|אֲתָ֗ה\rb* \rb and pronounced|יְהִ֔ב\rb* \rb judgment|וְדִינָ֣א\rb* \rb in favor of the saints|לְקַדִּישֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb of the Most High|עֶלְיוֹנִ֑ין\rb*, \rb and the time|וְזִמְנָ֣א\rb* \rb came|מְטָ֔ה\rb* \rb for them|קַדִּישִֽׁין׃\rb* \rb to possess|הֶחֱסִ֥נוּ\rb* \rb the kingdom|וּמַלְכוּתָ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb This is what|כֵּן֮\rb* \rb he said|אֲמַר֒\rb*: ‘\rb The fourth|רְבִיעָ֣יְתָ֔א\rb* \rb beast is|חֵֽיוְתָא֙\rb* \rb a fourth|רְבִיעָיָא\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb that will appear|תֶּהֱוֵ֣א\rb* \rb on the earth|בְאַרְעָ֔א\rb*,\rb |דִּ֥י\rb* \rb different|תִשְׁנֵ֖א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the other kingdoms|מַלְכְוָתָ֑א\rb*, \rb and it will devour|וְתֵאכֻל֙\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb earth|אַרְעָ֔א\rb*, \rb trample it down|וּתְדוּשִׁנַּ֖הּ\rb*, \rb and crush it|וְתַדְּקִנַּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb And the ten|עֲשַׂ֔ר\rb* \rb horns|וְקַרְנַיָּ֣א\rb* \rb are ten|עַשְׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכִ֖ין\rb* \rb who will rise|יְקֻמ֑וּן\rb* \rb from|מִנַּהּ֙\rb* \rb this kingdom|מַלְכוּתָ֔ה\rb*. \rb After them|אַחֲרֵיה֗וֹן\rb* \rb another king|וְאָחֳרָ֞ן\rb*, \rb different|יִשְׁנֵא֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the earlier ones|קַדְמָיֵ֔א\rb*, \rb will rise|יְק֣וּם\rb*\rb |וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb and subdue|יְהַשְׁפִּֽל׃\rb* \rb three|וּתְלָתָ֥ה\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכִ֖ין\rb*. \v 25 \rb He will speak out|יְמַלִּ֔ל\rb*\rb |וּמִלִּ֗ין\rb* \rb against|לְצַ֤ד\rb* \rb the Most High|עִלָּיָא\rb* \rb and oppress|יְבַלֵּ֑א\rb* \rb the saints|וּלְקַדִּישֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the Most High|עֶלְיוֹנִ֖ין\rb*, \rb intending|וְיִסְבַּ֗ר\rb* \rb to change|לְהַשְׁנָיָה֙\rb* \rb the appointed times|זִמְנִ֣ין\rb* \rb and laws|וְדָ֔ת\rb*; \rb and the saints will be given|וְיִתְיַהֲב֣וּן\rb* \rb into his hand|בִּידֵ֔הּ\rb* \rb for|עַד־\rb* \rb a time|עִדָּ֥ן\rb*, \rb and times|וְעִדָּנִ֖ין\rb*, \rb and half|וּפְלַ֥ג\rb* \rb a time|עִדָּֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb But the court|וְדִינָ֖א\rb* \rb will convene|יִתִּ֑ב\rb*, \rb and his dominion|וְשָׁלְטָנֵ֣הּ\rb* \rb will be taken away|יְהַעְדּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and completely destroyed|לְהַשְׁמָדָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּלְהוֹבָדָ֖ה\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |סוֹפָֽא׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb Then the sovereignty|וּמַלְכוּתָ֨ה\rb*, \rb dominion|וְשָׁלְטָנָ֜א\rb*, \rb and greatness|וּרְבוּתָ֗א\rb* \rb of|דִּ֚י\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַלְכְוָת֙\rb* \rb under|תְּח֣וֹת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb of heaven|שְׁמַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb will be given|יְהִיבַ֕ת\rb* \rb to the people|לְעַ֖ם\rb*, \rb the saints|קַדִּישֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the Most High|עֶלְיוֹנִ֑ין\rb*. \rb His kingdom|מַלְכוּתֵהּ֙\rb* \rb will be an everlasting|עָלַ֔ם\rb* \rb kingdom|מַלְכ֣וּת\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb rulers|שָׁלְטָ֣נַיָּ֔א\rb* \rb will serve|יִפְלְח֖וּן\rb* \rb and obey|וְיִֽשְׁתַּמְּעֽוּן׃\rb* \rb Him|לֵ֥הּ\rb*.’
\p \v 28 \rb |עַד־\rb* \rb Thus|כָּ֖ה\rb* \rb ends|סוֹפָ֣א\rb* \rb the matter|מִלְּתָ֑א\rb*. \rb As for me|אֲנָ֨ה\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָֽנִיֵּ֜אל\rb*, \rb my thoughts|רַעְיוֹנַ֣י\rb* \rb troubled me|יְבַהֲלֻנַּ֗נִי\rb* \rb greatly|שַׂגִּ֣יא׀\rb*, \rb and my face|וְזִיוַי֙\rb* \rb turned pale|יִשְׁתַּנּ֣וֹן\rb*.\rb |עֲלַ֔י\rb* \rb But I kept|נִטְרֵֽת׃פ\rb* \rb the matter|וּמִלְּתָ֖א\rb* \rb to myself|בְּלִבִּ֥י\rb*.”
\c 8
\s1 Daniel’s Vision of the Ram and the Goat
\p \v 1 \rb In the third|שָׁל֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the reign|לְמַלְכ֖וּת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb Belshazzar|בֵּלְאשַׁצַּ֣ר\rb*, \rb a vision|חָז֞וֹן\rb* \rb appeared|נִרְאָ֤ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb*,\rb |אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, \rb subsequent|אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb to the one that had appeared|הַנִּרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb earlier|בַּתְּחִלָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And in the vision|בֶּחָזוֹן֒\rb* \rb I saw|וָֽאֶרְאֶה֮\rb* \rb myself|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb in the citadel|הַבִּירָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb of Susa|בְּשׁוּשַׁ֣ן\rb*, \rb in the province|הַמְּדִינָ֑ה\rb* \rb of Elam|בְּעֵילָ֣ם\rb*. \rb I saw|וָאֶרְאֶה֙\rb* \rb in the vision|בֶּֽחָז֔וֹן\rb* \rb that I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb was|הָיִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the Ulai|אוּלָֽי׃\rb* \rb Canal|אוּבַ֥ל\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then I lifted up|וָאֶשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb* \rb and saw|וָאֶרְאֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb a ram|אַ֣יִל\rb* \rb with|וְל֣וֹ\rb* \rb two horns|קְרָנָ֑יִם\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֛ד\rb* \rb beside|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the canal|הָאֻבָ֖ל\rb*. \rb The horns|וְהַקְּרָנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb were long|גְּבֹה֗וֹת\rb*, \rb but one|וְהָאַחַת֙\rb* \rb was longer|גְּבֹהָ֣ה\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֔ית\rb*, \rb and the longer|וְהַ֨גְּבֹהָ֔ה\rb* \rb one grew up|עֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb later|בָּאַחֲרֹנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb I saw|רָאִ֣יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ram|הָאַ֡יִל\rb* \rb charging|מְנַגֵּחַ֩\rb* \rb toward the west|יָ֨מָּה\rb* \rb and the north|וְצָפ֜וֹנָה\rb* \rb and the south|וָנֶ֗גְבָּה\rb*. \rb No|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb animal|חַיּוֹת֙\rb* \rb could stand|יַֽעַמְד֣וּ\rb* \rb against him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and there was no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb deliverance|מַצִּ֖יל\rb* \rb from his power|מִיָּד֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He did|וְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb as he pleased|כִרְצֹנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and became great|וְהִגְדִּֽיל׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb As I|וַאֲנִ֣י׀\rb* \rb was|הָיִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb contemplating all this|מֵבִ֗ין\rb*, \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a goat|צְפִיר־\rb*\rb |וְהַ֨צָּפִ֔יר\rb* \rb with a prominent|חָז֖וּת\rb* \rb horn|קֶ֥רֶן\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָֽיו׃\rb*\rb |הָֽעִזִּים֙\rb* \rb came|בָּ֤א\rb* \rb out of|מִן־\rb* \rb the west|הַֽמַּעֲרָב֙\rb*, \rb crossing|עַל־\rb* \rb the surface|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the entire|כָל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb without|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb touching|נוֹגֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb the ground|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \v 6 \rb He came|וַיָּבֹ֗א\rb* \rb toward|עַד־\rb* \rb the two-horned|הַקְּרָנַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb ram|הָאַ֙יִל֙\rb*\rb |בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֔יתִי\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb beside|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the canal|הָאֻבָ֑ל\rb* \rb and rushed|וַיָּ֥רָץ\rb* \rb at him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb with furious|בַּחֲמַ֥ת\rb* \rb power|כֹּחֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb I saw him|וּרְאִיתִ֞יו\rb* \rb approach|מַגִּ֣יעַ׀\rb*\rb |אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb the ram|הָאַ֗יִל\rb* \rb in a rage|וַיִּתְמַרְמַ֤ר\rb* \rb against him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb and he struck|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ram|הָאַ֔יִל\rb* \rb and shattered|וַיְשַׁבֵּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb horns|קְרָנָ֔יו\rb*. \rb The ram|בָּאַ֖יִל\rb* \rb was|הָ֥יָה\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb powerless|כֹ֛חַ\rb* \rb to stand|לַעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb against him|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and the goat threw him|וַיַּשְׁלִיכֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֙רְצָה֙\rb* \rb and trampled him|וַֽיִּרְמְסֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb no one|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb could deliver|מַצִּ֛יל\rb* \rb the ram|לָאַ֖יִל\rb* \rb from his power|מִיָּדֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Thus the goat|וּצְפִ֥יר\rb*\rb |הָעִזִּ֖ים\rb* \rb became|עַד־\rb* \rb very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb great|הִגְדִּ֣יל\rb*, \rb but at the height of his power|וּכְעָצְמ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb his large|הַגְּדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb horn|הַקֶּ֣רֶן\rb* \rb was broken off|נִשְׁבְּרָה֙\rb*, \rb and four|אַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb prominent|חָז֤וּת\rb* \rb horns came up|וַֽתַּעֲלֶ֜נָה\rb* \rb in its place|תַּחְתֶּ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb pointing toward the four|לְאַרְבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb winds|רוּח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb From|וּמִן־\rb* \rb one|הָאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of these horns|מֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb a|אַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb little|מִצְּעִירָ֑ה\rb* \rb horn|קֶֽרֶן־\rb* \rb emerged|יָצָ֥א\rb* \rb and grew|וַתִּגְדַּל־\rb* \rb extensively|יֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the south|הַנֶּ֥גֶב\rb* \rb and the east|הַמִּזְרָ֖ח\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and toward|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the Beautiful Land|הַצֶּֽבִי׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb It grew as high|וַתִּגְדַּ֖ל\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and it cast down|וַתַּפֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb some of|מִן־\rb* \rb the host|הַצָּבָ֥א\rb* \rb and some|וּמִן־\rb* \rb of the stars|הַכּוֹכָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb to the earth|אַ֛רְצָה\rb* \rb and trampled them|וַֽתִּרְמְסֵֽם׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb It magnified itself|הִגְדִּ֑יל\rb*,\rb |וּמִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb even to|וְעַ֥ד\rb* \rb the Prince|שַֽׂר־\rb* \rb of the host|הַצָּבָ֖א\rb*; \rb it removed|הֵרִים\rb* \rb His daily sacrifice|הַתָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb and overthrew|וְהֻשְׁלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb the place|מְכ֥וֹן\rb* \rb of His sanctuary|מִקְדָּשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And in the rebellion|בְּפָ֑שַׁע\rb*,\f + \fr 8:12 \ft Or \fqa on account of transgression\f* \rb the host|וְצָבָ֛א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and the daily sacrifice|הַתָּמִ֖יד\rb* \rb were given over to the horn|תִּנָּתֵ֥ן\rb*, \rb and it flung|וְתַשְׁלֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb truth|אֱמֶת֙\rb* \rb to the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb and prospered|וְהִצְלִֽיחָה׃\rb* \rb in whatever it did|וְעָשְׂתָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then I heard|וָאֶשְׁמְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb a|אֶֽחָד־\rb* \rb holy one|קָד֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֑ר\rb*, \rb and another|אֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb holy|קָד֜וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |לַפַּֽלְמוֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb one said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to him|הַֽמְדַבֵּ֗ר\rb*, “\rb How|עַד־\rb* \rb long until the fulfillment of|מָתַ֞י\rb* \rb the vision|הֶחָז֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the daily sacrifice|הַתָּמִיד֙\rb*, \rb the rebellion|וְהַפֶּ֣שַׁע\rb* \rb that causes desolation|שֹׁמֵ֔ם\rb*, \rb and the surrender|תֵּ֛ת\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|וְקֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb and of the host|וְצָבָ֖א\rb* \rb to be trampled|מִרְמָֽס׃\rb*?”
\p \v 14 \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb It will take|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb 2,300|אַלְפַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֑וֹת\rb* \rb evenings|עֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb and mornings|בֹּ֔קֶר\rb*; \rb then the sanctuary|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb will be properly restored|וְנִצְדַּ֖ק\rb*.”
\s1 Gabriel Interprets Daniel’s Vision
\p \v 15 \rb While|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֖אל\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was watching|בִּרְאֹתִ֛י\rb* \rb the vision|הֶחָז֑וֹן\rb* \rb and trying to|וָאֲבַקְשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb understand it|בִינָ֔ה\rb*, \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb stood|עֹמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb before me|לְנֶגְדִּ֖י\rb* \rb one having the appearance|כְּמַרְאֵה־\rb* \rb of a man|גָֽבֶר׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb the voice|קוֹל־\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb calling|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb from between the banks of|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the Ulai|אוּלָ֑י\rb*: “\rb Gabriel|גַּבְרִיאֵ֕ל\rb*, \rb explain|הָבֵ֥ן\rb* \rb the vision|הַמַּרְאֶֽה׃\rb* \rb to this man|לְהַלָּ֖ז\rb*.”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb As he came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb near|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb to where I stood|עָמְדִ֔י\rb*, \rb I was terrified|נִבְעַ֔תִּי\rb* \rb and fell|וָאֶפְּלָ֖ה\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֑י\rb*.
\p “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb*, “\rb understand|הָבֵ֣ן\rb* \rb that|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb the vision|הֶחָזֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb concerns the time|לְעֶת־\rb* \rb of the end|קֵ֥ץ\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb While he was speaking|וּבְדַבְּר֣וֹ\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb I fell into a deep sleep|נִרְדַּ֥מְתִּי\rb*, \rb with|עַל־\rb* \rb my face|פָּנַ֖י\rb* \rb to the ground|אָ֑רְצָה\rb*.
\p \rb Then he touched|וַיִּ֨גַּע־\rb* \rb me|בִּ֔י\rb*, \rb helped me to my feet|וַיַּֽעֲמִידֵ֖נִי\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |עָמְדִֽי׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֣י\rb*, \rb I will make known to you|מוֹדִֽיעֲךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb will happen|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in the latter time|בְּאַחֲרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of wrath|הַזָּ֑עַם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb it concerns the appointed time|לְמוֹעֵ֥ד\rb* \rb of the end|קֵֽץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb The two-horned|הַקְּרָנָ֑יִם\rb* \rb ram|הָאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you saw|רָאִ֖יתָ\rb*\rb |בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb represents the kings|מַלְכֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Media|מָדַ֥י\rb* \rb and Persia|וּפָרָֽס׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb The shaggy|הַשָּׂעִ֖יר\rb* \rb goat|וְהַצָּפִ֥יר\rb* \rb represents the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Greece|יָוָ֑ן\rb*,\f + \fr 8:21 \ft Hebrew \fqa of Javan\f* \rb and the large|הַגְּדוֹלָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb horn|וְהַקֶּ֤רֶן\rb* \rb between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָ֔יו\rb* \rb is|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb the first|הָרִאשֽׁוֹן׃\rb* \rb king|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb*. \v 22 \rb The four horns|אַרְבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb that replaced|תַּחְתֶּ֑יהָ\rb* \rb the broken one|וְהַ֨נִּשְׁבֶּ֔רֶת\rb* \rb represent four|אַרְבַּ֧ע\rb* \rb kingdoms|מַלְכֻי֛וֹת\rb* \rb that will rise|וַתַּֽעֲמֹ֥דְנָה\rb* \rb from that nation|מִגּ֥וֹי\rb*\rb |יַעֲמֹ֖דְנָה\rb* \rb but will not have|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb the same power|בְכֹחֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb In the latter part|וּֽבְאַחֲרִית֙\rb* \rb of their reign|מַלְכוּתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb when the rebellion|הַפֹּשְׁעִ֑ים\rb* \rb has reached its full measure|כְּהָתֵ֖ם\rb*, \rb an insolent|עַז־\rb*\rb |פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb*, \rb skilled|וּמֵבִ֥ין\rb* \rb in intrigue|חִידֽוֹת׃\rb*, \rb will come to the throne|יַעֲמֹ֛ד\rb*. \v 24 \rb His power|כֹּחוֹ֙\rb* \rb will be great|וְעָצַ֤ם\rb*, \rb but it|בְכֹח֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְנִפְלָא֥וֹת\rb* \rb will not be his own|וְלֹ֣א\rb*. \rb He will cause terrible destruction|יַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb* \rb and succeed|וְהִצְלִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb in whatever he does|וְעָשָׂ֑ה\rb*. \rb He will destroy|וְהִשְׁחִ֥ית\rb* \rb the mighty men|עֲצוּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb along with the holy|קְדֹשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb people|וְעַם־\rb*. \v 25 \rb Through|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his craft|שִׂכְל֗וֹ\rb* \rb and by his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he will cause deceit|מִרְמָה֙\rb* \rb to prosper|וְהִצְלִ֤יחַ\rb*, \rb and in his own mind|וּבִלְבָב֣וֹ\rb* \rb he will make himself great|יַגְדִּ֔יל\rb*. \rb In a time of peace|וּבְשַׁלְוָ֖ה\rb* \rb he will destroy|יַשְׁחִ֣ית\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb and he will even stand|יַעֲמֹ֔ד\rb* \rb against|וְעַ֤ל־\rb* \rb the Prince|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of princes|שָׂרִים֙\rb*. \rb Yet he will be broken off|יִשָּׁבֵֽר׃\rb*, \rb but not|וּבְאֶ֥פֶס\rb* \rb by human hands|יָ֖ד\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb The vision|וּמַרְאֵ֨ה\rb* \rb of the evenings|הָעֶ֧רֶב\rb* \rb and the mornings|וְהַבֹּ֛קֶר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has been spoken|נֶאֱמַ֖ר\rb* \rb is true|אֱמֶ֣ת\rb*.\rb |ה֑וּא\rb* \rb Now you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb must seal up|סְתֹ֣ם\rb* \rb the vision|הֶֽחָז֔וֹן\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb it concerns the distant|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb future|לְיָמִ֥ים\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֗אל\rb*, \rb was exhausted|נִהְיֵ֤יתִי\rb* \rb and lay ill|וְנֶֽחֱלֵ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb for days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*. \rb Then I got up|וָאָק֕וּם\rb* \rb and went about|וָאֶֽעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb business|מְלֶ֣אכֶת\rb*. \rb I was confounded|וָאֶשְׁתּוֹמֵ֥ם\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the vision|הַמַּרְאֶ֖ה\rb*; \rb it was beyond|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb understanding|מֵבִֽין׃פ\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 Daniel’s Prayer for His People
\p \v 1 \rb In the first|אַחַ֗ת\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Darius|לְדָרְיָ֛וֶשׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Xerxes|אֲחַשְׁוֵר֖וֹשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 9:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa Ahasuerus\f* \rb a Mede|מָדָ֑י\rb* \rb by descent|מִזֶּ֣רַע\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was made ruler|הָמְלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 9:1 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* — \v 2 \rb in the first|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֤ת\rb* \rb of his reign|לְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּֽנִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, \rb understood|בִּינֹ֖תִי\rb* \rb from the sacred books|בַּסְּפָרִ֑ים\rb*\rb |מִסְפַּ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֤ה\rb*, \rb according to the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeremiah|יִרְמִיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*, \rb that the desolation|לְחָרְב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb would last|לְמַלֹּ֛אות\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 9:2 \ft See \ref Jeremiah 25:11–12|JER 25:11-12\ref* and Jeremiah 29:10.\f* \v 3 \rb So I turned my attention|וָאֶתְּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פָּנַ֗י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָי֙\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb to seek Him|לְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb by prayer|תְּפִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and petition|וְתַחֲנוּנִ֑ים\rb*, \rb with fasting|בְּצ֖וֹם\rb*, \rb sackcloth|וְשַׂ֥ק\rb*, \rb and ashes|וָאֵֽפֶר׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb And I prayed|וָֽאֶתְפַּֽלְלָ֛ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֖י\rb* \rb and confessed|וָאֶתְוַדֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וָאֹֽמְרָ֗ה\rb*, “\rb O|אָנָּ֤א\rb*, \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָי֙\rb*, \rb the great|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb and awesome|וְהַנּוֹרָ֔א\rb* \rb God|הָאֵ֤ל\rb*, \rb who keeps|שֹׁמֵ֤ר\rb* \rb His covenant|הַבְּרִית֙\rb* \rb of loving devotion|וְֽהַחֶ֔סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 9:4 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb to those who love Him|לְאֹהֲבָ֖יו\rb* \rb and keep|וּלְשֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָֽיו׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb we have sinned|חָטָ֥אנוּ\rb* \rb and done wrong|וְעָוִ֖ינוּ\rb*. \rb We have acted wickedly|וְהִרְשַׁעְנוּ\rb* \rb and rebelled|וּמָרָ֑דְנוּ\rb*. \rb We have turned away|וְס֥וֹר\rb* \rb from Your commandments|מִמִּצְוֺתֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִמִּשְׁפָּטֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb We have not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb listened|שָׁמַ֙עְנוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb in Your name|בְּשִׁמְךָ֔\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb our kings|מְלָכֵ֥ינוּ\rb*, \rb leaders|שָׂרֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb fathers|וַאֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶ֖ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb To You|לְךָ֤\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָי֙\rb*, \rb belongs righteousness|הַצְּדָקָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|כַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb we are covered|הַפָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb with shame|בֹּ֥שֶׁת\rb*— \rb the men|לְאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*, \rb the people|וּלְיוֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb and all|וּֽלְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֞ל\rb* \rb near|הַקְּרֹבִ֣ים\rb* \rb and far|וְהָרְחֹקִ֗ים\rb*, \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the countries|הָֽאֲרָצוֹת֙\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You have driven us|הִדַּחְתָּ֣ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb because of our unfaithfulness|בְּמַעֲלָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to You|בָֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb we|לָ֚נוּ\rb* \rb are covered|הַפָּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb with shame|בֹּ֣שֶׁת\rb* — \rb our kings|לִמְלָכֵ֥ינוּ\rb*, \rb our leaders|לְשָׂרֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb and our fathers|וְלַאֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb* — \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we have sinned|חָטָ֖אנוּ\rb* \rb against You|לָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb To the Lord|לַֽאדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb belong compassion|הָרַחֲמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and forgiveness|וְהַסְּלִח֑וֹת\rb*, \rb even though|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we have rebelled|מָרַ֖דְנוּ\rb* \rb against Him|בּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb and have not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb obeyed|שָׁמַ֔עְנוּ\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb to walk|לָלֶ֤כֶת\rb* \rb in His laws|בְּתֽוֹרֹתָיו֙\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He set|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb before us|לְפָנֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb His servants|עֲבָדָ֥יו\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb has transgressed|עָֽבְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your law|תּ֣וֹרָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and turned away|וְס֕וֹר\rb*, \rb refusing|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to obey|שְׁמ֣וֹעַ\rb* \rb Your voice|בְּקֹלֶ֑ךָ\rb*; \rb so the oath|הָאָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and the curse|וְהַשְּׁבֻעָ֗ה\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבָה֙\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַת֙\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb has been poured out|וַתִּתַּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵ֜ינוּ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we have sinned|חָטָ֖אנוּ\rb* \rb against You|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb You have carried out|וַיָּ֜קֶם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דְּבָרָיו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb spoken|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb against us|עָלֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb and against|וְעַ֤ל\rb* \rb our rulers|שֹֽׁפְטֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |שְׁפָט֔וּנוּ\rb* \rb by bringing|לְהָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb a great|גְדֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֣ה\rb*. \rb For under|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb has ever been done|נֶעֶשְׂתָ֗ה\rb* \rb like what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb has been done|נֶעֶשְׂתָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb it is written|כָּתוּב֙\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֔ה\rb*,\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb disaster|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֣אָה\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, \rb yet we have not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb sought the favor|חִלִּ֜ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb by turning|לָשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb from our iniquities|מֵֽעֲוֺנֵ֔נוּ\rb* \rb and giving attention|וּלְהַשְׂכִּ֖יל\rb* \rb to Your truth|בַּאֲמִתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Therefore the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has kept the calamity|הָ֣רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb in store|וַיִּשְׁקֹ֤ד\rb* \rb and brought it|וַיְבִיאֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb upon us|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb is righteous|צַדִּ֞יק\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |מַֽעֲשָׂיו֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He does|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*; \rb yet we have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb obeyed|שָׁמַ֖עְנוּ\rb* \rb His voice|בְּקֹלֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb brought|הוֹצֵ֨אתָ\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֜\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb with a mighty|חֲזָקָ֔ה\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֣ד\rb*, \rb and who made|וַתַּֽעַשׂ־\rb* \rb for Yourself|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb a name|שֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb renowned to this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|כַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb we have sinned|חָטָ֖אנוּ\rb*; \rb we have acted wickedly|רָשָֽׁעְנוּ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb*, \rb in keeping with all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb Your righteous acts|צִדְקֹתֶ֙ךָ֙\rb*, \rb I pray|נָ֤א\rb* \rb that Your anger|אַפְּךָ֙\rb* \rb and wrath|וַחֲמָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb may turn away|יָֽשָׁב־\rb* \rb from Your city|מֵעִֽירְךָ֥\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*, \rb Your holy|קָדְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb mountain|הַר־\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb because of our sins|בַחֲטָאֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb and the iniquities|וּבַעֲוֺנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֧ם\rb* \rb and Your people|וְעַמְּךָ֛\rb* \rb are a reproach|לְחֶרְפָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb around us|סְבִיבֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֗ינוּ\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb hear|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the prayers|תְּפִלַּ֤ת\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb petitions|תַּ֣חֲנוּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb*. \rb For Your sake|לְמַ֖עַן\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָֽי׃\rb*, \rb cause Your face|פָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to shine|וְהָאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Your desolate|הַשָּׁמֵ֑ם\rb* \rb sanctuary|מִקְדָּשְׁךָ֖\rb*. \v 18 \rb Incline|הַטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb Your ear|אָזְנְךָ֮\rb*, \rb O my God|אֱלֹהַ֥י׀\rb*, \rb and hear|וּֽשֲׁמָע֒\rb*; \rb open|פִּקְחָה\rb* \rb Your eyes|עֵינֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאֵה֙\rb* \rb the desolation|שֹֽׁמְמֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb of the city|וְהָעִ֕יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb that bears|נִקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb Your name|שִׁמְךָ֖\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֨חְנוּ\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb presenting|מַפִּילִ֤ים\rb* \rb our petitions|תַּחֲנוּנֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb our righteous acts|צִדְקֹתֵ֗ינוּ\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb Your great|הָרַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb compassion|רַחֲמֶ֥יךָ\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י׀\rb*, \rb listen|שְׁמָ֙עָה֙\rb*! \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י׀\rb*, \rb forgive|סְלָ֔חָה\rb*! \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֛י\rb*, \rb hear|הַֽקֲשִׁ֥יבָה\rb* \rb and act|וַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb*! \rb For Your sake|לְמַֽעֲנְךָ֣\rb*, \rb O my God|אֱלֹהַ֔י\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb delay|תְּאַחַ֑ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Your city|עִירְךָ֖\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and Your people|עַמֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb bear|נִקְרָ֔א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Your name|שִׁמְךָ֣\rb*.”
\s1 Gabriel’s Prophecy of the Seventy Weeks
\p \v 20 \rb While|וְע֨וֹד\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb was speaking|מְדַבֵּר֙\rb*, \rb praying|וּמִתְפַּלֵּ֔ל\rb*, \rb confessing|וּמִתְוַדֶּה֙\rb* \rb my sin|חַטָּאתִ֔י\rb* \rb and that|וְחַטַּ֖את\rb* \rb of my people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and presenting|וּמַפִּ֣יל\rb* \rb my petition|תְּחִנָּתִ֗י\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֔י\rb* \rb concerning|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb His|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb* \rb mountain|הַר־\rb*— \v 21 \rb while|וְע֛וֹד\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb was still praying|מְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |בַּתְּפִלָּ֑ה\rb*, \rb Gabriel|גַּבְרִיאֵ֡ל\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the man|וְהָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֨יתִי\rb* \rb in the earlier|בַּתְּחִלָּה֙\rb*\rb |מֻעָ֣ף\rb* \rb vision|בֶחָז֤וֹן\rb*, \rb came|נֹגֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb in swift flight|בִּיעָ֔ף\rb* \rb about the time|כְּעֵ֖ת\rb* \rb of the evening|עָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb sacrifice|מִנְחַת־\rb*. \v 22 \rb He instructed me|וַיָּ֖בֶן\rb* \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֑י\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*: “\rb O Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֕אל\rb*, \rb I have come|יָצָ֖אתִי\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb to give you insight|לְהַשְׂכִּילְךָ֥\rb* \rb and understanding|בִינָֽה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb At the beginning|בִּתְחִלַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of your petitions|תַּחֲנוּנֶ֜יךָ\rb*, \rb an answer|דָבָ֗ר\rb* \rb went out|יָצָ֣א\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb have come|בָּ֣אתִי\rb* \rb to tell you|לְהַגִּ֔יד\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you are|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb highly precious|חֲמוּד֖וֹת\rb*. \rb So consider|וּבִין֙\rb* \rb the message|בַּדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb and understand|וְהָבֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the vision|בַּמַּרְאֶֽה׃\rb*:
\p \v 24 \rb Seventy|שִׁבְעִ֜ים\rb* \rb weeks|שָׁבֻעִ֨ים\rb*\f + \fr 9:24 \ft Or \fqa Seventy sevens\ft ; also twice in verse 25 and once in verse 26 \f* \rb are decreed|נֶחְתַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb for|עַֽל־\rb* \rb your people|עַמְּךָ֣׀\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and your holy|קָדְשֶׁ֗ךָ\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb to stop|לְכַלֵּ֨א\rb* \rb their transgression|הַפֶּ֜שַׁע\rb*, \rb to put an end|וּלַחְתֹּם\rb* \rb to sin|חַטָּאוֹת\rb*, \rb to make atonement|וּלְכַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb for iniquity|עָוֺ֔ן\rb*, \rb to bring in|וּלְהָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb everlasting|עֹֽלָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb righteousness|צֶ֣דֶק\rb*, \rb to seal up|וְלַחְתֹּם֙\rb* \rb vision|חָז֣וֹן\rb* \rb and prophecy|וְנָבִ֔יא\rb*, \rb and to anoint|וְלִמְשֹׁ֖חַ\rb* \rb the Most Holy Place|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |קָֽדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 9:24 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies \ft or \fqa the Most Holy One\ft ; literally \fqa the Most Holy\f*
\p \v 25 \rb Know|וְתֵדַ֨ע\rb* \rb and understand this|וְתַשְׂכֵּ֜ל\rb*: \rb From|מִן־\rb* \rb the issuance|מֹצָ֣א\rb* \rb of the decree|דָבָ֗ר\rb* \rb to restore|לְהָשִׁיב֙\rb* \rb and rebuild|וְלִבְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the Messiah|מָשִׁ֣יחַ\rb*,\f + \fr 9:25 \ft Or \fqa the Anointed One\ft ; also in verse 26\f* \rb the Prince|נָגִ֔יד\rb*, \rb there will be seven|שִׁבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb weeks|שָׁבֻעִ֖ים\rb* \rb and sixty-two|שִׁשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֗יִם\rb* \rb weeks|וְשָׁבֻעִ֞ים\rb*. \rb It will be rebuilt|תָּשׁוּב֙\rb*\rb |וְנִבְנְתָה֙\rb* \rb with streets|רְח֣וֹב\rb* \rb and a trench|וְחָר֔וּץ\rb*, \rb but in times|הָעִתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb of distress|וּבְצ֖וֹק\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Then after|וְאַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb the sixty-two|שִׁשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb weeks|הַשָּׁבֻעִים֙\rb*\f + \fr 9:26 \ft Hebrew \fqa Then after sixty-two sevens\f* \rb the Messiah|מָשִׁ֖יחַ\rb* \rb will be cut off|יִכָּרֵ֥ת\rb* \rb and will have nothing|וְאֵ֣ין\rb*.
\p \rb Then the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the prince|נָגִ֤יד\rb* \rb who is to come|הַבָּא֙\rb* \rb will destroy|יַ֠שְׁחִית\rb* \rb the city|וְהָעִ֨יר\rb* \rb and the sanctuary|וְהַקֹּ֜דֶשׁ\rb*. \rb The end|וְקִצּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb will come like a flood|בַשֶּׁ֔טֶף\rb*, \rb and until|וְעַד֙\rb* \rb the end|קֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb there will be war|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*; \rb desolations|שֹׁמֵמֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb have been decreed|נֶחֱרֶ֖צֶת\rb*. \v 27 \rb And he will confirm|וְהִגְבִּ֥יר\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֛ית\rb* \rb with many|לָרַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb week|שָׁב֣וּעַ\rb*,\f + \fr 9:27 \ft Or \fqa for one seven\ft ; similarly again in this verse\f* \rb but in the middle|וַחֲצִ֨י\rb* \rb of the week|הַשָּׁב֜וּעַ\rb* \rb he will put an end|יַשְׁבִּ֣ית׀\rb* \rb to sacrifice|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb and offering|וּמִנְחָ֗ה\rb*. \rb And on|וְעַ֨ל\rb* \rb the wing of the temple|כְּנַ֤ף\rb* \rb will come the abomination|שִׁקּוּצִים֙\rb* \rb that causes desolation|מְשֹׁמֵ֔ם\rb*,\f + \fr 9:27 \ft Literally \fqa And on the wing (will come) the abomination that causes desolation, \ft or \fqa And on the wing of abominations (will come) one who causes desolation,\f* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the decreed|וְנֶ֣חֱרָצָ֔ה\rb* \rb destruction|כָּלָה֙\rb* \rb is poured out|תִּתַּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb him|שֹׁמֵֽם׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 9:27 \ft Literally \fqa until the decreed consummation is poured out upon (him who) is desolate.\f*”
\c 10
\s1 Daniel’s Vision by the Tigris
\p \v 1 \rb In the third|שָׁל֗וֹשׁ\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Cyrus|לְכ֙וֹרֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֔ס\rb*, \rb a message|דָּבָר֙\rb* \rb was revealed|נִגְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb to Daniel|לְדָֽנִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb was called|נִקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Belteshazzar|בֵּלְטְשַׁאצַּ֑ר\rb*. \rb The message|הַדָּבָר֙\rb* \rb was true|וֶאֱמֶ֤ת\rb*, \rb and it concerned a great|גָד֔וֹל\rb* \rb conflict|וְצָבָ֣א\rb*.\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Or \fqa true and greatly burdensome\f* \rb And the understanding|וּבִ֥ינָה\rb* \rb of the message|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb was given to him|וּבִין֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in a vision|בַּמַּרְאֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb In those|הָהֵ֑ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָֽנִיֵּאל֙\rb*, \rb was|הָיִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb mourning|מִתְאַבֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb for three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb full|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb weeks|שָׁבֻעִ֖ים\rb*. \v 3 \rb I ate|אָכַ֗לְתִּי\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb rich|חֲמֻד֞וֹת\rb* \rb food|לֶ֣חֶם\rb*, \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb meat|וּבָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb or wine|וָיַ֛יִן\rb* \rb entered|בָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֖י\rb*, \rb and I did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb anoint myself with oil|וְס֣וֹךְ\rb*\rb |סָ֑כְתִּי\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb weeks|שָׁבֻעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |יָמִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb were completed|מְלֹ֕את\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb On the twenty-fourth|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb day|וּבְי֛וֹם\rb* \rb of the first|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb as I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb was|הָיִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb standing on|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the bank|יַ֧ד\rb* \rb of the great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb river|הַנָּהָ֛ר\rb*, \rb the Tigris|חִדָּֽקֶל׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb I lifted up|וָאֶשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb*,\rb |וָאֵ֔רֶא\rb* \rb and behold|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb there was a certain|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb dressed|לָב֣וּשׁ\rb* \rb in linen|בַּדִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb with a belt|חֲגֻרִ֖ים\rb* \rb of fine gold|בְּכֶ֥תֶם\rb* \rb from Uphaz|אוּפָֽז׃\rb* \rb around his waist|וּמָתְנָ֥יו\rb*. \v 6 \rb His body was|וּגְוִיָּת֣וֹ\rb* \rb like beryl|כְתַרְשִׁ֗ישׁ\rb*, \rb his face|וּפָנָ֞יו\rb* \rb like the brilliance|כְּמַרְאֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of lightning|בָרָק֙\rb*, \rb his eyes|וְעֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb like flaming|אֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb torches|כְּלַפִּ֣ידֵי\rb*, \rb his arms|וּזְרֹֽעֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb and legs|וּמַרְגְּלֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb like the gleam|כְּעֵ֖ין\rb* \rb of polished|קָלָ֑ל\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*, \rb and|וְק֥וֹל\rb* \rb his voice|דְּבָרָ֖יו\rb* \rb like the sound|כְּק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of a multitude|הָמֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Only|לְבַדִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֤אל\rb*, \rb saw|וְרָאִיתִי֩\rb* \rb the vision|הַמַּרְאָ֔ה\rb*; \rb the men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb see it|רָא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַמַּרְאָ֑ה\rb*, \rb but|אֲבָ֗ל\rb* \rb a great|גְדֹלָה֙\rb* \rb terror|חֲרָדָ֤ה\rb* \rb fell|נָפְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and they ran|וַֽיִּבְרְח֖וּ\rb* \rb and hid themselves|בְּהֵחָבֵֽא׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb So I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb was left alone|נִשְׁאַ֣רְתִּי\rb*\rb |לְבַדִּ֔י\rb*, \rb gazing at|וָֽאֶרְאֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb great|הַגְּדֹלָה֙\rb* \rb vision|הַמַּרְאָ֤ה\rb*. \rb No|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb strength|כֹּ֑ח\rb* \rb remained|נִשְׁאַר־\rb* \rb in me|בִּ֖י\rb*; \rb my face|וְהוֹדִ֗י\rb* \rb grew|נֶהְפַּ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |עָלַי֙\rb* \rb deathly pale|לְמַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb*, \rb and I was powerless|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |עָצַ֖רְתִּי\rb*\rb |כֹּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of his words|דְּבָרָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and as I listened|וּכְשָׁמְעִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |ק֣וֹל\rb*,\rb |דְּבָרָ֔יו\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb*\rb |הָיִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb fell into a deep sleep|נִרְדָּ֥ם\rb*,\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb with my face|פָּנַ֖י\rb*\rb |וּפָנַ֥י\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Suddenly|וְהִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb a hand|יָ֖ד\rb* \rb touched|נָ֣גְעָה\rb* \rb me|בִּ֑י\rb* \rb and set me trembling|וַתְּנִיעֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my hands|וְכַפּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יָדָֽי׃\rb* \rb and knees|בִּרְכַּ֖י\rb*. \v 11 \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֡י\rb*, “\rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֣אל\rb*, \rb you are a man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb who is highly precious|חֲ֠מֻדוֹת\rb*. \rb Consider carefully|הָבֵ֨ן\rb* \rb the words|בַּדְּבָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֨י\rb* \rb about to say|דֹבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*. \rb Stand up|וַעֲמֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |עָמְדֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb been sent|שֻׁלַּ֣חְתִּי\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*.”
\p \rb And when he had said|וּבְדַבְּר֥וֹ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb to me|עִמִּ֛י\rb*,\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I stood up|עָמַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb trembling|מַרְעִֽיד׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֣א\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּאל֒\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַי֮\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the first|הָרִאשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you purposed|נָתַ֧תָּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb*\rb |לִבְּךָ֛\rb* \rb to understand|לְהָבִ֧ין\rb* \rb and to humble|וּלְהִתְעַנּ֛וֹת\rb* \rb yourself before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֖יךָ\rb*, \rb your words|דְבָרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb were heard|נִשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִי־\rb* \rb have come|בָ֖אתִי\rb* \rb in response to them|בִּדְבָרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb However, the prince|וְשַׂ֣ר׀\rb* \rb of the kingdom|מַלְכ֣וּת\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרַ֗ס\rb* \rb opposed|עֹמֵ֤ד\rb* \rb me|לְנֶגְדִּי֙\rb* \rb for twenty-one|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb*.\rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb Then Michael|מִֽיכָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb one|אַחַ֛ד\rb* \rb of the chief|הָרִאשֹׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb princes|הַשָּׂרִ֥ים\rb*, \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to help me|לְעָזְרֵ֑נִי\rb*, \rb for I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb had been left|נוֹתַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb with|אֵ֖צֶל\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Persia|פָרָֽס׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Now I have come|וּבָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb to explain to you|לַהֲבִ֣ינְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb will happen|יִקְרָ֥ה\rb* \rb to your people|לְעַמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb in the latter|בְּאַחֲרִ֣ית\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb*\rb |ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb the vision|חָז֖וֹן\rb* \rb concerns those days|לַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb While he was speaking|וּבְדַבְּר֣וֹ\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|כַּדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to me|עִמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb I set|נָתַ֧תִּי\rb* \rb my face|פָנַ֛י\rb* \rb toward the ground|אַ֖רְצָה\rb* \rb and became speechless|וְנֶאֱלָֽמְתִּי׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb one with the likeness|כִּדְמוּת֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 10:16 \ft Most MT manuscripts; literally \fqa with the likeness of sons of man\ft ; DSS, LXX, and one MT manuscript \fqa with the likeness of the hand of a man\f* \rb touched|נֹגֵ֖עַ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb my lips|שְׂפָתָ֑י\rb*, \rb and I opened|וָאֶפְתַּח־\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֗י\rb*\rb |וָאֲדַבְּרָה֙\rb* \rb and said|וָאֹֽמְרָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the one standing|הָעֹמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb before me|לְנֶגְדִּ֔י\rb*, “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֗י\rb*, \rb because of the vision|בַּמַּרְאָה֙\rb*, \rb I am overcome|נֶהֶפְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb with anguish|צִירַי֙\rb*\rb |עָלַ֔י\rb*, \rb and I have|עָצַ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb strength|כֹּֽחַ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb How|וְהֵ֣יךְ\rb* \rb can I|יוּכַ֗ל\rb*, \rb your|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb*\rb |זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb servant|עֶ֤בֶד\rb*, \rb speak|לְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb you|זֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹ֣נִי\rb*? \rb Now|מֵעַ֙תָּה֙\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb have|יַעֲמָד־\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb strength|כֹ֔חַ\rb*, \rb nor|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb is any breath|וּנְשָׁמָ֖ה\rb* \rb left|נִשְׁאֲרָה־\rb* \rb in me|בִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Again|וַיֹּ֧סֶף\rb* \rb the one with the likeness|כְּמַרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb touched|וַיִּגַּע־\rb* \rb me|בִּ֛י\rb* \rb and strengthened me|וַֽיְחַזְּקֵֽנִי׃\rb*. \v 19 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֧א\rb*,\rb |אִישׁ־\rb* \rb you who are highly precious|חֲמֻד֛וֹת\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Peace be|שָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb with you|לָ֖ךְ\rb*! \rb Be strong now|חֲזַ֣ק\rb*; \rb be very strong|וַחֲזָ֑ק\rb*!”
\p \rb As he spoke|וּֽבְדַבְּר֤וֹ\rb* \rb with me|עִמִּי֙\rb*, \rb I was strengthened|הִתְחַזַּ֔קְתִּי\rb* \rb and said|וָאֹֽמְרָ֛ה\rb*, “\rb Speak|יְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have strengthened me|חִזַּקְתָּֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 “\rb Do you know|הֲיָדַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb* \rb why|לָמָּה־\rb* \rb I have come|בָּ֣אתִי\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*?” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. “\rb I must return|אָשׁ֔וּב\rb* \rb at once|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the prince|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of Persia|פָּרָ֑ס\rb*, \rb and when I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have gone forth|יוֹצֵ֔א\rb*, \rb behold|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the prince|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of Greece|יָוָ֖ן\rb*\f + \fr 10:20 \ft Hebrew \fqa of Javan\f* \rb will come|בָּֽא׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb But first|אֲבָל֙\rb* \rb I will tell|אַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what is inscribed|הָרָשׁ֥וּם\rb* \rb in the Book|בִּכְתָ֖ב\rb* \rb of Truth|אֱמֶ֑ת\rb*. \rb Yet no|וְאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb has the courage|מִתְחַזֵּ֤ק\rb* \rb to support me|עִמִּי֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb*, \rb except|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb Michael|מִיכָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb your prince|שַׂרְכֶֽם׃פ\rb*.[’’]
\c 11
\s1 Kings of the South and North
\p \v 1 “\rb And I|וַאֲנִי֙\rb*, \rb in the first|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Darius|לְדָרְיָ֖וֶשׁ\rb* \rb the Mede|הַמָּדִ֑י\rb*, \rb stood up|עָמְדִ֛י\rb* \rb to strengthen|לְמַחֲזִ֥יק\rb* \rb and protect|וּלְמָע֖וֹז\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Now then|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*, \rb I will tell|אַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb you|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb the truth|אֱמֶ֖ת\rb*:\rb |הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb Three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֨ה\rb* \rb more|עוֹד֩\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִ֜ים\rb* \rb will arise|עֹמְדִ֣ים\rb* \rb in Persia|לְפָרַ֗ס\rb*, \rb and then a fourth|וְהָֽרְבִיעִי֙\rb*, \rb who will be|עֹֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb far|גָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb richer|יַעֲשִׁ֤יר\rb* \rb than all the others|מִכֹּ֔ל\rb*. \rb By the power|וּכְחֶזְקָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb of his wealth|בְעָשְׁר֔וֹ\rb*, \rb he will stir up|יָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb everyone|הַכֹּ֔ל\rb* \rb against|אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the kingdom|מַלְכ֥וּת\rb* \rb of Greece|יָוָֽן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 11:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa of Javan\f*
