\p \v 23 \rb After|וּמִן־\rb* \rb an alliance is made|הִֽתְחַבְּר֥וּת\rb* \rb with him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*, \rb he will act|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb deceitfully|מִרְמָ֑ה\rb*; \rb for he will rise|וְעָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb to power|וְעָצַ֖ם\rb* \rb with only a few|בִּמְעַט־\rb* \rb people|גּֽוֹי׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb In a time of peace|בְּשַׁלְוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb he will invade|יָבוֹא֒\rb* \rb the richest|וּבְמִשְׁמַנֵּ֣י\rb* \rb provinces|מְדִינָה֮\rb* \rb and do|וְעָשָׂ֗ה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb and forefathers|וַאֲב֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb did|עָשׂ֤וּ\rb*. \rb He will lavish|יִבְז֑וֹר\rb* \rb plunder|בִּזָּ֧ה\rb*, \rb loot|וְשָׁלָ֛ל\rb*, \rb and wealth on his followers|וּרְכ֖וּשׁ\rb*,\rb |לָהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and he will plot|יְחַשֵּׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |מַחְשְׁבֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb against|וְעַ֧ל\rb* \rb the strongholds|מִבְצָרִ֛ים\rb* — \rb but only for|וְעַד־\rb* \rb a time|עֵֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And with a large|גָּדוֹל֒\rb* \rb army|בְּחַ֣יִל\rb* \rb he will stir up|וְיָעֵר֩\rb* \rb his power|כֹּח֨וֹ\rb* \rb and his courage|וּלְבָב֜וֹ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the South|הַנֶּגֶב֮\rb*, \rb who|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הַנֶּ֗גֶב\rb* \rb will mobilize|יִתְגָּרֶה֙\rb*\rb |לַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb a very|עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb large|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb and powerful|וְעָצ֖וּם\rb* \rb army|בְּחַֽיִל־\rb* \rb but will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb withstand|יַעֲמֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the plots|מַחֲשָׁבֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb devised|יַחְשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*. \v 26 \rb Those who eat|וְאֹכְלֵ֧י\rb*\rb |פַת־\rb* \rb from his provisions|בָּג֛וֹ\rb* \rb will seek to destroy him|יִשְׁבְּר֖וּהוּ\rb*; \rb his army|וְחֵיל֣וֹ\rb* \rb will be swept away|יִשְׁט֑וֹף\rb*, \rb and many|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb will fall|וְנָפְל֖וּ\rb* \rb slain|חֲלָלִ֥ים\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb And the two|וּשְׁנֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִים֙\rb*, \rb with their hearts|לְבָבָ֣ם\rb* \rb bent on evil|לְמֵרָ֔ע\rb*, \rb will speak|יְדַבֵּ֑רוּ\rb* \rb lies|כָּזָ֣ב\rb* \rb at|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb table|שֻׁלְחָ֥ן\rb*, \rb but to no|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb avail|תִצְלָ֔ח\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb still|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb the end|קֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb will come at the appointed time|לַמּוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb The king of the North will return|וְיָשֹׁ֤ב\rb* \rb to his land|אַרְצוֹ֙\rb* \rb with great|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb wealth|בִּרְכ֣וּשׁ\rb*, \rb but his heart|וּלְבָב֖וֹ\rb* \rb will be set against|עַל־\rb* \rb the holy|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb*; \rb so he will do damage|וְעָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb and return|וְשָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb to his own land|לְאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb At the appointed time|לַמּוֹעֵ֥ד\rb* \rb he will invade|וּבָ֣א\rb* \rb the South|בַנֶּ֑גֶב\rb* \rb again|יָשׁ֖וּב\rb*, \rb but this time will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb be|תִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb like the first|כָרִאשֹׁנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְכָאַחֲרֹנָֽה׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Ships|צִיִּ֤ים\rb* \rb of Kittim|כִּתִּים֙\rb*\f + \fr 11:30 \ft Or \fqa western coastlands \ft or \fqa Mediterranean islands\f* \rb will come|וּבָ֨אוּ\rb* \rb against him|ב֜וֹ\rb*, \rb and he will lose heart|וְנִכְאָ֔ה\rb*. \rb Then he will turn back|וְשָׁ֛ב\rb* \rb and rage|וְזָעַ֥ם\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the holy|ק֖וֹדֶשׁ\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִֽית־\rb* \rb and do damage|וְעָשָׂ֑ה\rb*. \rb So he will return|וְשָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb and show favor|וְיָבֵ֔ן\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb those who forsake|עֹזְבֵ֖י\rb* \rb the holy|קֹֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb*. \v 31 \rb His|מִמֶּ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb forces|וּזְרֹעִ֖ים\rb* \rb will rise up|יַעֲמֹ֑דוּ\rb* \rb and desecrate|וְחִלְּל֞וּ\rb* \rb the temple|הַמִּקְדָּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb fortress|הַמָּעוֹז֙\rb*. \rb They will abolish|וְהֵסִ֣ירוּ\rb* \rb the daily sacrifice|הַתָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb and set up|וְנָתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb the abomination|הַשִּׁקּ֥וּץ\rb* \rb of desolation|מְשׁוֹמֵֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb With flattery|בַּחֲלַקּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb he will corrupt|יַחֲנִ֖יף\rb* \rb those who violate|וּמַרְשִׁיעֵ֣י\rb* \rb the covenant|בְרִ֔ית\rb*, \rb but the people|וְעַ֛ם\rb* \rb who know|יֹדְעֵ֥י\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהָ֖יו\rb* \rb will firmly|יַחֲזִ֥קוּ\rb* \rb resist him|וְעָשֽׂוּ׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb Those with insight|וּמַשְׂכִּ֣ילֵי\rb*\rb |עָ֔ם\rb* \rb will instruct|יָבִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb many|לָֽרַבִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb though for a time|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb they will fall|וְנִכְשְׁל֞וּ\rb* \rb by sword|בְּחֶ֧רֶב\rb* \rb or flame|וּבְלֶהָבָ֛ה\rb*, \rb or be captured|בִּשְׁבִ֥י\rb* \rb or plundered|וּבְבִזָּ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb Now when they fall|וּבְהִכָּ֣שְׁלָ֔ם\rb*, \rb they will be granted|יֵעָזְר֖וּ\rb* \rb a little|מְעָ֑ט\rb* \rb help|עֵ֣זֶר\rb*, \rb but many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb will join|וְנִלְו֧וּ\rb* \rb them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb insincerely|בַּחֲלַקְלַקּֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb Some of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the wise|הַמַּשְׂכִּילִ֣ים\rb* \rb will fall|יִכָּֽשְׁל֗וּ\rb* \rb so that they may be refined|לִצְר֥וֹף\rb*, \rb purified|וּלְבָרֵ֥ר\rb*, \rb and made spotless|וְלַלְבֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the time|עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb of the end|קֵ֑ץ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb it will still|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb come at the appointed time|לַמּוֹעֵֽד׃\rb*.
\s1 The King Who Exalts Himself
\p \v 36 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb will do|וְעָשָׂ֨ה\rb* \rb as he pleases|כִרְצוֹנ֜וֹ\rb* \rb and will exalt|וְיִתְרוֹמֵ֤ם\rb* \rb and magnify himself|וְיִתְגַּדֵּל֙\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb god|אֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and he will speak|יְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb monstrous things|נִפְלָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb against|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb the God|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb of gods|אֵלִ֔ים\rb*. \rb He will be successful|וְהִצְלִ֙יחַ֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the time of wrath|זַ֔עַם\rb* \rb is completed|כָּ֣לָה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb what has been decreed|נֶחֱרָצָ֖ה\rb* \rb must be accomplished|נֶעֱשָֽׂתָה׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb He will show no regard|יָבִ֔ין\rb* \rb for|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of his fathers|אֲבֹתָיו֙\rb*, \rb nor|וְעַל־\rb* \rb for the one desired|חֶמְדַּ֥ת\rb* \rb by women|נָשִׁ֛ים\rb*, \rb nor|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb for any|כָּל־\rb* \rb other god|אֱל֖וֹהַּ\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יָבִ֑ין\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he will magnify himself|יִתְגַּדָּֽל׃\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb them all|כֹּ֖ל\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb And in|עַל־\rb* \rb their place|כַּנּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb he will honor|יְכַבֵּ֑ד\rb* \rb a god|וְלֶאֱלֹ֙הַּ֙\rb* \rb of fortresses|מָֽעֻזִּ֔ים\rb*— \rb a god|וְלֶאֱל֜וֹהַּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֗יו\rb*\rb |יְכַבֵּ֛ד\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know|יְדָעֻ֣הוּ\rb*— \rb with gold|בְּזָהָ֥ב\rb*, \rb silver|וּבְכֶ֛סֶף\rb*, \rb precious|יְקָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb stones|וּבְאֶ֥בֶן\rb*, \rb and riches|וּבַחֲמֻדֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 39 \rb He will attack|וְעָשָׂ֞ה\rb* \rb the strongest fortresses|לְמִבְצְרֵ֤י\rb*\rb |מָֽעֻזִּים֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the help of a foreign|נֵכָ֔ר\rb* \rb god|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb* \rb and will greatly|יַרְבֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb honor|כָב֑וֹד\rb* \rb those who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb acknowledge him|הִכִּיר\rb*, \rb making them rulers|וְהִמְשִׁילָם֙\rb* \rb over many|בָּֽרַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and distributing|יְחַלֵּ֥ק\rb* \rb the land|וַאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb for a price|בִּמְחִֽיר׃\rb*.\f + \fr 11:39 \ft Or \fqa for a reward\f*
\p \v 40 \rb At the time|וּבְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb of the end|קֵ֗ץ\rb*, \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the South|הַנֶּ֔גֶב\rb* \rb will engage him in battle|יִתְנַגַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |עִמּוֹ֙\rb*,\f + \fr 11:40 \ft Hebrew \fqa will thrust at him\f* \rb but the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the North|הַצָּפ֗וֹן\rb* \rb will storm out|וְיִשְׂתָּעֵ֨ר\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb with chariots|בְּרֶ֙כֶב֙\rb*, \rb horsemen|וּבְפָ֣רָשִׁ֔ים\rb*, \rb and many|רַבּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb ships|וּבָאֳנִיּ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb invading|וּבָ֥א\rb* \rb many countries|בַאֲרָצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and sweeping through them|וְעָבָֽר׃\rb* \rb like a flood|וְשָׁטַ֥ף\rb*. \v 41 \rb He will also invade|וּבָא֙\rb* \rb the Beautiful|הַצְּבִ֔י\rb* \rb Land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb and many countries|וְרַבּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb will fall|יִכָּשֵׁ֑לוּ\rb*. \rb But these|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb will be delivered|יִמָּלְט֣וּ\rb* \rb from his hand|מִיָּד֔וֹ\rb*: \rb Edom|אֱד֣וֹם\rb*, \rb Moab|וּמוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and the leaders|וְרֵאשִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb He will extend|וְיִשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb his power|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb over many countries|בַּאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and not even|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |תִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the land|וְאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb will escape|לִפְלֵיטָֽה׃\rb*. \v 43 \rb He will gain control|וּמָשַׁ֗ל\rb* \rb of the treasures|בְּמִכְמַנֵּי֙\rb* \rb of gold|הַזָּהָ֣ב\rb* \rb and silver|וְהַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb and over all|וּבְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the riches|חֲמֻד֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb and the Libyans|וְלֻבִ֥ים\rb* \rb and Cushites|וְכֻשִׁ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 11:43 \ft That is, people from the upper Nile region\f* \rb will also submit to him|בְּמִצְעָדָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 44 \rb But news|וּשְׁמֻע֣וֹת\rb* \rb from the east|מִמִּזְרָ֖ח\rb* \rb and the north|וּמִצָּפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb will alarm him|יְבַהֲלֻ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and he will go out|וְיָצָא֙\rb* \rb with great|גְדֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb fury|בְּחֵמָ֣א\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁמִ֥יד\rb* \rb many|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb and devote them to destruction|וּֽלְהַחֲרִ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 11:44 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \v 45 \rb He will pitch|וְיִטַּע֙\rb* \rb his royal|אַפַּדְנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb tents|אָהֳלֶ֣י\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the sea|יַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and the beautiful|צְבִי־\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb mountain|לְהַר־\rb*, \rb but he will meet|וּבָא֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb his end|קִצּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb with no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to help|עוֹזֵ֖ר\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.[’’]
\c 12
\s1 The End Times
\r (\ref Revelation 1:1–3|REV 1:1-3\ref*)
\p \v 1 “\rb At that|הַהִיא֩\rb* \rb time|וּבָעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Michael|מִֽיכָאֵ֜ל\rb*, \rb the great|הַגָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb prince|הַשַּׂ֣ר\rb* \rb who stands watch|יַעֲמֹ֨ד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb your people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*,\rb |עַמֶּךָ֒\rb* \rb will rise up|הָעֹמֵד֮\rb*. \rb There will be|וְהָיְתָה֙\rb* \rb a time|עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb of distress|צָרָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the likes of which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb will not have|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb occurred|נִהְיְתָה֙\rb* \rb from the beginning|מִֽהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb of nations|גּ֔וֹי\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb time|הָעֵ֣ת\rb*. \rb But at that|הַהִיא֙\rb* \rb time|וּבָעֵ֤ת\rb* \rb your people|עַמְּךָ֔\rb* — \rb everyone whose name|כָּל־\rb* \rb is found|הַנִּמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb written|כָּת֥וּב\rb* \rb in the book|בַּסֵּֽפֶר׃\rb* — \rb will be delivered|יִמָּלֵ֣ט\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And many|וְרַבִּ֕ים\rb* \rb who sleep|מִיְּשֵׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the dust|עָפָ֖ר\rb* \rb of the earth|אַדְמַת־\rb* \rb will awake|יָקִ֑יצוּ\rb*, \rb some|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb to everlasting|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb life|לְחַיֵּ֣י\rb*, \rb but others|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb to shame|לַחֲרָפ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and everlasting|עוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb contempt|לְדִרְא֥וֹן\rb*.\f + \fr 12:2 \ft See \ref John 5:29|JHN 5:29\ref* and Revelation 11:18.\f* \v 3 \rb Then the wise|וְהַ֨מַּשְׂכִּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb will shine|יַזְהִ֖רוּ\rb* \rb like the brightness|כְּזֹ֣הַר\rb* \rb of the heavens|הָרָקִ֑יעַ\rb*,\f + \fr 12:3 \ft Or \fqa expanse \ft or \fqa firmament\ft ; see also \ref Genesis 1:6–8|GEN 1:6-8\ref*.\f* \rb and those who lead many|הָֽרַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb to righteousness|וּמַצְדִּיקֵי֙\rb* \rb will shine like the stars|כַּכּוֹכָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָ֥ם\rb* \rb and ever|וָעֶֽד׃פ\rb*.\f + \fr 12:3 \ft See \ref Matthew 13:43|MAT 13:43\ref*.\f*
\p \v 4 \rb But you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָֽנִיֵּ֗אל\rb*, \rb shut up|סְתֹ֧ם\rb* \rb these words|הַדְּבָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb and seal|וַחֲתֹ֥ם\rb* \rb the book|הַסֵּ֖פֶר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the time|עֵ֣ת\rb* \rb of the end|קֵ֑ץ\rb*. \rb Many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb will roam to and fro|יְשֹׁטְט֥וּ\rb*, \rb and knowledge|הַדָּֽעַת׃\rb* \rb will increase|וְתִרְבֶּ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָנִיֵּ֔אל\rb*, \rb looked|וְרָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb others|אֲחֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb standing|עֹמְדִ֑ים\rb* \rb there|הֵ֙נָּה֙\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb on this bank|לִשְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the river|הַיְאֹ֔ר\rb* \rb and one|וְאֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb on the opposite|הֵ֖נָּה\rb* \rb bank|לִשְׂפַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַיְאֹֽר׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb One of them said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb to the man|לָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb dressed|לְב֣וּשׁ\rb* \rb in linen|הַבַּדִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was above|מִמַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb the waters|לְמֵימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the river|הַיְאֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb How long|מָתַ֖י\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the fulfillment|קֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb of these wonders|הַפְּלָאֽוֹת׃\rb*?”
\p \v 7 \rb And the man|הָאִ֣ישׁ׀\rb* \rb dressed|לְב֣וּשׁ\rb* \rb in linen|הַבַּדִּ֗ים\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was above|מִמַּעַל֮\rb* \rb the waters|לְמֵימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the river|הַיְאֹר֒\rb*, \rb raised|וַיָּ֨רֶם\rb* \rb his right hand|יְמִינ֤וֹ\rb* \rb and his left hand|וּשְׂמֹאלוֹ֙\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֞ע\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb swear|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֖ע\rb* \rb by Him who lives|בְּחֵ֣י\rb* \rb forever|הָעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb saying|כִּי֩\rb*, “\rb It will be for a time|לְמוֹעֵ֨ד\rb*, \rb and times|מֽוֹעֲדִ֜ים\rb*, \rb and half a time|וָחֵ֗צִי\rb*. \rb When the power|יַד־\rb* \rb of the holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb has finally been|וּכְכַלּ֛וֹת\rb* \rb shattered|נַפֵּ֥ץ\rb*, \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb will be completed|תִּכְלֶ֥ינָה\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb*, \rb but I did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb understand|אָבִ֑ין\rb*. \rb So I asked|וָאֹ֣מְרָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֕י\rb*, \rb what|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb will be the outcome|אַחֲרִ֖ית\rb* \rb of these things|אֵֽלֶּה׃פ\rb*?”
\p \v 9 “\rb Go on your way|לֵ֣ךְ\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּנִיֵּ֑אל\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb are closed up|סְתֻמִ֧ים\rb* \rb and sealed|וַחֲתֻמִ֛ים\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb of the end|קֵֽץ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb will be purified|יִ֠תְבָּֽרֲרוּ\rb*, \rb made spotless|וְיִֽתְלַבְּנ֤וּ\rb*, \rb and refined|וְיִצָּֽרְפוּ֙\rb*, \rb but the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֔ים\rb* \rb will continue to act wickedly|וְהִרְשִׁ֣יעוּ\rb*. \rb None|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֑ים\rb* \rb will understand|יָבִ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb but the wise|וְהַמַּשְׂכִּלִ֖ים\rb* \rb will understand|יָבִֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb And from the time|וּמֵעֵת֙\rb* \rb the daily sacrifice|הַתָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb is abolished|הוּסַ֣ר\rb* \rb and the abomination|שִׁקּ֣וּץ\rb* \rb of desolation|שֹׁמֵ֑ם\rb* \rb set up|וְלָתֵ֖ת\rb*, \rb there will be 1,290|אֶ֖לֶף\rb*\rb |מָאתַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |וְתִשְׁעִֽים׃\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֕ים\rb*. \v 12 \rb Blessed is|אַשְׁרֵ֥י\rb* \rb he who waits|הַֽמְחַכֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and reaches the end|וְיַגִּ֑יעַ\rb* \rb of the 1,335|אֶ֕לֶף\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb days|לְיָמִ֕ים\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb But as for you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb go on your way|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb until the end|לַקֵּ֑ץ\rb*. \rb You will rest|וְתָנ֛וּחַ\rb*, \rb and then you will arise|וְתַעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb to your inheritance|לְגֹרָלְךָ֖\rb* \rb at the end|לְקֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb of the days|הַיָּמִֽין׃\rb*.”
